{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T06:14:00.865Z","ordinal":494970,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18647-4a32-7a30-bab7-2a3c3cdf19a7","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-51d4729f-649a-4573-8f98-f4d1de0e93b9","process_id":"17379","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","nl -ba docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | sed -n '1,22p'; rg -n -C 2 'resize|terminal|0/15|xterm|operator report|cell' docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification 2>/dev/null | head -100; git show -s --format='%H%n%P%n%s' HEAD"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/release-readiness-20261029","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"nl -ba docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | sed -n '1,22p'; rg -n -C 2 'resize|terminal|0/15|xterm|operator report|cell' docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification 2>/dev/null | head -100; git show -s --format='%H%n%P%n%s' HEAD"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"     1\t# v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n     2\t\n     3\t## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 05:52 UTC)\n     4\t\n     5\t**Authoritative source:** `origin/main` is `6b786d54dd5bf60234c67fec6ef070c62af9b141`, including PR #311 and the merged readiness correction in PR #316. The main CodeQL run [40822684525](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40822684525) passed. Main CI [40822684551](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40822684551) remains in progress: Node 22 and 24 passed; Linux x86_64 is still running `npm test`. No complete current-main CI pass is claimed.\n     6\t\n     7\t**Requirements and version:** On PR #318's exact head `2c532d701c5b84b0d3308b02897520337addc36b` (which includes the current main), `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 remain deferred to exact-RC qualification: REQ-AGT-002, REQ-AGT-010, REQ-PRV-003, REQ-REL-003, REQ-REL-005, REQ-AGT-110, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-REL-114, REQ-QUAL-101, REQ-QUAL-107, REQ-QUAL-108 and REQ-QUAL-109. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes at `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage checks, not installed-RC acceptance.\n     8\t\n     9\t**Open source changes:** PR [#318](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/318) is based on `6b786d54dd5bf60234c67fec6ef070c62af9b141`, head `2c532d701c5b84b0d3308b02897520337addc36b`. Its four-file evaluator diff has independent `ACCEPT` review at SHA-256 `56ab8a3ecef2ada575aacd09e3e5148948fb6b013640c92b071d11598a629184`; requirements, version, and diff checks pass. CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript pass, but both Node 22 and Node 24 CI jobs failed: `eval_hardened.test.ts` could not find `go` while testing hidden-source isolation (exit 127). The failure is a CI toolchain-provisioning gap; it is not evidence that the corpus evaluator passed. Entire Gates also failed, and Linux packaging was skipped after the matrix failure. SageBridge has a separate workflow-only candidate at `d53caea7c480c5e88dff43c6e5d4cb8a16868400` to provision the toolchains; its independent review and push are pending. PR [#319](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/319), head `668721d8135d3a3332bca27b820caa5a4a76c7af` on the same base, has independent source-review `ACCEPT`; Node 22/24, CodeQL, and JavaScript/TypeScript pass, while Linux packaging/tests and Entire Gates remain pending. Neither PR is merged.\n    10\t\n    11\t**Held-out custody and qualification:** The historical T2 and T3 custody reports identify the OpenCode primary session as prior custodian/integrator, not task author. The current claim file assigns the custodian workflow to OpenCode, reports T2 successor preparation at 20/40 tasks (218 cases), a failed revalidation batch (`rc=1`), and no complete 40-task custody acceptance. T3's reported 8/8 covers digest/schema/isolation metadata, not task-quality qualification. Public issue comments contain conflicting handoff descriptions (SageBridge as accepted successor versus OpenCode still holding the active custody workflow); current custodian identity and acknowledged transfer require reconciliation. No private payloads were accessed by implementation work. T2/T3/T4 held-out qualification, standalone/provider acceptance, long-task/fault-injection qualification, and successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility remain incomplete.\n    12\t\n    13\t**Terminal and release gates:** Acceptance §5.3 requires actual operator execution for xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. Status remains **0/15**; automated PTY results do not count. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` is reachable and has the required terminal programs; RC10 is installed, but no matrix cell has been run and this host's GUI session is not exposed through the current noninteractive SSH session. Screenshots are waived by DEC-18 only; all interactive checks and per-cell verdicts remain mandatory under DEC-19. The latest public release is `v1.0.0-rc.10`; the selected distribution target is the GitHub installer, not npm. No stable `v1.0.0` release exists.\n    14\t\n    15\t**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Publication authorization remains granted but gated on complete mandatory acceptance. The evaluator CI provisioning correction is being prepared on a separately claimed workflow branch; PR #319's exact Linux gate is running. Exact-RC construction and qualification remain gated on pre-RC source readiness and complete independent custody acceptance; terminal operator evidence is still required before independent RC acceptance.\n    16\t\n    17\t## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 04:23 UTC; superseded)\n    18\t\n    19\t**Remote revision reconciliation:** `origin/main` is `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d`; `origin/v1/integration` is `7d6673f108316dda015b858c85b2abe20f3a4f78`. The integration ref is an ancestor of main (875 commits behind), not a divergent head. Current release PRs target main; evidence from the two refs must remain distinct.\n    20\t\n    21\t**Source gates on main:** `origin/main` is `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d` (PR #312 merge). Exact-main CI run [40802654248](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40802654248) and CodeQL run [40802654255](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40802654255) passed on that SHA. The exact-source requirements gate passed with 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open); 12 requirements remain mapped to exact-RC qualification. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage results, not installed-RC qualification.\n    22\t\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:1:# Manual real-terminal acceptance worksheet\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-2-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:3:For `REQ-QUAL-108` / `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`, following [`ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3](ACCEPTANCE.md#53-manual-real-terminal-matrix-e3).\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-4-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:5:> **Required for v1.0.0.** Complete all 15 cells against the exact installed RC. Blank cells are incomplete; no result is inferred. Automated PTY runs do not count as manual cell evidence. DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts only. The prior waiver record is withdrawn by [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver).\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-6-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-7-## Installed candidate identity\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-8-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:9:Fill these fields from the installed candidate before the first cell. Do not copy identity from a source branch or local build.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-10-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-11-- RC tag: ______________________________________________\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-17-- Operator and UTC date/time: ____________________________\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-18-- Host OS and version: __________________________________\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:19:- Per-cell evidence record directory or reference: ________\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-20-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:21:Record the actual terminal versions/protocol configuration used. Kitty must have the kitty keyboard protocol on; record the tmux 3.x version and its GNOME Terminal host version.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-22-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-23-| Environment | Version / protocol details |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-24-|---|---|\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:25:| xterm | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-26-| kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:27:| tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | tmux: ; GNOME Terminal: |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:28:| VS Code integrated terminal | VS Code: ; integrated terminal profile: |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:29:| GNOME Terminal | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-30-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:31:## Procedure to perform in every matrix cell\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-32-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:33:Run each step against the installed candidate in the terminal and size named by that row. Record the observations and evidence references for the cell.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-34-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-35-1. Launch `nexus`; confirm the TUI appears.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-36-2. At the approval panel, type continuously across it, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-37-3. Exercise multiline input with Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:38:4. Resize during streaming.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-39-5. Press Esc during `sleep 30`; confirm no child processes survive.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:40:6. Press Ctrl-C twice; confirm clean terminal restoration (echo on, no stray escape codes).\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-41-7. Exercise `NO_COLOR`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-42-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:43:Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). This does not waive any live manual interaction, check, observation, per-cell verdict, or evidence record. Automated PTY runs do not count as completion of these manual real-terminal cells.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-44-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:45:## Partial operator report\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-46-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:47:In response to the RC10 matrix request, the release owner reported that the client rendered at the tested sizes except in tmux inside GNOME Terminal; that setup could not be resized below 43×13, and the other results seemed okay. The report was received on 2026-10-29; test time, exact installed artifact identity, terminal versions, and per-cell check outcomes were not supplied. Treat this as useful partial operator information only: it does not fill any matrix cell or establish the installed-RC gate. No screenshot was supplied; DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-48-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:49:## Terminal × size results\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-50-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:51:Select exactly one PASS or FAIL for each cell. Record observed outcomes for every check and a per-cell evidence reference bound to the installed RC identity, terminal environment, and size. Record failures in the disposition/notes field.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-52-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:53:| # | Terminal environment | Size | Verdict (select one) | Per-cell evidence / result reference | Failure disposition / notes |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-54-|---:|---|---:|---|---|---|\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:55:| 1 | xterm | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:56:| 2 | xterm | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:57:| 3 | xterm | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-58-| 4 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-59-| 5 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-60-| 6 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:61:| 7 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:62:| 8 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:63:| 9 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:64:| 10 | VS Code integrated terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:65:| 11 | VS Code integrated terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:66:| 12 | VS Code integrated terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:67:| 13 | GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:68:| 14 | GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:69:| 15 | GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | |