failure may satisfy the\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:93:§5.3 disposition requirement, but the cell remains FAIL and ACC-TUI-MANUAL\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:94:remains unmet until every cell passes.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-95-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-96-Operator summary / evidence index: ______________________________________________\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-97-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:98:This worksheet records manual terminal evidence only. It does not replace the separate CI PTY, installed-RC, or independent acceptance gates in `ACCEPTANCE.md`.\n--\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md-14-- `npm run build` in `cli/`: passed on the candidate commit.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md-15-- `node --import=tsx --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern='ACC-SAFE-01' test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts` in `cli/`: 1 test passed. The test launches the actual `nexus` TUI and `nexus repl` in trusted and untrusted workspaces with explicit `review`, explicit `auto`, and unset mode. It verifies that unset mode prompts in both trust states, auto mode executes, review mode denies without approval, and project instructions load only after trust.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md:16:- `node --import=tsx --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern='ACC-SAFE-09/10' test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts` in `cli/`: 1 test passed. It verifies `/test` approval disclosure, trust-independent review and auto behavior, actual bwrap workspace mounting, and Escape cancellation. Before cancellation the driver confirms the unique `sleep 30` descendant is visible in the host `/proc` by exact argv and process name; after Escape the test requires the process to disappear within three seconds. The fixture terminates any remaining canary before cleanup if an assertion fails.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md-17-- `python3 -m py_compile cli/test/helpers/startup_permission_driver.py`: passed.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md-18-- `git diff --check`: passed.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md-19-\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md:20:The source tests cover the applicable source acceptance criteria. They do not claim installed-RC qualification, held-out qualification, cross-runner qualification, or human terminal acceptance. Those release gates remain pending.\n524a2dcd4421994e72b98609054b44efaefa1b93\n6b786d54dd5bf60234c67fec6ef070c62af9b141\ndocs(release): refresh current convergence checkpoint\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":807603947}},"started_at_ms":1793254440057,"completed_at_ms":1793254440865}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T06:14:02.374Z","ordinal":494971,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1864b-4585-7d43-98ef-d74268bbc69e","call_id":"call_bbee1bb8b4e34094bfc6cde475c27e85","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 4392)\nTotal output lines: 125\n\n     1\t# v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n     2\t\n     3\t## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 05:52 UTC)\n     4\t\n     5\t**Authoritative source:** `origin/main` is `6b786d54dd5bf60234c67fec6ef070c62af9b141`, including PR #311 and the merged readiness correction in PR #316. The main CodeQL run [40822684525](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40822684525) passed. Main CI [40822684551](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40822684551) remains in progress: Node 22 and 24 passed; Linux x86_64 is still running `npm test`. No complete current-main CI pass is claimed.\n     6\t\n     7\t**Requirements and version:** On PR #318's exact head `2c532d701c5b84b0d3308b02897520337addc36b` (which includes the current main), `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 remain deferred to exact-RC qualification: REQ-AGT-002, REQ-AGT-010, REQ-PRV-003, REQ-REL-003, REQ-REL-005, REQ-AGT-110, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-REL-114, REQ-QUAL-101, REQ-QUAL-107, REQ-QUAL-108 and REQ-QUAL-109. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes at `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage checks, not installed-RC acceptance.\n     8\t\n     9\t**Open source changes:** PR [#318](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/318) is based on `6b786d54dd5bf60234c67fec6ef070c62af9b141`, head `2c532d701c5b84b0d3308b02897520337addc36b`. Its four-file evaluator diff has independent `ACCEPT` review at SHA-256 `56ab8a3ecef2ada575aacd09e3e5148948fb6b013640c92b071d11598a629184`; requirements, version, and diff checks pass. CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript pass, but both Node 22 and Node 24 CI jobs failed: `eval_hardened.test.ts` could not find `go` while testing hidden-source isolation (exit 127). The failure is a CI toolchain-provisioning gap; it is not evidence that the corpus evaluator passed. Entire Gates also failed, and Linux packaging was skipped after the matrix failure. SageBridge has a separate workflow-only candidate at `d53caea7c480c5e88dff43c6e5d4cb8a16868400` to provision the toolchains; its independent review and push are pending. PR [#319](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/319), head `668721d8135d3a3332bca27b820caa5a4a76c7af` on the same base, has independent source-review `ACCEPT`; Node 22/24, CodeQL, and JavaScript/TypeScript pass, while Linux packaging/tests and Entire Gates remain pending. Neither PR is merged.\n    10\t\n    11\t**Held-out custody and qualification:** The historical T2 and T3 custody reports identify the OpenCode primary session as prior custodian/integrator, not task author. The current claim file assigns the custodian workflow to OpenCode, reports T2 successor preparation at 20/40 tasks (218 cases), a failed revalidation batch (`rc=1`), and no complete 40-task custody acceptance. T3's reported 8/8 covers digest/schema/isolation metadata, not task-quality qualification. Public issue comments contain conflicting handoff descriptions (SageBridge as accepted successor versus OpenCode still holding the active custody workflow); current custodian identity and acknowledged transfer require reconciliation. No private payloads were accessed by implementation work. T2/T3/T4 held-out qualification, standalone/provider acceptance, long-task/fault-injection qualification, and successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility remain incomplete.\n    12\t\n    13\t**Terminal and release gates:** Acceptance §5.3 requires actual operator execution for xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. Status remains **0/15**; automated PTY results do not count. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` is reachable and has the required terminal programs; RC10 is installed, but no matrix cell has been run and this host's GUI session is not exposed through the current noninteractive SSH session. Screenshots are waived by DEC-18 only; all interactive checks and per-cell verdicts remain mandatory under DEC-19. The latest public release is `v1.0.0-rc.10`; the selected distribution target is the GitHub installer, not npm. No stable `v1.0.0` release exists.\n    14\t\n    15\t**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Publication authorization remains granted but gated on complete mandatory acceptance. The evaluator CI provisioning correction is being prepared on a separately claimed workflow branch; PR #319's exact Linux gate is running. Exact-RC construction and qualification remain gated on pre-RC source readiness and complete independent custody acceptance; terminal operator evidence is still required before independent RC acceptance.\n    16\t\n    17\t## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 04:23 UTC; superseded)\n    18…1992 tokens truncated…L | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:69:| 15 | GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-70-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-71-## Acceptance gate\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-72-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:73:- Safety checks 2, 5, and 6: **zero failures across all 15 cells**. Any failure here blocks this gate.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-74-- Any failure on another check requires a written disposition: fix, or a documented known limitation.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:75:- All 15 cells have exactly one verdict, check outcomes, and per-cell evidence references: [ ] yes  [ ] no\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-76-- All non-safety failures have a written disposition: [ ] yes  [ ] no  [ ] no such failures\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-77-- Safety gate has zero failures: [ ] yes  [ ] no\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-79-§5.3 matrix gate: [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL  [ ] INCOMPLETE\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-80-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:81:Mark the §5.3 matrix gate PASS when all 15 verdicts, check outcomes, and per-cell evidence\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-82-references are complete, checks 2, 5, and 6 have zero failures, and every\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-83-failure on another check has a written disposition. Mark it FAIL if any safety\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-87-ACC-TUI-MANUAL: [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL  [ ] INCOMPLETE\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-88-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:89:Mark ACC-TUI-MANUAL PASS only when all 15 cell verdicts are PASS and the\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:90:per-cell outcomes and evidence records are complete. Screenshots are waived per DEC-18. Mark it FAIL if any\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:91:cell is FAIL. Mark it INCOMPLETE when evidence is missing and no cell has\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-92-failed. A documented known limitation for a non-safety failure may satisfy the\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:93:§5.3 disposition requirement, but the cell remains FAIL and ACC-TUI-MANUAL\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:94:remains unmet until every cell passes.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-95-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-96-Operator summary / evidence index: ______________________________________________\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md-97-\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:98:This worksheet records manual terminal evidence only. It does not replace the separate CI PTY, installed-RC, or independent acceptance gates in `ACCEPTANCE.md`.\n--\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md-14-- `npm run build` in `cli/`: passed on the candidate commit.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md-15-- `node --import=tsx --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern='ACC-SAFE-01' test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts` in `cli/`: 1 test passed. The test launches the actual `nexus` TUI and `nexus repl` in trusted and untrusted workspaces with explicit `review`, explicit `auto`, and unset mode. It verifies that unset mode prompts in both trust states, auto mode executes, review mode denies without approval, and project instructions load only after trust.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md:16:- `node --import=tsx --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern='ACC-SAFE-09/10' test/repl_approval_e2e.test.ts` in `cli/`: 1 test passed. It verifies `/test` approval disclosure, trust-independent review and auto behavior, actual bwrap workspace mounting, and Escape cancellation. Before cancellation the driver confirms the unique `sleep 30` descendant is visible in the host `/proc` by exact argv and process name; after Escape the test requires the process to disappear within three seconds. The fixture terminates any remaining canary before cleanup if an assertion fails.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md-17-- `python3 -m py_compile cli/test/helpers/startup_permission_driver.py`: passed.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md-18-- `git diff --check`: passed.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md-19-\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md:20:The source tests cover the applicable source acceptance criteria. They do not claim installed-RC qualification, held-out qualification, cross-runner qualification, or human terminal acceptance. Those release gates remain pending.\n524a2dcd4421994e72b9860