sults seemed okay. The report was received on 2026-10-29; test time, exact installed artifact identity, terminal versions, and per-cell check outcomes were not supplied. Treat this as useful partial operator information only: it does not fill any matrix cell or establish the installed-RC gate. No screenshot was supplied; DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:55:| 1 | xterm | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:56:| 2 | xterm | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:57:| 3 | xterm | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:58:| 4 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:59:| 5 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:60:| 6 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:61:| 7 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:62:| 8 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:63:| 9 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:64:| 10 | VS Code integrated terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:65:| 11 | VS Code integrated terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:66:| 12 | VS Code integrated terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:67:| 13 | GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:68:| 14 | GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:69:| 15 | GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md:31:- `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`: passed (123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 exact-RC deferrals).\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-WORKTREE-RECORD-MIGRATION-20261027/README.md:7:| Affected behavior | Earlier builds recorded the active speculative worktree as the task's `workspacePath` (`checkpointDurableState` used the current workspace identity after switching). Recovery from the repository root passes `expectedWorkspace = <root>`, so `loadTaskStateLocked` threw `WorkspaceIdentityMismatchError` before the worktree binding could be used. `listTasks({ workspace: root })` also missed the record, and resuming from inside `.nexus/worktrees/<taskId>` is not a supported entry point. The result was a task created by a pre-fix build that could not be resumed from the root at all. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json:46:  \"qualification_status\": \"partial; OpenRouter verification and its required live task remain outstanding. This record does not establish overall RC acceptance.\"\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-MCP-CONFIG-PERSIST-20261024/README.md:54:- Refusing an unparseable config, or a present-but-unusable `mcpServers` value, requires the operator to repair the\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/README.md:15:marker. The validator tested the operator-home and synthetic-store access\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/README.md:38:process-tree cleanup, denied access to operator and synthetic-store files, and\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/README.md:54:cleanup, denied access to operator and synthetic-store files, fail-closed\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/README.md:89:cleanup, denied access to operator and synthetic-store files, fail-closed\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-READONLY-MODE-ESCALATION-20261024/README.md:8:| Severity | Medium: a read-only session is meant to be a safe inspection posture for untrusted workspaces; this lets the operator (or a misleading UI) unlock writes, MCP server startup, theme/knowledge/skill scaffolding without leaving the session. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-EDIT-FILE-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md:45:  partial edits for larger files. A future slicing feature would need a different design.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-20261020T0338Z-synthetic.md:14:The store argument was a temporary synthetic directory containing a canary file. The evaluator could not access that directory or the isolated operator home. No held-out store, task, answer, validator, or private corpus material was accessed. This run verifies the current host controls and denial of the synthetic path; it does not establish custodian-store permissions, corpus custody acceptance, or qualification readiness.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/validate-6383623-20261023T193626Z.json:31:      \"name\": \"workspace root is the dedicated, operator-owned, size-capped tmpfs\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/validate-6383623-20261023T193626Z.json:45:      \"name\": \"the evaluator cannot reach operator files or the held-out store\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/validate-6383623-20261023T193626Z.json:70:        \"file\": \"eval/host/operator_home.mjs\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_PR-12a/validation.md:62:   *Result:* 122 rows; tested 108, partial 5, implemented 2, open 7 (0 problems). `REQ-REL-115` verified as `tested` with valid spec, plan, and test references.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_PR-12a/validation.md:72:- **No Root Privileges:** Installs and upgrades cleanly within operator prefix (default `~/.local`).\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_PR-12a/validation.md:77:- **Process Continuity:** Active TUI process remains running on its loaded version; no running components killed; restart requirement clearly communicated to operator.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_VERSION_PROBE_STORAGE/corrected-local-precondition.tap:12:  operator: '=='\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-NAT64-SSRF-20261024/README.md:42:- NAT64 prefixes other than the well-known `/96` and local-use `/48` (operator-specific `/64`, `/56`,\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-SSRF-IPV6-CONNECT-20261023/README.md:60:operator configuration. Teredo (`2001::/32`) is likewise not decoded. Both predate this change and are\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-20261021T0443Z-synthetic.md:16:The store argument was a temporary root-owned synthetic directory containing one canary. The validator checked that the evaluator could not access its path; no held-out corpus, task, answer, validator, or private custody data was accessed. The synthetic store and temporary probe home were removed after the run.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:29:    [provider_capabilities] reason=step model=m context 18000 (operator); output allowance 500 (operator); discovery unsupported (catalog lists no limits); token counting unsupported\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:31:    [token_count] step=1 request_id=6ea58816-c1e5-4786-bccd-78fc356ec96d source=client_estimate prompt_tokens=4787 client_estimate=4787 context_limit=18000 (operator) output_allowance=500 (operator) tool_headroom_policy=500 unmeasured=\"the connection advertises no request counting\"\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:33:    [token_count] step=2 request_id=d3fe1b49-ec1c-40b4-b547-605fd04a826c source=client_estimate prompt_tokens=4855 client_estimate=4855 context_limit=18000 (operator) output_allowance=500 (operator) tool_headroom_policy=500 unmeasured=\"the connection advertises no request counting\"\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:35:    [token_c