ix (REQ-AGT-104, REQ-AGT-105, ACC-CONT-05; partial AGT-05 per REQ-AGT-111 POST-V1) | `cli/src/agent.ts`, `cli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts` |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/INDEP-REVIEW-CONTINUITY/review-prep.md:85:2. **VQ-2** Were *all* former `depth === 0` durability gates converted, and are the remaining depth checks genuinely about the interactive operator (steering/UI), not durability?\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/INDEP-REVIEW-CONTINUITY/review-prep.md:88:5. **VQ-5** What happens in the *same process* after a partial commit failure — is the turn actually stopped (PERSISTENCE_FAILED) and is the in-memory state never reported as durable?\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/INDEP-REVIEW-CONTINUITY/review-prep.md:157:2. Walk VQ-1/VQ-2 fully: enumerate every former `depth === 0` site listed in PLAN-04 task 2 and classify each remaining `depth` check at `e1759ca` (grep `this.depth` in agent.ts: 1484, 1639-1640, 2434, 3623, 3863 — verify each is genuinely operator-interactive, not durability).\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/validate-8f4504e.json:31:      \"name\": \"workspace root is the dedicated, operator-owned, size-capped tmpfs\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/validate-8f4504e.json:45:      \"name\": \"the evaluator cannot reach operator files or the held-out store\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/validate-8f4504e.json:70:        \"file\": \"eval/host/operator_home.mjs\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-20261020T1457Z-synthetic.json:31:      \"name\": \"workspace root is the dedicated, operator-owned, size-capped tmpfs\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-20261020T1457Z-synthetic.json:45:      \"name\": \"the evaluator cannot reach operator files or the held-out store\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-20261020T1457Z-synthetic.json:70:        \"file\": \"eval/host/operator_home.mjs\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-DOCTOR-UNREADABLE-STATE-20261024/README.md:8:| Severity | Medium-low: a truthfulness defect in the diagnostic operator's tool. It can hide a permissions/type problem and discourage investigation of unreadable sessions or task state. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-UI-TERMINAL-INJECTION-20261025/README.md:7:| Affected behavior | The legacy CLI `TerminalUI` redacted secrets but printed tool output, errors, plan names/details, diffs, code, thoughts (debug), inference messages and model summaries without removing terminal controls. A malicious file read by the agent, a command error, or model text containing ESC/OSC/C1 sequences wrote them to the operator’s terminal (screen/title/clipboard style attacks). The TUI sidecar already sanitizes these with `stripEscapes`/`visibleControls`; the CLI path did not. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/INDEP-REVIEW-CONTINUITY/dispositions.md:22:- **Evidence:** prior work-unit test used manual `compactNow(false)` + in-process recovery; SIGKILL tests were depth-0 and operator-invoked.\n     1\t# Manual real-terminal acceptance worksheet\n     2\t\n     3\tFor `REQ-QUAL-108` / `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`, following [`ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3](ACCEPTANCE.md#53-manual-real-terminal-matrix-e3).\n     4\t\n     5\t> **Required for v1.0.0.** Complete all 15 cells against the exact installed RC. Blank cells are incomplete; no result is inferred. Automated PTY runs do not count as manual cell evidence. DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts only. The prior waiver record is withdrawn by [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver).\n     6\t\n     7\t## Installed candidate identity\n     8\t\n     9\tFill these fields from the installed candidate before the first cell. Do not copy identity from a source branch or local build.\n    10\t\n    11\t- RC tag: ______________________________________________\n    12\t- Full RC source commit: ________________________________\n    13\t- Installed package/archive name and location: ____________\n    14\t- Installed artifact SHA256: ____________________________\n    15\t- Installation procedure/run reference: __________________\n    16\t- `nexus --version` output reference: ____________________\n    17\t- Operator and UTC date/time: ____________________________\n    18\t- Host OS and version: __________________________________\n    19\t- Per-cell evidence record directory or reference: ________\n    20\t\n    21\tRecord the actual terminal versions/protocol configuration used. Kitty must have the kitty keyboard protocol on; record the tmux 3.x version and its GNOME Terminal host version.\n    22\t\n    23\t| Environment | Version / protocol details |\n    24\t|---|---|\n    25\t| xterm | |\n    26\t| kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | |\n    27\t| tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | tmux: ; GNOME Terminal: |\n    28\t| VS Code integrated terminal | VS Code: ; integrated terminal profile: |\n    29\t| GNOME Terminal | |\n    30\t\n    31\t## Procedure to perform in every matrix cell\n    32\t\n    33\tRun each step against the installed candidate in the terminal and size named by that row. Record the observations and evidence references for the cell.\n    34\t\n    35\t1. Launch `nexus`; confirm the TUI appears.\n    36\t2. At the approval panel, type continuously across it, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key.\n    37\t3. Exercise multiline input with Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter.\n    38\t4. Resize during streaming.\n    39\t5. Press Esc during `sleep 30`; confirm no child processes survive.\n    40\t6. Press Ctrl-C twice; confirm clean terminal restoration (echo on, no stray escape codes).\n    41\t7. Exercise `NO_COLOR`.\n    42\t\n    43\tScreenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). This does not waive any live manual interaction, check, observation, per-cell verdict, or evidence record. Automated PTY runs do not count as completion of these manual real-terminal cells.\n    44\t\n    45\t## Partial operator report\n    46\t\n    47\tIn response to the RC10 matrix request, the release owner reported that the client rendered at the tested sizes except in tmux inside GNOME Terminal; that setup could not be resized below 43×13, and the other results seemed okay. The report was received on 2026-10-29; test time, exact installed artifact identity, terminal versions, and per-cell check outcomes were not supplied. Treat this as useful partial operator information only: it does not fill any matrix cell or establish the installed-RC gate. No screenshot was supplied; DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts.\n    48\t\n    49\t## Terminal × size results\n    50\t\n    51\tSelect exactly one PASS or FAIL for each cell. Record observed outcomes for every check and a per-cell evidence reference bound to the installed RC identity, terminal environment, and size. Record failures in the disposition/notes field.\n    52\t\n    53\t| # | Terminal environment | Size | Verdict (select one) | Per-cell evidence / result reference | Failure disposition / notes |\n    54\t|---:|---|---:|---|---|---|\n    55\t| 1 | xterm | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n    56\t| 2 | xterm | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n    57\t| 3 | xterm | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n    58\t| 4 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n    59\t| 5 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n    60\t| 6 | kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n    61\t| 7 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n    62\t| 8 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n    63\t| 9 | tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n    64\t| 10 | VS Code integrated terminal | 80×24 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n    65\t| 11 | VS Code integrated terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n    66\t| 12 | VS Code integrated terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n    67