idence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json:46:  \"qualification_status\": \"partial; OpenRouter verification and its required live task remain outstanding. This record does not establish overall RC acceptance.\"\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-MCP-CONFIG-PERSIST-20261024/README.md:54:- Refusing an unparseable config, or a present-but-unusable `mcpServers` value, requires the operator to repair the\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/README.md:15:marker. The validator tested the operator-home and synthetic-store access\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/README.md:38:process-tree cleanup, denied access to operator and synthetic-store files, and\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/README.md:54:cleanup, denied access to operator and synthetic-store files, fail-closed\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/README.md:89:cleanup, denied access to operator and synthetic-store files, fail-closed\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-READONLY-MODE-ESCALATION-20261024/README.md:8:| Severity | Medium: a read-only session is meant to be a safe inspection posture for untrusted workspaces; this lets the operator (or a misleading UI) unlock writes, MCP server startup, theme/knowledge/skill scaffolding without leaving the session. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-EDIT-FILE-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md:45:  partial edits for larger files. A future slicing feature would need a different design.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-20261020T0338Z-synthetic.md:14:The store argument was a temporary synthetic directory containing a canary file. The evaluator could not access that directory or the isolated operator home. No held-out store, task, answer, validator, or private corpus material was accessed. This run verifies the current host controls and denial of the synthetic path; it does not establish custodian-store permissions, corpus custody acceptance, or qualification readiness.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/validate-6383623-20261023T193626Z.json:31:      \"name\": \"workspace root is the dedicated, operator-owned, size-capped tmpfs\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/validate-6383623-20261023T193626Z.json:45:      \"name\": \"the evaluator cannot reach operator files or the held-out store\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/validate-6383623-20261023T193626Z.json:70:        \"file\": \"eval/host/operator_home.mjs\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_PR-12a/validation.md:62:   *Result:* 122 rows; tested 108, partial 5, implemented 2, open 7 (0 problems). `REQ-REL-115` verified as `tested` with valid spec, plan, and test references.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_PR-12a/validation.md:72:- **No Root Privileges:** Installs an…3435 tokens truncated…led candidate before the first cell. Do not copy identity from a source branch or local build.\n    10\t\n    11\t- RC tag: ______________________________________________\n    12\t- Full RC source commit: ________________________________\n    13\t- Installed package/archive name and location: ____________\n    14\t- Installed artifact SHA256: ____________________________\n    15\t- Installation procedure/run reference: __________________\n    16\t- `nexus --version` output reference: ____________________\n    17\t- Operator and UTC date/time: ____________________________\n    18\t- Host OS and version: __________________________________\n    19\t- Per-cell evidence record directory or reference: ________\n    20\t\n    21\tRecord the actual terminal versions/protocol configuration used. Kitty must have the kitty keyboard protocol on; record the tmux 3.x version and its GNOME Terminal host version.\n    22\t\n    23\t| Environment | Version / protocol details |\n    24\t|---|---|\n    25\t| xterm | |\n    26\t| kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on) | |\n    27\t| tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal | tmux: ;