{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T06:15:42.379Z","ordinal":495038,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18647-4a32-7a30-bab7-2a3c3cdf19a7","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-758a2b24-b2d2-47d6-9396-cbe404f3ee78","process_id":"88407","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git diff --check; git status --short --branch; git diff --stat; git diff -- docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md; git fetch origin codex/release-readiness-20261029 --quiet; git rev-parse HEAD origin/codex/release-readiness-20261029; git log --oneline --decorate -3 HEAD"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/release-readiness-20261029","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git diff --check; git status --short --branch; git diff --stat; git diff -- docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md; git fetch origin codex/release-readiness-20261029 --quiet; git rev-parse HEAD origin/codex/release-readiness-20261029; git log --oneline --decorate -3 HEAD"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## codex/release-readiness-20261029...origin/codex/release-readiness-20261029\n M docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | 14 +++++++-------\n 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\nindex 37a6eedf..75f8310a 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n@@ -1,18 +1,18 @@\n # v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n \n-## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 05:52 UTC)\n+## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 06:14 UTC)\n \n-**Authoritative source:** `origin/main` is `6b786d54dd5bf60234c67fec6ef070c62af9b141`, including PR #311 and the merged readiness correction in PR #316. The main CodeQL run [40822684525](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40822684525) passed. Main CI [40822684551](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40822684551) remains in progress: Node 22 and 24 passed; Linux x86_64 is still running `npm test`. No complete current-main CI pass is claimed.\n+**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` is `6b786d54dd5bf60234c67fec6ef070c62af9b141`, including PR #311 and the merged readiness correction in PR #316. `origin/v1/integration` remains at `7d6673f108316dda015b858c85b2abe20f3a4f78`, an ancestor of main. Main CodeQL run [40822684525](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40822684525) passed. Exact-main CI run [40822684551](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40822684551) completed successfully at 05:58:56 UTC: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86_64 all passed.\n \n-**Requirements and version:** On PR #318's exact head `2c532d701c5b84b0d3308b02897520337addc36b` (which includes the current main), `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 remain deferred to exact-RC qualification: REQ-AGT-002, REQ-AGT-010, REQ-PRV-003, REQ-REL-003, REQ-REL-005, REQ-AGT-110, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-REL-114, REQ-QUAL-101, REQ-QUAL-107, REQ-QUAL-108 and REQ-QUAL-109. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes at `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage checks, not installed-RC acceptance.\n+**Requirements and version:** On exact `origin/main` `6b786d54dd5bf60234c67fec6ef070c62af9b141`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 remain deferred to exact-RC qualification: REQ-AGT-002, REQ-AGT-010, REQ-PRV-003, REQ-REL-003, REQ-REL-005, REQ-AGT-110, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-REL-114, REQ-QUAL-101, REQ-QUAL-107, REQ-QUAL-108 and REQ-QUAL-109. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes at `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage checks, not installed-RC acceptance.\n \n-**Open source changes:** PR [#318](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/318) is based on `6b786d54dd5bf60234c67fec6ef070c62af9b141`, head `2c532d701c5b84b0d3308b02897520337addc36b`. Its four-file evaluator diff has independent `ACCEPT` review at SHA-256 `56ab8a3ecef2ada575aacd09e3e5148948fb6b013640c92b071d11598a629184`; requirements, version, and diff checks pass. CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript pass, but both Node 22 and Node 24 CI jobs failed: `eval_hardened.test.ts` could not find `go` while testing hidden-source isolation (exit 127). The failure is a CI toolchain-provisioning gap; it is not evidence that the corpus evaluator passed. Entire Gates also failed, and Linux packaging was skipped after the matrix failure. SageBridge has a separate workflow-only candidate at `d53caea7c480c5e88dff43c6e5d4cb8a16868400` to provision the toolchains; its independent review and push are pending. PR [#319](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/319), head `668721d8135d3a3332bca27b820caa5a4a76c7af` on the same base, has independent source-review `ACCEPT`; Node 22/24, CodeQL, and JavaScript/TypeScript pass, while Linux packaging/tests and Entire Gates remain pending. Neither PR is merged.\n+**Open source changes:** PR [#318](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/318), head `2c532d701c5b84b0d3308b02897520337addc36b`, has independent `ACCEPT` source review, but both Node 22 and Node 24 CI jobs failed because `eval_hardened.test.ts` could not find `go` while testing hidden-source isolation (exit 127); Linux was skipped. This is a CI toolchain-provisioning gap, not evaluator qualification evidence. PR [#322](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/322), head `d53caea7c480c5e88dff43c6e5d4cb8a16868400`, adds CI-only pinned Go/Rust toolchain provisioning and has independent `ACCEPT` review; setup succeeded, but its Node 22/24 CLI suites are still running. PR [#319](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/319), head `668721d8135d3a3332bca27b820caa5a4a76c7af`, and PR [#320](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/320), head `2124538d21b84454319c5485140b266f11510a5a`, both have independent `ACCEPT` reviews and passing Node 22/24, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks; Linux and Entire Gates remain in progress. PR [#321](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/321), head `524a2dcd4421994e72b98609054b44efaefa1b93`, refreshes this checkpoint; its Node 24, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks pass, Node 22 and Entire Gates are still running, and its first independent documentation review requested two corrections that are being applied here. None of these PRs is merged.\n \n-**Held-out custody and qualification:** The historical T2 and T3 custody reports identify the OpenCode primary session as prior custodian/integrator, not task author. The current claim file assigns the custodian workflow to OpenCode, reports T2 successor preparation at 20/40 tasks (218 cases), a failed revalidation batch (`rc=1`), and no complete 40-task custody acceptance. T3's reported 8/8 covers digest/schema/isolation metadata, not task-quality qualification. Public issue comments contain conflicting handoff descriptions (SageBridge as accepted successor versus OpenCode still holding the active custody workflow); current custodian identity and acknowledged transfer require reconciliation. No private payloads were accessed by implementation work. T2/T3/T4 held-out qualification, standalone/provider acceptance, long-task/fault-injection qualification, and successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility remain incomplete.\n+**Held-out custody and qualification:** The latest public metadata update on issue #1 (06:02 UTC) records unresolved custody ownership: a historical handoff log names SageBridge as an accepted successor, while the active custody record still names OpenCode. The latest posted T2 count is 20/40 tasks; no new custody acceptance or qualification result is recorded. T3's reported 8/8 covers digest/schema/isolation metadata, not task-quality qualification. The custodian identity and acknowledged transfer must be reconciled before qualification. No private payloads were accessed by implementation work. T2/T3/T4 held-out qualification, standalone/provider acceptance, long-task/fault-injection qualification, and successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility remain incomplete.\n \n-**Terminal and release gates:** Acceptance §5.3 requires actual operator execution for xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. Status remains **0/15**; automated PTY results do not count. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` is reachable and has the required terminal programs; RC10 is installed, but no matrix cell has been run and this host's GUI session is not exposed through the current noninteractive SSH session. Screenshots are waived by DEC-18 only; all interactive checks and per-cell verdicts remain mandatory under DEC-19. The latest public release is `v1.0.0-rc.10`; the selected distribution target is the GitHub installer, not npm. No stable `v1.0.0` release exists.\n+**Terminal and release gates:** Acceptance §5.3 requires actual operator execution for xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. There are **0/15 accepted cells**. The operator's partial RC10 report says the client rendered at tested sizes except tmux inside GNOME Terminal, which could not be resized below 43×13; other results “seemed okay.” The report lacks test time, exact installed artifact identity, terminal versions, and per-cell check outcomes, so it does not complete any cell. Automated PTY results do not count. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` has the required terminal programs; the successor RC is not yet available for the matrix. Screenshots are waived by DEC-18 only; all interactive checks and per-cell verdicts remain mandatory under DEC-19. The latest public release is `v1.0.0-rc.10`; the selected distribution target is the GitHub installer, not npm. No stable `v1.0.0` release exists.\n \n-**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Publication authorization remains granted but gated on complete mandatory acceptance. The evaluator CI provisioning correction is being prepared on a separately claimed workflow branch; PR #319's exact Linux gate is running. Exact-RC construction and qualification remain gated on pre-RC source readiness and complete independent custody acceptance; terminal operator evidence is still required before independent RC acceptance.\n+**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Publication authorization remains granted but gated on complete mandatory acceptance. PRs #319 and #320 are in exact-head Linux validation, PRs #321 and #322 have matrix checks running, and PR #318 awaits the corrected CI toolchain setup and exact-base revalidation. Exact-RC construction and qualification remain gated on pre-RC source readiness and complete independent custody acceptance; terminal operator evidence is still required before independent RC acceptance.\n \n ## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 04:23 UTC; superseded)\n \n524a2dcd4421994e72b98609054b44efaefa1b93\n524a2dcd4421994e72b98609054b44efaefa1b93\n524a2dcd (HEAD -> codex/release-readiness-20261029, origin/codex/release-readiness-20261029) docs(release): refresh current convergence checkpoint\n6b786d54 (origin/main) Merge pull request #311 from mikeholownych/v1/qualify-all-accepted-v9\nfc2ec326 Merge pull request #316 from mikeholownych/codex/restore-terminal-human-matrix\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":214392736}},"started_at_ms":1793254541164,"completed_at_ms":1793254542379}}
