{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T06:21:18.071Z","ordinal":495311,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18651-eb77-7c23-9bbb-04a3dd73b15e","author":"/root/review_pr300_readiness","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_pr300_readiness\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — Reviewed PR #321 at exact head `84e6bb7ce9e2ba3cc287db5a40119937870c51d4` against base `a0356c4d8f0f0b9b943d4033aff59795fcab83b4`. The diff changes only `docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md`.\n\nBoth prior findings are fixed: the checkpoint reports main CI as successful on `6b786d54` and post-merge CI/CodeQL in progress on `a0356c4d`; the terminal section says **0/15 accepted cells** and clearly records the partial RC10 report without counting it as a completed cell.\n\nI verified `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` on an isolated worktree at exact main `a0356c4d`; both passed, with 12 requirements deferred and version `1.0.0-rc.10`. GitHub confirms PR #319 merged as `a0356c4d`, with required checks passed. PR #318 remains failed on its Node jobs; #320 and #322 remain open with Linux and Entire checks in progress; PR #321’s fresh exact-head checks are still in progress.\n\nCustody remains incomplete: public metadata and the active claim report 20/40 T2 tasks and no custody acceptance. The manual matrix remains 0/15 accepted; the partial operator report lacks exact artifact identity and per-cell outcomes. The checkpoint preserves `IN_PROGRESS` acceptance and does not claim an accepted RC or stable release.\n\nDiff SHA-256: `e74295e69320f041c1a19842c255940fd7de62c33c87a0bdee448bb63158161a`\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18651-eaeb-77d3-9068-c0816219322f","create_time":1793254878.0716994,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":23194}}
