{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T06:21:41.036Z","ordinal":495332,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a18652-452b-7081-a1c9-5cafed50da36","call_id":"call_5a91ade894944376940ff8fee9ee4432","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr311_draft_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — reviewed commit `d53caea7c480c5e88dff43c6e5d4cb8a16868400`; exact patch SHA-256: `b42067a589cd9bda7802cf1550a2a7741d99cb3e34b44827eee58b1d66d4c85f`.\\n\\nBoth `test-matrix` and `linux-x86_64` copy the active Go root and Rust sysroot to the fixed locations, set root ownership and remove group/other write permission, then compare the copied Go, Rust, and Cargo versions with their source tools. The filesystem changes are confined to the ephemeral CI runner; I found no source-path overlap or cross-job persistence issue in the workflow.\\n\\nRead-only source review; no tests run.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr300_readiness\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — Reviewed PR #321 at exact head `84e6bb7ce9e2ba3cc287db5a40119937870c51d4` against base `a0356c4d8f0f0b9b943d4033aff59795fcab83b4`. The diff changes only `docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md`.\\n\\nBoth prior findings are fixed: the checkpoint reports main CI as successful on `6b786d54` and post-merge CI/CodeQL in progress on `a0356c4d`; the terminal section says **0/15 accepted cells** and clearly records the partial RC10 report without counting it as a completed cell.\\n\\nI verified `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` on an isolated worktree at exact main `a0356c4d`; both passed, with 12 requirements deferred and version `1.0.0-rc.10`. GitHub confirms PR #319 merged as `a0356c4d`, with required checks passed. PR #318 remains failed on its Node jobs; #320 and #322 remain open with Linux and Entire checks in progress; PR #321’s fresh exact-head checks are still in progress.\\n\\nCustody remains incomplete: public metadata and the active claim report 20/40 T2 tasks and no custody acceptance. The manual matrix remains 0/15 accepted; the partial operator report lacks exact artifact identity and per-cell outcomes. The checkpoint preserves `IN_PROGRESS` acceptance and does not claim an accepted RC or stable release.\\n\\nDiff SHA-256: `e74295e69320f041c1a19842c255940fd7de62c33c87a0bdee448bb63158161a`\\n\\n\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr302\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Trail 30 is the matching open change for PR #315’s exact branch and head. Its approval list is empty.\\n\\nI did **not** approve: `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file entire auth status` identifies the active account as **Mike Holownych**, the PR author and trail author/assignee. Only that one Entire context is configured, so I have no independent non-owner authenticated identity to submit the approval. The approval remains outstanding.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18651-eaeb-77d3-9068-c0816219322f","create_time":1793254901.0359247}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
