4:12 metadata request: SageBridge's 04:15 status says it is coordinating only. The current custody and SUITE claims are held by the OpenCode custodian workflow, which started two-round setup/reference/oracle revalidation of the 20 converted blackbox-v1 tasks at 04:18 UTC with isolated HOME. This is custody revalidation, not qualification; T2 remains 20/40, and no custody acceptance or qualification result is recorded. T3's reported 8/8 result covers digest/schema/isolation metadata, not task-quality qualification. Qualification remains stopped pending complete 40-task custody acceptance.\n\n#1 OPEN updated 2026-10-29T06:02:22Z https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1\n---\nmikeholownych 2026-10-29T05:32:15Z\nMetadata-only checkpoint for the release path: PR #318 now has a current-main candidate and its exact-head CI is running. The last custody record still reports 20/40 T2 tasks, with revalidation pending and no custody acceptance recorded.\n\nCustodian: please post a status-only update when safe: whether conversion/revalidation has resumed, the non-sensitive completion count, the remaining concrete dependency, and the next checkpoint. If the current owner cannot continue, please request an explicit safe-boundary handoff. Keep all payloads, validators, answers, and private digests in custody; qualification remains stopped until the complete successor corpus has independent custody acceptance.\n\n#1 OPEN updated 2026-10-29T06:02:22Z https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1\n---\nmikeholownych 2026-10-29T06:02:22Z\nMetadata-only custody ownership reconciliation (2026-10-29): the claims log records `CUSTODY_HANDOFF_ACCEPTED` at 02:21:25Z from former custodian `opencode` (`available=yes`, next claim `CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION`, actor SageBridge). At 04:15:36Z SageBridge recorded `coordination_only`; the current `CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION/owner.json` still names `opencode`. Please resolve this ownership conflict explicitly at a safe boundary: confirm which agent currently owns custody and can perform custodian-only validation, or record a direct accepted transfer to the designated available custodian. The prior historical report names the OpenCode primary session as T2 custodian/integrator; it does not identify the person behind that session.\n\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":566379730}},"started_at_ms":1793255186758,"completed_at_ms":1793255187325}}
