{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T06:31:33.297Z","ordinal":495711,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18651-eaeb-77d3-9068-c0816219322f","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-b46a0926-7d67-40fb-b896-10acf37125fc","process_id":"34513","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","xerj feedback --submit --agent \"Codex GPT-6.1\" --used-for \"Checked Nexus runtime identity implementation while reconciling a reported dogfooding defect against current origin/main\" --verdict \"XERJ located the identity declaration; git grep confirmed exact prompt injection. It is present on origin/main but must still be verified on the next release candidate; indexing was core-only and not sufficient alone.\""],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"xerj feedback --submit --agent \"Codex GPT-6.1\" --used-for \"Checked Nexus runtime identity implementation while reconciling a reported dogfooding defect against current origin/main\" --verdict \"XERJ located the identity declaration; git grep confirmed exact prompt injection. It is present on origin/main but must still be verified on the next release candidate; indexing was core-only and not sufficient alone.\""}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"the `--remote` flag is unsupported when a repository argument is provided\n\nCreate a fork of a repository.\n\nWith no argument, creates a fork of the current repository. Otherwise, forks\nthe specified repository.\n\nBy default, the new fork is set to be your `origin` remote and any existing\norigin remote is renamed to `upstream`. To alter this behavior, you can set\na name for the new fork's remote with `--remote-name`.\n\nThe `upstream` remote will be set as the default remote repository.\n\nAdditional `git clone` flags can be passed after `--`.\n\n\nUSAGE\n  gh repo fork [<repository>] [-- <gitflags>...] [flags]\n\nFLAGS\n  --clone                 Clone the fork\n  --default-branch-only   Only include the default branch in the fork\n  --fork-name string      Rename the forked repository\n  --org string            Create the fork in an organization\n  --remote                Add a git remote for the fork\n  --remote-name string    Specify the name for the new remote (default \"origin\")\n\nINHERITED FLAGS\n  --help   Show help for command\n\nEXAMPLES\n  # Fork a repository\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo\n  \n  # Fork a repository and clone it locally\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo --clone\n  \n  # Fork a repository without cloning it, skip the prompt\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo --clone=false\n\nLEARN MORE\n  Use `gh <command> <subcommand> --help` for more information about a command.\n  Read the manual at https://cli.github.com/manual\n  Learn about exit codes using `gh help exit-codes`\n  Learn about accessibility experiences using `gh help accessibility`\n\nerror: this account cannot push to xerj-org/xerj, and forking failed: `gh repo fork xerj-org/xerj --remote --remote-name xerj-fork` failed\nNothing was branched.\n\n# Ready-to-run — files ONLY the field report, nothing else.\n# Run these in a clone of xerj-org/xerj, not in the project you are working in.\ngit clone https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj.git\ncd xerj\ngh repo fork xerj-org/xerj --remote --remote-name xerj-fork\nxerj feedback \\\n --agent \"Codex GPT-6.1\" \\\n  --used-for \"Checked Nexus runtime identity implementation while reconciling a reported dogfooding defect against current origin/main\" --pointed-at \"1051 records under /home/mike/xerj-sources/nexus-code/core/src (autoindex run run-20261028T022152Z-ff10-0000)\" \\\n  --verdict \"XERJ located the identity declaration; git grep confirmed exact prompt injection. It is present on origin/main but must still be verified on the next release candidate; indexing was core-only and not sufficient alone.\" --numbers \"not measured\" \\\n  -o user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-29-checked-nexus-runtime-identity-implementation.md\ngit checkout -b field-report/checked-nexus-runtime-identity-implementation\ngit add user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-29-checked-nexus-runtime-identity-implementation.md\ngit commit --only user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-29-checked-nexus-runtime-identity-implementation.md -m \"docs(field-report): checked-nexus-runtime-identity-implementation\"\ngit push -u xerj-fork field-report/checked-nexus-runtime-identity-implementation\ngh pr create --repo xerj-org/xerj --base main --head YOUR_LOGIN:field-report/checked-nexus-runtime-identity-implementation \\\n  --title \"Agent field report: Checked Nexus runtime identity implementation while reconciling a reported dogfooding defect against current origin/main\" \\\n  --body \"Field report only; see user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-29-checked-nexus-runtime-identity-implementation.md.\"\nGitHub is unavailable (the pull request could not be opened (see above)); sending the field report to https://xerj.org/api/field-report instead.\nsent field report to https://xerj.org/api/field-report (HTTP 200)\n{\"ok\":true,\"stored\":true,\"note\":\"Thanks. The canonical path is a GitHub PR: https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj/tree/main/user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":16,"nanos":505079142}},"started_at_ms":1793255476791,"completed_at_ms":1793255493297}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T06:31:34.249Z","ordinal":495712,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18651-eaeb-77d3-9068-c0816219322f","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-65dbd36d-b21f-4903-8827-c01e86917664","process_id":"44943","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git grep -n -i -E 'runtime identity|identify this runtime|Claude Code, Codex CLI' origin/main -- cli/test cli/src | head -80; git show --stat --oneline d97ccb70; git show --stat --oneline b9a23d51; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | rg -n -i 'identity|dogfood|rc.10|candidate|rc' | head -35"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git grep -n -i -E 'runtime identity|identify this runtime|Claude Code, Codex CLI' origin/main -- cli/test cli/src | head -80; git show --stat --oneline d97ccb70; git show --stat --oneline b9a23d51; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | rg -n -i 'identity|dogfood|rc.10|candidate|rc' | head -35"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"origin/main:cli/src/agent.ts:231:const NEXUS_RUNTIME_IDENTITY = `### Runtime Identity\norigin/main:cli/src/agent.ts:232:You are Nexus Code, the agent host. The language model provider and model are components Nexus connects to; they do not define or replace the host application. Do not identify this runtime as Claude Code, Codex CLI, OpenCode, or another client based on a model name, provider, skill instructions, or installed executable. When describing the current host or choosing instructions conditional on the host application, identify Nexus Code as the current host. If instructions do not include a compatible Nexus or generic path, explain the mismatch and ask the operator how to proceed.`;\norigin/main:cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts:38:    const hostIdentityAt = systemPrompt.indexOf(\"### Runtime Identity\");\norigin/main:cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts:44:    assert.match(systemPrompt, /Do not identify this runtime as Claude Code/);\nd97ccb70 fix(agent): preserve Nexus runtime identity\n cli/src/agent.ts                        |  9 +++--\n cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts | 63 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 2 files changed, 70 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\nb9a23d51 docs(release): record runtime identity RC gap\n docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | 4 ++--\n 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\n7:**Source gates on main:** `origin/main` is `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d` (PR #312 merge). Exact-main CI run [40802654248](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40802654248) and CodeQL run [40802654255](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40802654255) passed on that SHA. The exact-source requirements gate passed with 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open); 12 requirements remain mapped to exact-RC qualification. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage results, not installed-RC qualification.\n9:**Candidate convergence:** PR #311 remains open at `742d00871c311d6829e8a4d0a1a3a1800701b954` on the older base `cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e`; its prior Node 22/24, Linux x86_64 and CodeQL checks passed, but they do not qualify the current base. A local candidate at `fe28ec9e686b90e69e42a7a13d55f50264b3775f` includes the reviewed source changes and readiness refresh; the completed full suite below ran on a different immutable snapshot and is not exact-candidate evidence. PR #316 carries the terminal-matrix correction at head `2e9ad10df4bab065bc9573680e3ed659709e4293` against main `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d`; independent review accepted that exact head, CodeQL and JS/TS passed, Node 22/24 and Entire Gates remain in progress at 04:23 UTC, and GitHub reports the PR blocked. PR #315's waiver conclusion conflicts with the current release decision and must not be merged as-is.\n11:**Qualification and custody:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The claims identify OpenCode as the prior/current custodian workflow, but do not verify the responsible human identity; SageBridge's 04:15 status says it is coordinating only. The successor T2 store remains 20/40 tasks; the remaining Go/Rust tasks need the reviewed, pinned-toolchain change integrated. Reported T3 digest/schema/isolation checks are 8/8, which is not full T3 task-quality qualification. At 04:23 UTC the OpenCode custodian holds SUITE for two-round setup/reference/oracle revalidation of the 20 converted tasks with isolated HOME; a live validator child process was observed. This is custody revalidation, not held-out qualification; no result or custody acceptance is recorded. Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; the latest metadata-only correction was posted at 04:18 UTC. T2 custody acceptance and qualification, full T3/T4 qualification, current-candidate provider and standalone qualification, fault injection, successor-RC reproducibility and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. RC10 evidence does not qualify a successor candidate.\n13:**Terminal gate:** The release owner requires all 15 manual terminal cells (five environments × three sizes) on the exact installed RC. The latest verified worksheet status is 0/15 accepted cells; blank cells remain incomplete. Actual operator execution and per-cell outcomes are mandatory; automated CI or PTY results do not substitute. [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) waives screenshots only. [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) withdraws the prior matrix-waiver record. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` has the required terminal applications, but the manual matrix remains outstanding.\n15:**Suite evidence:** `make test` completed on immutable snapshot `03bfaa394c906d900574f35104e521844049403c` with isolated HOME and the required evaluator workspace/runtime fixtures: 1,993 tests across 224 suites, 1,991 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped, 0 cancelled; Rust tests and post-test security lifecycle gates passed. The full run took 3,167,118 ms. This snapshot is not exact current main, PR #311 candidate `fe28ec9`, or an RC, so the result does not qualify those revisions. The SUITE claim transferred to the OpenCode custodian at 04:18 UTC for the 20-task custody revalidation above.\n17:**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Stable publication remains gated on mandatory exact-RC qualification and acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted; no further authorization is requested.\n23:**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`, the merge commit for PR #305. Exact-main CI run [40751988282](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40751988282) and CodeQL run [40751988267](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40751988267) passed on that SHA. The source requirements check passed on this revision with 123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, and 12 deferred to exact-RC qualification. These source-stage results do not qualify an installed release candidate.\n25:**Integrated changes and open PRs:** PR #299 merged as `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` (merge commit `145d464dd819a20bf918dfbb4f0176f2c4840a08`). PR #307 merged as `90837aa5193d7c071066d27ccefd2b2ea2db0aff`. PR #305 merged at `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`; its GitHub Entire Gates check concluded **NEUTRAL** (“No trail tracks this branch”). PR #302 was closed unmerged. PR #308 supersedes it and is open at `2c1b2dfa6b10f736367020a86228ab64a4173500` on current base `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`. Exact-head CI run [40757432379](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40757432379) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; Linux packaging/tests remain in progress. CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript passed. The PR head fixes the `globName` test by staging it with the literal `:(literal)` pathspec. A separate local follow-up commit `9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8` applies literal staging to the `magicName` fixture and asserts that it entered the index; this follow-up is not on the PR head. Its focused 77/77 result is owner-reported without a retained log, so that additional fixture change still needs exact-head checks before integration. PR #309 is open at `aace981bc3f46e10f1e57c5498825a76e9994ee5` on the current base. Run [40758300812](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40758300812) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript passed, and Linux packaging/tests are in progress. PR #300 is open at `f3957a67ac8f9b5ea1e60be2494b9402d943230f` on the current base. Run [40757603196](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40757603196) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; Linux packaging/tests remain in progress. A fresh checkpoint accuracy correction was posted on PR #300 (comment [6479279112](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300#issuecomment-6479279112)); this local update addresses the stale PR heads and main-CI status identified there. Source PR checks are distinct from release qualification.\n27:**Qualification and release:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Official cross-runner run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805) passed for the published RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, rebuilding on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Its machine-readable evidence reports `REQ-REL-114` / `ACC-SUP-08` `PASS` and matching hashes for six outputs, including the published archive and `sbom.cdx.json`; see the [RC10 reproducibility record](../reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/README.md). The requirements ledger still marks `REQ-REL-114` `UNV`/open; its owner must reconcile that disposition. RC10 evidence does not establish successor-RC qualification. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned (last updated 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC); no custodian acceptance or held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification is established. The terminal matrix remains 0/15; the user waived screenshot artifacts, while terminal behavior checks remain unrun. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC qualification, required human terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance gates remain outstanding. Stable publication remains gated.\n29:**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Passing source CI and RC10-only provider/reproducibility evidence do not establish release acceptance. Existing publication authorization remains gated by acceptance.\n31:The checkpoints below are retained as historical evidence; their source revision, PR, CI, and qualification statements are superseded by this observation.\n35:**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `145d464dd819a20bf918dfbb4f0176f2c4840a08`. Exact-head CI run [40720824591](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40720824591) passed the Node 22 and Node 24 test matrices; the Linux packaging/reproducibility job was still running at observation time. CodeQL run [40720824319](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40720824319) passed. The CI jobs completed `sync-version --check` and the requirements checker successfully on this source. These results qualify the source revision only; they do not qualify an installed release candidate.\n39:PR [#307](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/307) is based on `145d464` at `88bf19c817f8de7461faf9826e405e52630bb08f`. Its clean-checkout build-identity correction has an independent ACCEPT review for the exact diff (SHA-256 `c0c7b8be14de2cf1aab3246b2f34596ba4aae30c2d527c1afbe93e1ce0105295`); JS/TS, CodeQL and Node 22/24 pass, Linux packaging and Entire remain pending. PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) contains this readiness record at exact head `dded46ba54001bd511aefce4719839f4b77c85ef`; its corrected checkpoint has just been pushed and all exact-head checks are pending. PRs [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) and [#306](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/306) are explicitly v1.1 scope and are not part of the v1.0.0 merge path.\n41:**Requirements and qualification:** Current-main CI's requirements checker passes; the most recent explicit `--enforce` result was on PR #302 head `c3901774` before the nested-workspace-only follow-up: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to installed-RC qualification. RC10 has scope-limited exact-artifact evidence: OpenRouter pinned-model verification and one synthetic live task passed, and the cross-runner workflow passed for the six listed release artifacts across Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 and against published RC10 (run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805)). A later checkpoint correction incorrectly claimed this workflow failed because of an npm-version mismatch. That correction is superseded: GitHub records run `40564959805` and its `compare` job as completed successfully; the current checkpoint above reports that final result. This historical correction is retained here to preserve the audit trail. These results apply only to immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; they do not qualify a successor candidate or establish full release acceptance. The newly pushed #302 head must complete exact checks before its requirements evidence is refreshed. Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. GitHub installer is the selected distribution target; npm publication is inapplicable.\n43:Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; its last update was 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC, with no custodian response observed. No held-out payload was accessed and no held-out qualification was run. The manual terminal matrix's last recorded result is 0/15; terminal setup exists on Ubuntu, but no operator screenshots or cell verdicts have been supplied. Held-out/T2/T3/T4, remaining provider and standalone coverage, successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n45:**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Source CI is mostly complete on `145d464`; PR #302's latest delta awaits independent review and exact Node 22/24 completion, while #307 has independent source review but exact PR checks remain pending. RC10 has passing, bounded provider and cross-runner evidence, but no accepted RC exists and mandatory qualification remains open. Publication authorization remains granted and gated by acceptance.\n47:The checkpoint below (observed 2026-10-28 15:28 UTC) is retained as historical evidence and is superseded for source revision, CI, PR heads, and release-gate state.\n51:**Authoritative source and requirements gate:** `origin/main` is `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212` (PR #304 merge). Current-main CI [40693030763](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030763) and CodeQL [40693030710](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030710) both completed SUCCESS on that exact revision. A clean detached worktree at that exact source ran `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` with isolated `HOME`: 123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. This passes the source-stage enforcement gate only.\n53:**Release PRs and exact-head checks:** PRs [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) (`004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f`), [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) (`11dc196fcdd733f8de71dfc95ff70e109d8f4492`), [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) (`3c52580ae1da6b7f1282018f4d3702dcb75f8bd7`), and [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) (`97f1c6ead710bc059126ba65b37ad1e5fde17666`) are all based on `b2ae2fe`. Exact-head Node 22/24, Linux x86_64, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks passed for these candidates. Their Entire Gates checks are failures, so none is mergeable through the required workflow. PR #302's trail reports five high-severity findings and missing reviewer approval. The independent source reviewer ACCEPTed the cumulative diff after a partial source read and did not run tests as part of that review. A separate owner-authored PR update records `tsc --noEmit` and 53/53 targeted restore tests, and advises a second review of `checkpoint.ts` because of its size. PR #299, #300, and #305 also lack successful Entire approval. No findings were bypassed and no self-approval was recorded.\n57:**Qualification, custody, and publication:** GitHub still lists [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) as the latest release; there is no `v1.0.0` tag or stable release. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, with the last metadata-only custodian request at 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC and no response observed. No protected payload was accessed or qualification run. The manual terminal matrix remains 0/15; the final installed RC does not exist. Exact-RC held-out/T2/T3/T4, provider and standalone coverage, cross-runner reproducibility, human terminal evidence, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. The chosen distribution target remains the GitHub installer; npm publication is inapplicable.\n59:**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. PR integration is blocked by required Entire review findings/approvals; exact-RC qualification is additionally blocked by independent held-out custody and the required human terminal matrix. Existing publication authorization remains granted but gated. The checkpoint below is retained as the 13:34 UTC snapshot and is superseded for current CI, requirements, PR checks, local suite result, and release status.\n63:**Authoritative source:** `origin/main` is `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`, the PR #304 merge. Main CI [40693030763](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030763) has Node 22 and Node 24 matrix jobs passed (13:23:35 and 13:23:05 UTC); Linux x86_64 remains in progress. CodeQL [40693030710](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030710) passed at 13:07:03 UTC. On a clean detached worktree at this exact head, `HOME=/tmp/nexus-req-home XDG_CONFIG_HOME=/tmp/nexus-req-xdg node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 requirements; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to exact-RC qualification. PR #304 adds opt-in v1.1 Git-aware operations to current main; its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed and Entire Gates concluded neutral. The independent review recorded an unresolved correctness defect: an explicit restart recreates a clean worktree while resuming the old agent conversation. That behavior must be fixed and requalified before an RC built from this main can be accepted.\n65:**Source PRs:** PR [#303](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/303) is integrated at `4cac22d`; its exact-head required CI and independent review passed. PR [#304](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/304) is integrated at `b2ae2fe`; its exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, CodeQL and JS/TS checks passed and Entire Gates concluded neutral. Its independent review nevertheless found the restart/conversation defect above. PR [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) addresses that defect at `f7e573ec8de98fb3ec24a96e148a84b4ccab151f`, with independent review ACCEPT at diff SHA-256 `cf1abd6ce5e7083aebe526efaaee85380dee295fced7814a7ddedcd609a11615`. Build and focused test TypeScript check passed; the runtime test was not run locally because `SUITE` is claimed by `kimi-main`. Exact-head Node 22 and Node 24 jobs in run `40694815985` both failed with 1,882 passed, 2 failed and 2 skipped: `durable_continuity.test.ts` expected the explicit-restart recovery warning, and `tdd_work_units.test.ts` uses a fake agent without `restartConversation`. JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; Linux was skipped after the matrix failures, and Entire Gates remain pending. PR [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) is at `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` on base `b2ae2fe`; independent review ACCEPTed this exact head at diff SHA-256 `55afcdc8ed8044bb0aa0a54932c5ba6513763b564bc8fb76014b3334db33ae38`. Its Node 22/24 jobs are in progress, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, and Entire Gates are pending. Issue [#298](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/298) remains open until its fix is integrated and current-main checks pass. At the 13:34:51 UTC snapshot cutoff, before the readiness-only correction was pushed, PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) was at `e1974fd82dba1aba8e5e2e5b1bc9cf964fe6db20` on base `b2ae2fe`; Node 22/24 and Entire were in progress, while JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. The subsequent documentation-only update restarted exact-head checks; the claim record tracks its latest head and current statuses. The independent factual review found stale status/head references in the prior checkpoint; corrected evidence is pending re-review. PR [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) is at `659d6a63a8708ebe98240ec1937b0f2acdcdfac4` on base `b2ae2fe`; Node 22/24, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, while Linux x86_64 (run `40693955666`) is in progress and Entire Gates are pending. Independent read-only review ACCEPTed the final cumulative diff `1099e6ff6b68ab9907ac66c908bf45c8ab1af338d3b6a14227d45d60cf35dc29`; no tests were run as part of review. Exact-head CI is still pending.\n69:**Runtime identity dogfooding defect:** The user-reported RC8 behavior in which a Claude-specific skill led the model to describe Nexus as Claude Code has a source fix in merged PR [#273](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/273), integrated at `d97ccb70c87db096c75e1bd4ff58dbcdf0aa8ab1` (PR merge commit `e94208d09cb4d5023e4379187fc6c603bba960d2`). The fixed system prompt states Nexus Code is the host and is appended after workspace skills; activated skills are also prefaced with `Host application: Nexus Code`. `cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts` reproduces a Claude model plus Claude-specific skill and verifies both boundaries. That test passed 1/1 in an isolated exact-main `b293b44` snapshot; PR #273's Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks passed, and exact-main CI also passed. The public RC10 tag (`16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`) predates the PR merge, so this fix still needs verification in the successor RC.\n71:**Qualification and custody:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` is still the latest release (published 2026-10-27); the package at `b293b44` is also `1.0.0-rc.10`, so source changes require a successor RC before installed-RC qualification. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 exists. Held-out issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest public status request was posted 2026-10-28 12:42 UTC, with no custodian response as of this checkpoint. The public 40-task manifest is not custody acceptance, and no held-out qualification has started. T2/T3/T4, evaluator/custody acceptance, remaining provider and standalone gates, cross-runner reproducibility, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix remains 0/15; the Ubuntu desktop has setup evidence only, with no qualifying screenshots or cell verdicts recorded.\n73:**Disposition:** Engineering convergence remains active; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`. No RC is accepted and no stable release is published. Public RC10 remains the latest release; the repository target is the GitHub installer (npm publication is inapplicable per operator decision). Continue source remediation and exact-head review/CI, then build and qualify a successor RC only after pre-RC gates and PR #305's restart fix pass; keep all installed-RC gates bound to that exact artifact.\n75:The 07:55 checkpoint below is retained as historical evidence; its source, CI, PR, and qualification state is superseded by this checkpoint.\n79:**Authoritative source and source checks:** `origin/main` is `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4`, merge commit for PR [#297](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/297). Its exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks passed; Entire Gates was neutral. Post-merge CI [40652572596](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40652572596) is running and CodeQL [40652572591](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40652572591) passed. Exact-main CI [40647479745](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40647479745) completed successfully on its parent source commit `ceaf60072b7c364edac523d2517fb12df8f5f6cd`, including Node 22/24 tests, Linux tests, packaging, reproducibility, SBOM, and installer checks. The requirements gate also passed on exact current main `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4` in an isolated worktree (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 applicable release-qualification rows remain deferred to their documented exact-RC stages). PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) is being updated to this exact main revision. Source checks do not establish installed-RC acceptance.\n81:**Requested codebase-review findings are part of the v1.0.0 scope:** The large capability registry is split into category modules (`cli/src/core/capabilities.ts`, 10,046 bytes, plus `capability_definitions/`); scheduler logic is in `cli/src/core/scheduler.ts` (23,696 bytes), with `operation.ts` reduced to 12,818 bytes; runner revalidation, execution, and persistence are separated from `operation_runner.ts` (14,931 bytes). Runner decomposition and bounded revalidation/runner diagnostics were integrated through PR [#287](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/287); TDD evidence diagnostics landed through PR [#295](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/295), and scheduler observer diagnostics through PR [#296](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/296). PR [#297](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/297), now merged, adds regression coverage for the TDD diagnostic paths. The capability split and scheduler extraction were integrated through PRs [#286](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/286) and [#285](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/285), respectively. PR [#293](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/293) added operator guidance for `DecisionRejected` and is merged with its Node 22/24, Linux, and CodeQL checks successful. These source changes are implemented on current `main`.\n83:**Lifecycle, scheduler, and evaluation evidence:** `cli/test/convergence_integration.test.ts` covers end-to-end scheduling and execution scenarios. `cli/test/convergence_scheduler_properties.test.ts` runs generated DAG invariants over 100 fixed seeds; this is reproducible generated coverage, not a claim that every scheduler property or arbitrary graph has been proven. PR #297’s regression tests for the TDD diagnostic paths are merged and its required CI passed. The `eval/` pilot suite does not satisfy held-out acceptance: the independent 40-task corpus, custody acceptance, and exact-RC qualification remain required and open.\n87:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Held-out T2/T3/T4, remaining live-provider and standalone gates, successor-RC artifact qualification, cross-runner evidence, the 15-cell human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; stable publication remains gated on these mandatory checks.\n89:The 03:50 checkpoint below is retained as historical evidence; its source, PR, CI, and qualification statements are superseded by this checkpoint.\n93:**Authoritative source and source checks:** `main` is now `d3b7af3ca3d216841f8ff8a0e7b4cefbd637ef9f`, the merge commit for PR [#285](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/285) (merged 2026-10-28 03:38:26 UTC). The exact PR-head Linux retry and required CI passed before merge. Post-merge CI [40627840511](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40627840511) is running the Node 22/24 matrix; CodeQL [40627840517](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40627840517) passed. This is source validation, not installed-RC acceptance. The prior main CI [40621815585](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40621815585) passed on `59f07c4` and does not establish post-merge `d3b7af3` status.\n95:**Integration queue:** PR #285 merged to `d3b7af3`; its exact diff hash and independent ACCEPT were preserved, and the initial state-store lock timeout did not reproduce in its full Linux retry. PR [#289](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/289) is refreshed onto `d3b7af3` at `3f66ee138b1d8aeded2902851f659873d887f307`; its seven-file patch SHA-256 remains `3e13bdaa…`. Fresh Node 22/24/JavaScript checks and Entire Gates are in progress. The first fresh reviewer response described only the docs file, but the GitHub and local diff both contain six implementation/test files plus docs; a complete read-only source review has been requested, so the rebase is not independently accepted yet. PR [#293](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/293), DecisionRejected operator documentation, is refreshed onto `d3b7af3` at `d0e1fbfb10463948b640361bb123177e9490ee1b`; its exact docs diff SHA-256 remains `83de84d7…`. Independent review ACCEPT was reconfirmed at this exact head. Fresh CI is running. Entire's refreshed trail currently reports Approvals failed (no reviewers approved), Findings passed, Up to date passed, and CI pending. The reviewer confirmed no Entire approval integration or distinct identity is available in their session, so the required trail approval remains outstanding. PR [#292](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/292) remains on base `8b24d8e1`, is reported conflicting against current main, and its Entire Gates check failed for missing reviewer approval and staleness. Its remote checks do not establish current-base readiness. No merge is inferred from stale checks.\n97:**RC10 E2 archive repair:** PR #288 restored the 21 retained log files whose entries were already present in the archive manifest, corrected the evidence README's attestation and lifecycle disclosures, and updated `SHA256SUMS`. On the merged candidate, all 45 manifest entries passed `sha256sum -c`; Gitleaks found no leaks; the exact diff received independent ACCEPT. This review accepted the archive repair and factual README corrections only. It did not accept the RC10 E2 product qualification or turn the historical logs into new test results.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":30634}},"started_at_ms":1793255494248,"completed_at_ms":1793255494249}}
