urrent release documentation. Superseded PRs #137 and #146 were closed after their intended policy changes were verified in current main; their older branch evidence is not current qualification evidence.\n509:**RC identity and publication:** Remote immutable tags are `v1.0.0-rc.1` at `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779` and `v1.0.0-rc.2` at `19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`; both predate the accepted Node 22 floor. GitHub currently publishes RC1 as a prerelease; RC2 has a tag but no published release. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 tag/release is established. The next candidate needs a fresh RC3 identity after its source/version checks; it must be installed and qualified before acceptance.\n517:The live GitHub `v1-protected-branches` ruleset (ID `25340146`) currently requires `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, and `linux-x86_64`; it does not require Node 20. The checked-in ruleset snapshot now matches that live required-check set. No live protection setting was modified. PR #137 still targets an older base, PR #146 remains a draft, and the refreshed candidate branch has not yet been opened as a replacement PR. Independent review of the refreshed candidate requested these documentation reconciliations; code/runtime review otherwise found no blocker.\n535:**RC and publication:** The published `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag resolves to `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779`, an ancestor of current `main`, and is not an artifact built from current source. Its published asset digest is `8d7dd32f3d00adb98d4f0ea2c6a484ea8e04fc547b4d78b21b060000eda22b9d`. The next candidate needs a new immutable identity, currently expected to be `v1.0.0-rc.2`, with synchronized version metadata and release notes. Exact-RC artifact/install checks, held-out T2, provider and standalone qualification, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, independent RC acceptance, and stable-promotion disposition remain outstanding. Publication authorization is granted but gated on those results. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release exists.\n537:**Runtime floor:** The merged DEC-12 and current `main` specify Node `>=20`; the upstream release schedule lists Node 20 end of life as 2026-04-30. Open PR #143 proposes to correct that date in the RC1 release note; its exact checks passed on the prior base, and it still needs a refresh against current `main`. README, quickstart, and the development guide still contain the old date on `main`; edits to those files are part of the separate Node 22 lane. PR #137 is open and ready for review, implementing its stated owner-directed `>=22` target. It remains based on old base `8935918` and needs a current-main refresh. Its Node 22/24, Linux packaging, and CodeQL checks pass on that prior base, but the required `test-matrix (20)` context is absent and it has no independent review. The proposed source change is not integrated and conflicts with accepted DEC-12 and REQ-REL-111, which still specify `>=20` and a Node 20/22/24 matrix. The active ruleset requires `test-matrix (20)`, which this candidate omits; its checks are on the prior base and no independent review is recorded. Do not treat `>=22` as v1 policy until the policy records and required checks are formally reconciled. No runtime-floor change is made by this checkpoint.\n581:- **Held-out corpus and custody:** Public T2 manifest `eval/heldout-manifest.json` remains the 40-task identity `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`; T3 public manifest identity remains `85fb9cafbe18e846bd64fb13eb4bfa0f92df0792bc93d12adaa685e04c9f1383`. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) has no custodian response since 2026-10-21 12:21 UTC. Current evaluator qualification rejects the sealed T2 corpus's legacy `hidden.command` format; the documented path requires a custodian-owned compatible immutable successor and repeated custody checks. Private digest re-derivation, exposure history, setup/reference validation, effective access separation, and current custody acceptance remain unverified here. No payload, validator, reference solution, or hidden answer was accessed, and no held-out run has started.\n596:- **Held-out custody and qualification:** The custodian previously accepted the sealed 40-task manifest identity `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b` and its private digest/reference validation. This does not establish evaluator acceptance or T2 qualification. The implementing agent has not accessed private payloads. No held-out run has started because evaluator confidentiality preflight remains unaccepted and corpus/evaluator schema compatibility is unresolved.\n606:- **Evaluator boundary and T2 custody:** PR #33's exact source CI passes resource-bound and Git-history canary fixtures, but the independent unconditional-system-mount finding remains open. Separately, the custodian report accepts the sealed manifest identity `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`, its custody, author-session provenance, private digest validation, and reference validation; private payloads were not inspected for this checkpoint. The sealed tasks use legacy `hidden: { dir, into, command }` checks, while evaluator qualification requires `blackbox-v1`. Custody acceptance does not resolve this format mismatch or evaluator-boundary acceptance. No T2 qualification has started.\n617:- **Qualification host:** PR #22 is still based on `a7126aa` (head `7d30494`); its historical exact-head CI passed, but it is not current-base evidence. The owner confirmed the file split with PR #26 and requested owner approval before running `eval/host/provision.sh`. No host account, sudoers, mount unit, or runtime directory has been provisioned. Resource-limit qualification and held-out execution remain blocked until this host boundary is installed and validated.\n618:- **Held-out T2 custody:** The custodian reported re-derived manifest, 40 task, and 40 private-payload digest matches; isolated author-session audits; and 40/40 reference validation. The public manifest identity is `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`. At 10:38:44 UTC the custodian recorded moving the store and quarantine to `root:root` mode `0700` (task/reference subdirectories `0500`) without changing contents or manifest identity, and explicitly accepted sealed-manifest custody under this boundary. Coordinator verification was limited to metadata (`stat`, `namei`, and a denied `ls` as uid `mike`); private payloads were not inspected. This is custody evidence, not T2 qualification: held-out execution remains blocked on host provisioning, frozen resources, and an installed RC.\n640:  - `.github/workflows/repro.yml` and `scripts/repro-identity.mjs` (`86bdbe6`, PR #20) enforce fail-closed tag/commit/clean-tree/version identity across independent Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builders.\n688:- After the build, isolated `make test` passed: Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087 across 193 suites; zero failures and zero skipped. Runtime was Node 24.11.1. `scripts/security_gates.sh` passed its npm audit (zero high/critical), Rust advisory/license, credential-scan, diff-hygiene and documentation checks. Output is retained outside the repository at `/tmp/nexus-v1-make-test-built-6151.log` (SHA-256 `b72e0e15819985fc48f39998d2adc5ce90e9dd125519784c25a2a2b4d2db9521`).\n708:| `REQ-REL-114` | open (workflow enforced at `86bdbe6`; RC run pending) | `.github/workflows/repro.yml` and `scripts/repro-identity.mjs` (PR #20 `86bdbe6`) enforce fail-closed tag/commit/clean-tree/toolchain/artifact identity across Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builders, covered by `repro_identity.test.ts`. Live execution on an actual RC tag remains pending RC construction. | Final RC tag and `.github/workflows/repro.yml` run | Release engineering | Dispatch `repro.yml` against the exact `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag/commit and archive both runner manifests and comparison evidence. |\n742:### Release identity and source gates\n753:- E2 is **partial**: all eight fresh-install/minimum-runtime cells and eight expected negative preflight cells passed across the prepared Ubuntu 22.04/24.04, Debian 12 and Fedora 40 images. One Ubuntu 22.04 / Node 22 lifecycle cell passed alpha.2 upgrade, repair, rollback and uninstall. The remaining lifecycle cases are not complete. Current-source evaluator host preflight passed 10/10 using synthetic markers only; this is not held-out custody or qualification evidence.\n760:- Reproducibility workflow [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) built successfully on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 from the exact tag, but its official `compare` job **failed**. The comparator's earlier archive and compatibility checks passed; it then found that `metadata.tools` records npm `10.9.9` in the published RC SBOM versus npm `10.9.4` in both rebuild SBOMs. Because it stopped at that mismatch, the later `install.sh` comparison was not reached. A local comparison of only the runner identity artifacts passed but did not establish `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08`; the official result is authoritative. `REQ-REL-114` remains open until the toolchain is aligned, the release/rebuild evidence is regenerated as needed, and a new exact-RC comparison passes.\n780:- **Authoritative source:** `origin/main` is `8580c821f57119768db01614d31cd60e8766468b`, the merge of PR #306 on top of `90837aa` (which contains PR #307). PR #306 adds operation context budgeting and durable conversation checkpoints. PR #307's build-identity change is present on this main revision.\n781:- **Requirements and version checks:** On a clean detached worktree at exactly `8580c82`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows; tested 108, partial 6, implemented 2, open 7. The 12 listed rows remain deferred to exact-RC qualification. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passed with all components at `1.0.0-rc.10`.\n",