{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T06:35:00.325Z","ordinal":495863,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0db389702a7164cc016ae2e9096688819f82441e3713ec757e","status":"completed","call_id":"call_0bc940e6940c4e3f88fdd0094e323279","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:`python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path('docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md')\ntext = p.read_text()\nstart = text.index('## Current release checkpoint (')\nend = text.index('## Historical checkpoint', start)\nsection = \"\"\"## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 06:36 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` is `91e394900ee8a9b7c813866c54543abc1f7dd74c`, merging PR #320 atop `a0356c4d8f0f0b9b943d4033aff59795fcab83b4`; `origin/v1/integration` remains `7d6673f108316dda015b858c85b2abe20f3a4f78`. Post-merge CI [40829723082](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40829723082) is still running the Node 22/24 test suites; CodeQL [40829723067](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40829723067) passed on exact main. On a clean detached worktree at exact `91e39490`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 deferred to exact-RC qualification), and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passed with all components at `1.0.0-rc.10`. Source gates do not establish installed-RC acceptance.\n\n**Integrated changes and open PRs:** PR #319 (UTF-8 batch reads) merged as `a0356c4d` after exact-head required CI and independent review passed. PR #320 (manual terminal harness and screenshot-waiver handling) merged as `91e39490` after Node 22/24, Linux packaging, JS/TS, and CodeQL passed; Entire Gates concluded neutral. PR [#322](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/322), head `d53caea7c480c5e88dff43c6e5d4cb8a16868400`, adds CI-only pinned Go/Rust toolchain provisioning for PR #318; independent review ACCEPT, Node 22/24, JS/TS, and CodeQL passed, while exact-head Linux remains in progress. PR [#318](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/318), head `2c532d701c5b84b0d3308b02897520337addc36b`, has independent ACCEPT source review but its Node 22/24 jobs failed because `eval_hardened.test.ts` could not find `go` (exit 127); Linux was skipped. It must be rebased and rerun after #322 integrates. PR [#321](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/321), head `84e6bb7ce9e2ba3cc287db5a40119937870c51d4`, is the readiness refresh on base `a0356c4d`; its independent review ACCEPT and checks (Node 22 passed, Node 24 running, JS/TS and CodeQL passed) apply to that exact old base/head. After #320 moved main to `91e39490`, this candidate is being refreshed and must receive new exact-head checks and review. It is not merged.\n\n**Runtime identity dogfood defect:** The user's RC8 dogfood run showed Nexus following a skill's instruction to identify as Claude Code. The fix is integrated in current main as `d97ccb70c87db096c75e1bd4ff58dbcdf0aa8ab1` (`cli/src/agent.ts`) with regression coverage in `cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts`; it is an ancestor of `6b786d54`, whose CI [40822684551](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40822684551) passed. The immutable RC10 tag does not contain this instruction or test, so RC10 does not demonstrate the fix. Build the successor RC from a source revision containing it and independently verify Nexus identity using the installed artifact before acceptance.\n\n**Held-out custody and qualification:** Public issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) has no update after 06:02 UTC. It records unresolved ownership: the historical accepted-handoff entry names SageBridge, while the active `CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION` claim still names OpenCode and supplies no host/PID/worktree for safe activity reconciliation. The latest posted count is 20/40 tasks; no custody acceptance or qualification result is recorded. T3's reported 8/8 is digest/schema/isolation metadata only, not task-quality qualification. No private payload was accessed by implementers. T2 custody acceptance and T2/T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider acceptance, long-task/fault-injection qualification, and successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility remain incomplete. Qualification must remain stopped until custody ownership, integrity, and acceptance are independently resolved.\n\n**Terminal and release gates:** Acceptance §5.3 requires an operator to run five real terminal environments (xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60: **0/15 accepted cells**. A fresh SSH preflight to `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`) confirmed all five terminal programs are installed, GNOME Terminal 3.58.0 and tmux 3.6; the RC10 qualification binary reports `1.0.0-rc.10 (16ee8ca36438)` and SHA-256 `320d7dc1603d30f863a9560a9101ab3fe1a57f164b7119c49e01d9ace40792c4`. This is environment preparation only, not a matrix result. The successor RC is not yet available. The new `scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md` contains the human procedure; DEC-18 waives screenshots only, and all interactive checks, per-cell verdicts, measurements and exact-artifact identity remain mandatory. The latest public release is `v1.0.0-rc.10`; the approved distribution target is the GitHub installer, not npm. No stable `v1.0.0` release exists.\n\n**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Publication authorization remains granted but gated on complete mandatory acceptance. Main is `91e39490`; post-merge Node 22/24 CI is still running. PR #322's Linux check and #321's old-base Node 24 check remain in progress; #321 must be rebased and re-reviewed, and #318 must be requalified after #322. Held-out custody, protected qualification, successor-RC construction and qualification, manual terminal evidence and independent exact-RC acceptance remain open.\n\n\"