 `AGENTS.md` already states that `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file` must be set before running any `entire` command, and gives `export ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file` as the example.\n\nThe shared checkout’s dirty `AGENTS.md` is missing that section, so I left it untouched to preserve its other work. No repository change is needed on `origin/main`.","turn_id":"01a18647-4a32-7a30-bab7-2a3c3cdf19a7"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2e5e13e94819f9df305314db4b10e","order":23195,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18651-f9af-7133-b347-c9e931082f09","text":"The independent reviewer has accepted the updated readiness PR. I’m refreshing its exact-head checks and the main branch’s post-merge CI now, then I’ll advance any lane that is clear to integrate.","turn_id":"01a18651-eaeb-77d3-9068-c0816219322f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2e6712784819f8039c697be2fa727","order":23198,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18654-2d20-7352-b9b5-7ac21974f117","text":"The release-critical PRs are still progressing on exact heads: PR #322 and #320 have Node, CodeQL, and JS/TS checks green, with Linux packaging/reproducibility running; PR #321 has its independent ACCEPT and the two Node suites still running. I’ve recorded the review disposition in the readiness claim.","turn_id":"01a18651-eaeb-77d3-9068-c0816219322f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2e85f7768819f8429338149e98d6d","order":23205,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1865b-b750-73b2-a35a-e278119e2847","text":"The RC8 identity defect has a source fix and regression test on current `origin/main`, but the published RC10 artifact predates that fix. I’m checking the readiness record so the next candidate explicitly carries this release blocker instead of letting the source fix be mistaken for installed-RC evidence.","turn_id":"01a18651-eaeb-77d3-9068-c0816219322f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2e8b19f18819f9b7ff77d444cda5d","order":23206,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1865c-f8a3-78f1-9b8e-f3835050f0cb","text":"PR #320 has now merged as `91e39490`, after all required checks and independent ACCEPT. That advances main while PR #321’s checks are still running on the prior base. I’m rebasing the readiness branch locally onto the new main, preserving the identity-gap update; I’ll wait for those old checks to finish before triggering the fresh exact-head run.","turn_id":"01a18651-eaeb-77d3-9068-c0816219322f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2e96851c8819f96ca075296414926","order":23209,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1865f-c22f-7c11-9237-be9aeb6e4511","text":"PR #320’s merge is now reflected in the readiness branch. I also recorded the dogfooding identity gap: current main has the fix and test, while published RC10 lacks both. Exact-main requirements enforcement and version sync pass at `91e39490`; I’m holding the readiness push until the prior checks and independent review finish.","turn_id":"01a18651-eaeb-77d3-9068-c0816219322f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2eb13355c819fa62c73852951728c","order":23220,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18666-481f-7f21-8cdc-ef6dccbab1b2","text":"PR #322 has merged as `183158f0`, resolving the missing Go/Rust toolchain setup that caused #318’s hosted test failures. Its required checks and independent review passed. Main post-merge CI is running on the new head; I’m keeping the #318 and readiness updates isolated until those runs finish.","turn_id":"01a18651-eaeb-77d3-9068-c0816219322f"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":23224,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":15987,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c","receiver_turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c\nSource thread: 01a15488-7e03-70f3-9a99-99c