QL passed; Entire Gates concluded neutral. PR #322 (pinned Go/Rust evaluator toolchains for CI) merged as 183158f0 after exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, JS/TS, CodeQL and independent review passed; its post-merge CI and CodeQL remain active. PR [#318](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/318) has been refreshed onto current main at 07e2d2c63fcd2cded4331c88d3c0c5bfb323a930. Its four-file evaluator diff is unchanged at SHA-256 56ab8a3ecef2ada575aacd09e3e5148948fb6b013640c92b071d11598a629184, matching the previously independently ACCEPTed patch. On the refreshed head, Node 22/24 and Linux are in progress; JS/TS and CodeQL pass. No new held-out task or payload was used. PR [#321](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/321) still remotely points to old head 84e6bb7 on base a0356c4; Node 22/24, JS/TS and CodeQL passed there, Linux is running, and Entire is in progress. A local readiness candidate has been refreshed onto exact main 183158f0 at c5aa1f4555dea53f1796907fab774c4538fd0f21; it has no new exact-head checks or independent review yet and has not been pushed. No PR #318 or #321 merge is claimed.\n\n**Runtime identity dogfood defect:** The user's RC8 dogfood run showed Nexus following a skill's instruction to identify as Claude Code. The source fix is integrated in current main as d97ccb70c87db096c75e1bd4ff58dbcdf0aa8ab1 (cli/src/agent.ts), with regression coverage in cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts; it is an ancestor of exact-main 6b786d54, whose CI [40822684551](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40822684551) passed. The immutable RC10 tag does not contain the new explicit identity guard or regression test, so RC10 does not demonstrate the fix. Build the successor RC from a source revision containing it and independently verify Nexus identity using the installed artifact before acceptance.\n\n**Local AI provider setup:** The reported missing local setup option is implemented by PR [#256](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/256), “configure local AI endpoint from connect flow,” merged as 1aa8832ba280c3bb01941fc73a28f9549146e8fa. Its exact Node 22/24, Linux, CodeQL, and JS/TS checks passed. The RC10 tag contains the appliance setup row in core/src/bin/nexus_tui/models.rs and the local endpoint connect flow in the sidecar; this confirms feature presence in that package, not a recorded operator interaction. Verify the flow again from the installed successor RC before acceptance.\n\n**Held-out custody and qualification:** Public issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) has no update since 06:02 UTC. It records unresolved ownership: the historical accepted-handoff entry names SageBridge, while the active CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION claim still names OpenCode and supplies no host/PID/worktree for safe activity reconciliation. The latest posted count is 20/40 tasks; no custody acceptance or qualification result is recorded. T3's reported 8/8 is digest/schema/isolation metadata only, not task-quality qualification. No private payload was accessed by implementers. T2 custody acceptance and T2/T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider acceptance, long-task/fault-injection qualification, and successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility remain incomplete. Qualification must remain stopped until custody ownership, integrity, and acceptance are independently resolved.\n\n**Terminal and release gates:** Acceptance §5.3 requires an operator to run five real terminal environments (xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60: **0/15 accepted cells**. A fresh SSH preflight to ubuntu-desktop (10.0.8.3) confirmed all five terminal programs are installed: xterm 407, kitty 0.45.0, GNOME Terminal 3.58.0, tmux 3.6, and VS Code 1.143.1; the RC10 qualification binary reports 1.0.0-rc.10 (16ee8ca36438) and SHA-256 320d7dc1603d30f863a9560a9101ab3fe1a57f164b7119c49e01d9ace40792c4. This is environment preparation only, not a matrix result. The successor RC is not yet available. The new scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md contains the human procedure; DEC-18 waives screenshots only, and all interactive checks, per-cell verdicts, measurements and exact-artifact identity remain mandatory. The latest public release is v1.0.0-rc.10; the approved distribution target is the GitHub installer, not npm. No stable v1.0.0 release exists.\n\n**Disposition:** NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE; acceptance IN_PROGRESS. Publication authorization remains granted but gated on complete mandatory acceptance. Main is 183158f0 with post-merge CI/CodeQL active. PR #318 has current-base exact checks in progress; PR #321 is stale remotely and awaits a fresh reviewed/pushed candidate after current suites complete. Held-out custody, protected qualification, successor-RC construction and qualification, manual terminal evidence and independent exact-RC acceptance remain open.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 04:23 UTC; superseded)\n\n**Remote revision reconciliation:** `origin/main` is `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d`; `origin/v1/integration` is `7d6673f108316dda015b858c85b2abe20f3a4f78`. The integration ref is an ancestor of main (875 commits behind), not a divergent head. Current release PRs target main; evidence from the two refs must remain distinct.\n\n**Source gates on main:** `origin/main` is `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d` (PR #312 merge). Exact-main CI run [40802654248](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40802654248) and CodeQL run [40802654255](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40802654255) passed on that SHA. The exact-source requirements gate passed with 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open); 12 requirements remain mapped to exact-RC qualification. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports `1.0.0-rc.10`. These are source-stage results, not installed-RC qualification.\n\n**Candidate convergence:** PR #311 remains open at `742d00871c311d6829e8a4d0a1a3a1800701b954` on the older base `cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e`; its prior Node 22/24, Linux x86_64 and CodeQL checks passed, but they do not qualify the current base. A local candidate at `fe28ec9e686b90e69e42a7a13d55f50264b3775f` includes the reviewed source changes and readiness refresh; the completed full suite below ran on a different immutable snapshot and is not exact-candidate evidence. PR #316 carries the terminal-matrix correction at head `2e9ad10df4bab065bc9573680e3ed659709e4293` against main `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d`; independent review accepted that exact head, CodeQL and JS/TS passed, Node 22/24 and Entire Gates remain in progress at 04:23 UTC, and GitHub reports the PR blocked. PR #315's waiver conclusion conflicts with the current release decision and must not be merged as-is.\n\n**Qualification and custody:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The claims identify OpenCode as the prior/current custodian workflow, but do not verify the responsible human identity; SageBridge's 04:15 status says it is coordinating only. The successor T2 store remains 20/40 tasks; the remaining Go/Rust tasks need the reviewed, pinned-toolchain change integrated. Reported T3 digest/schema/isolation checks are 8/8, which is not full T3 task-quality qualification. At 04:23 UTC the OpenCode custodian holds SUITE for two-round setup/reference/oracle revalidation of the 20 converted tasks with isolated HOME; a live validator child process was observed. This is custody revalidation, not held-out qualification; no result or custody acceptance is recorded. Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; the latest metadata-only correction was posted at 04:18 UTC. T2 custody acceptance and qualification, full T3/T4 qualification, current-candidate provider and standalone qualification, fault injection, successor-RC reproducibility and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. RC10 evidence does not qualify a successor candidate.\n\n**Terminal gate:** The release owner requires all 15 manual terminal cells (five environments × three sizes) on the exact installed RC. The latest verified worksheet status is 0/15 accepted cells; blank cells remain incomplete. Actual operator execution and per-cell outcomes are mandatory; automated CI or PTY results do not substitute. [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) waives screenshots only. [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) withdraws the prior matrix-waiver record. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` has the required terminal applications, but the manual matrix remains outstanding.\n\n**Suite evidence:** `make test` completed on immutable snapshot `03bfaa394c906d900574f35104e521844049403c` with isolated HOME and the required evaluator workspace/runtime fixtures: 1,993 tests across 224 suites, 1,991 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped, 0 cancelled; Rust tests and post-test security lifecycle gates passed. The full run took 3,167,118 ms. This snapshot is not exact current main, PR #311 candidate `fe28ec9`, or an RC, so the result does not qualify those revisions. The SUITE claim transferred to the OpenCode custodian at 04:18 UTC for the 20-task custody revalidation above.\n\n**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Stable publication remains gated on mandatory exact-RC qualification and acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted; no further authorization is requested.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 20:18 UTC; superseded)\n\nThis historical checkpoint includes a matrix-waiver conclusion that was later withdrawn by the current DEC-19 decision. It records the prior checkpoint only and is not the current acceptance disposition.\n\n**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origi