{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T07:02:20.577Z","ordinal":497075,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a18677-7ea1-7d50-9576-02cd68542afe","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2912)\nTotal output lines: 110\n\n# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Made something a person can open (PR, deck, page, image, report)? Attach it to that item: fields {\"work_product\": \"https://…\" or \"/absolute/file\"}; several, with titles, as one JSON string: \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"}]\"\n- Deliverables: write a deck, report, page or other file the person asked for as a file and attach it as work_product before you finish. When you stop, claude-mem copies each attached file (and any deck, document, page, image or spreadsheet you wrote outside the source tree) into this project's deliverables bucket, ~/.claude-mem/deliverables/<project>/, and links it on the request's card in My Work.\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- ...551 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-10-29 7:02am UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 50 obs (19,788t read) | 112,072t work | 82% savings\n\n### Oct 27, 2026\nS1755 RC10 CI monitoring — PR #263 linux-x86_64 and PR #264 Node 22/24 still in progress; OpenRouter E5 task classified incomplete (Oct 27, 2:32 AM)\nS1756 RC10 CI monitoring and qualification gate status — PR #263 fully green, PR #264 linux still running, manual terminal matrix 0/15 (Oct 27, 2:37 AM)\nS1778 Nexus v1.0.0 release gate monitoring — CI polling, PR code reviews (#299, #301, #302), and work state checkpointing (Oct 27, 2:54 AM)\n### Oct 28, 2026\nS1772 Nexus v1.0.0 release gate monitoring — session start status check and PR investigation (Oct 28, 8:25 AM)\nS1773 Entire Review of PR #301 (operation view) — independent read-only code review while monitoring PR #302 CI (Oct 28, 8:58 AM)\nS1774 Nexus v1.0.0 release gate monitoring — PR #301 review, ubuntu-desktop E3 preflight, and CI polling (Oct 28, 9:07 AM)\nS1779 Nexus v1.0.0 release gate monitoring — PR #302 independent review, CI polling, and claims log maintenance (Oct 28, 9:09 AM)\nS1780 Nexus v1.0.0 release gate monitoring — CI polling continues for PRs #301/#302, Entire auth investigation, claims log maintenance (Oct 28, 9:15 AM)\nS1781 Nexus v1.0.0 release gate monitoring — requirements enforcement, ruleset verification, PR review, and CI polling after new main commit (Oct 28, 9:16 AM)\n### Oct 29, 2026\n24158 2:14a ○ PR #311 Both Node 22/24 Passed — linux-x86_64 Job Now Queued; All Required Matrix Gates Green\n24095 \" ○ System Under Sustained IO Pressure — retention.test.ts Blocked 2m39s on jbd2\n24174 2:15a ○ Custodian Identity Gap Confirmed by User — No Documentation of Prior Custodian Rights\n24096 2:16a ○ retention.test.ts Process Exited — IO Pressure Dropping After Journal Flush\n24097 2:17a ○ opencode Process Confirmed Live — Former Custodian Identity Not Established, Authorized Routing Required\n24098 \" ○ Agent Mail Summary — DEC-19 Waiver Contradictions Documented, Custody Lane Blocked, Four Persistent Action Items\n24099 2:19a ○ Custody Candidate Session Identified — Session ses_eb3269f3 from Oct 18 Matches Custody Metadata Only, Authorization Unverified\n24100 \" ○ Entire Brain Status — Retrieval UNSAFE Due to 161 Uncommitted Paths in Worktree\n24101 2:20a ○ Full Worktree State and Claims Inventory — 60+ Active Claims, Multiple dogfood Worktrees, CLAIM GATEWAY Entry\n24102 \" ○ Full Suite Run on Snapshot 03bfaa3 Failed — Multiple TUI/PTY and Eval Tests Failed, SUITE Released\n24103 \" ○ PR #314 Full Review Details — Mandatory 15-Cell Terminal Matrix Across 5 Terminals × 3 Sizes Documented\n24104 \" ○ PR #311 Node 22/24 Both Passed — linux-x86_64 Started at 02:14 UTC, Entire Gates Still Pending\n24105 \" ○ linux-x86_64 CI Job Full Step Sequence Revealed — Packaging, SBOM, Reproducibility Checks Pending After npm test\n24106 \" ○ PR #312 and PR #313 Both Confirmed MERGED — Merge Timestamps and Heads Established\n24107 \" ○ Active Agent Roster — Four Agents: /root Running, Two Completed, One Interrupted\n24108 \" ○ Local Suite Still Running on Snapshot 03bfaa3 — C…443 tokens truncated…age\n24119 2:29a ○ nexus-trail23 Final Suite Results — 1989/1993 Pass, 2 Failures, 2 Skipped\n24120 \" ○ resource contract Failure Root Cause — 3 Survivor Processes After cgroup Exit, Expected 0\n24121 \" ○ Both nexus-trail23 Failures Confirmed as CI-Fixture Precondition Failures, Not Logic Regressions\n24122 \" ○ CI Workflow Configures NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT and RUNTIME_ROOT — Both Tests Require GHA Runner Setup\n24123 \" ○ CI Fixture Setup — tmpfs Mount at /mnt/nexus-eval-ci with bubblewrap, user-cgroups, and Go/Node Prerequisites\n24124 \" ○ resource contract Test Falls Back to /dev/shm — Local Run Used Wrong Workspace Root\n24127 2:30a ○ eval/resources.mjs and eval/isolate.mjs Not in Source Tree — Built Artifacts Required for Tests\n24128 \" ○ /srv/nexus-qual/ws IS Mounted as tmpfs — resource contract Failure Was Pure cgroup Survivor Leak\n24131 \" ○ eval/resources.mjs Found at Top-Level /home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-trail23-verify-03bf/eval/ — Not Under cli/\n24132 \" ○ ensure-ci-user-cgroups.sh Requires systemd User Scope Delegation — Missing on Local Host Caused survivorsAfterExit Failure\n24134 \" ○ Local Host Has sudo, setpriv, and User systemd — cgroup Delegation Gap Is Fixable\n24136 2:31a ✓ Local CI Fixtures Provisioned — 128MB tmpfs at /mnt/nexus-trail23-capped and Runtime Root at /var/tmp/nexus-trail23-runtime\n24140 \" ✓ Targeted Rerun of Two Failing Tests with Local CI Fixtures — In Progress\n24143 2:32a ○ resource contract Test PASSES With Local CI Fixtures — Confirmed Pure Environment Gap\n24146 \" ○ eval_version_probe_storage Fails — Runtime Root at /var/tmp Rejected as \"Protected Candidate Runtime Root Forbidden\"\n24148 2:33a ○ /opt/nexus-eval-ci-runtime Already Exists with Correct Permissions — Local CI Runtime Root Ready\n24150 \" ○ eval_version_probe_storage Passes With /opt/nexus-eval-ci-runtime — Both Suite Failures Confirmed as Pure Environment Gaps\n24152 \" ✓ SUITE Claim Updated and Claims Log Triage Entry Written — Final Full make test Rerun Starting\n24157 2:34a ○ Final Full Suite Rerun Started — cargo test Running core/Cargo.toml After 44 Seconds\n\nAccess 112k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n⚠️ Heads up: claude-mem can't save memories right now.\n\nThe memory observer's allowance on claude is used up (since 2026-10-29T02:39:06.521Z).\n\nLatest error: Claude rejected the request because its five-hour usage allowance is exhausted.\n\nUntil the allowance resets or you add capacity, nothing from this session — or any\nother — will be remembered.\n\nRestarting will NOT help here: it does not replenish the allowance or clear the\npersisted cooldown — so please leave the worker alone.\nSwitch the observer to another provider in ~/.claude-mem/settings.json if you need\nmemory capture before the allowance resets.\n\n(Assistant: tell the user about this outage at the very start of your first reply,\nquoting the error above. Do NOT restart the worker and do NOT suggest restarting it.)\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only.\nServer runtime: use Smart search by default in three steps—search({query}) for an index, timeline({anchor: ID}) for context, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records selected after reviewing the index and timeline. These tools use the configured server project; optional projectId selects another authorized server project. No auto or guided modes. Dumb search is unavailable in this runtime.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed.\n\nFull hook output saved to: /tmp/hook_outputs/01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731/14297ca9-1124-4c6c-9a4a-0f6570ff7d2f.txt"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18669-d27e-75d2-996e-5705cd6cc03e","create_time":1793257340.5777063,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"],"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"harness","hook":true}}]}}}
