{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T07:03:34.061Z","ordinal":497121,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18678-40eb-70b2-b167-11dc8ca1d04f","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a18678-40eb-70b2-b167-11dc8ca1d04f","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae2efc22e1c819f85d6cf6c18a731f9","usage":{"input_tokens":86897,"cached_input_tokens":74624,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":333,"reasoning_output_tokens":316,"total_tokens":87230},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":229939,"cached_input_tokens":209792,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1193,"reasoning_output_tokens":671,"total_tokens":231132},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9293063343,"cached_input_tokens":9193994752,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":26915631,"reasoning_output_tokens":15780297,"total_tokens":9319978974}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T07:03:37.053Z","ordinal":497122,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a18678-a95d-7b60-8dc4-a493b218901a","call_id":"call_d932a48860bb4911b61c912c5855039a","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr311_draft_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — exact four-file diff SHA-256: `56ab8a3ecef2ada575aacd09e3e5148948fb6b013640c92b071d11598a629184`.\\n\\nPinned toolchain roots and their contents are checked for root ownership, canonical paths, and write/symlink safety before use. Candidate and Python oracle mounts are read-only; oracle launches clear the environment, use offline Go/Rust settings and temporary caches, and refuse protected-corpus overlap. The fixtures cover unsafe roots, production launch paths, and Go/Rust execution.\\n\\n**Independence note:** I previously reviewed related evaluator-toolchain and provisioning changes, so this is a fresh review of the exact candidate, but should not be represented as fully independent of those earlier reviews. No tests run.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr300_readiness\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**CHANGES_REQUIRED** for PR #318.\\n\\nExact diff SHA-256: `56ab8a3ecef2ada575aacd09e3e5148948fb6b013640c92b071d11598a629184`.\\n\\n- Oracle code can bypass the approved compiler paths: the sandbox mounts all of `/usr/bin` read-only, while Python oracle code can execute arbitrary subprocesses. Setting `PATH` to prefer pinned Go/Rust roots does not prevent invoking unapproved compilers by absolute path. The new tests check PATH and mount arguments but do not exercise this escape.\\n- The toolchain versions are not fixed: CI selects Go `1.22.x` and copies whichever Rust sysroot the runner provides, comparing each copy only to its source. Runner image or toolcache updates can silently change the qualification compilers.\\n\\nThe new mounts are read-only and checked for ownership, permissions, and symlinks; oracle caches are placed under `/tmp`, and offline settings are applied. I did not edit files or run tests.\\n\\n\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr302\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Trail 30 is the matching open change for PR #315’s exact branch and head. Its approval list is empty.\\n\\nI did **not** approve: `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file entire auth status` identifies the active account as **Mike Holownych**, the PR author and trail author/assignee. Only that one Entire context is configured, so I have no independent non-owner authenticated identity to submit the approval. The approval remains outstanding.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18678-40eb-70b2-b167-11dc8ca1d04f","create_time":1793257417.0530434}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
