ound this memory)\";\n322-\n--\n352-/** How an earlier version marked a finding it cut to its start; such copies are still read from persisted records. */\n353-const LEGACY_SHORTENED = \" …[shortened to fit this memory]\";\n354:const FINDINGS_OUTGROWN = \"[Nexus: your recorded findings have outgrown this memory. As more are recorded, the oldest are shown condensed, then only indexed, then only listed by id; read_findings returns any of them in full. Write what you have established into your work product now (the file or change your task produces; if it produces none, state it in the task_completed summary), and before stating that something is absent or never happens, check your findings with read_findings; then continue with what remains.]\";\n355-const FINDINGS_INSTRUCTIONS = \"You keep the working notes of an autonomous software-engineering agent. The tool output below is about to be removed from the agent's context window. Record, for the agent's current request, what this output actually shows: concrete facts with file paths, symbol names and line numbers, and anything it shows to be missing or inconsistent. Write each fact as its own line, with the file path or symbol it concerns. State only what the output itself shows; do not speculate, plan, or restate the request. Where output is marked as cut off, limited or incomplete, say what it could not show, and do not record that something is absent on the strength of it. If the output is irrelevant to the request, say so in one line. Plain text, at most 250 words.\";\n356-\n357-function unseenTruncationNotice(shown: number, total: number): string {\n358:  return `\\n[Nexus: output truncated to fit the context window; showed the first ${shown} of ${total} characters. The rest was not shown to you, so do not assume what it contains. Note what you learned from this part, then inspect the specific parts you still need with narrower calls (read_file with start_line/end_line, outline_file, search_code) instead of repeating this one.]`;\n359-}\n360-\n361-// Only a well-formed trailing notice marks a truncated result; file text that quotes the template does not.\n362:const UNSEEN_TRUNCATION = /\\n\\[Nexus: output truncated to fit the context window; showed the first \\d+ of \\d+ characters\\.[^\\]\\n]*\\]$/;\n363-\n364-function isTruncatedObservation(message: ChatMessage): boolean {\n--\n442-\n443-/** The note `toolResultContent` puts before a re-run's output; not part of the output's identity. */\n444:const RERUN_NOTICE = /^\\[Nexus: you ran this same call before;[^\\]]*\\]\\n/;\n445:const STEP_NOTICE = /^\\[Nexus: (your recorded findings have outgrown your memory|this is step \\d+ of \\d+);[^\\]]*\\]\\n/;\n446:const CUT_NOTICE = /^\\[Nexus: your response at step \\d+ was cut off[^\\]]*\\]\\n/;\n447-/** A response that failed after running this long was most likely ended by the provider's limit on how long one may take. */\n448-const LONG_RESPONSE_MS = 120_000;\n--\n461-    : \" Keep each reply well under that size.\";\n462-  const dropped = calls.length ? \"Nothing from that reply ran and no file was written\" : \"None of that reply was kept\";\n463:  return `[Nexus: your previous reply was cut off at ${limit} ${what}. ${dropped}; it is not in this conversation.${parts} Do not resend the same reply in one piece: it would be cut off again, and a second cut-off reply in a row ends the turn. This is ${position}. Continue the task.]`;\n464-}\n465-\n466-function cutResponseNotice(step: number, seconds: number): string {\n467:  return `[Nexus: your response at step ${step} was cut off after ${seconds} s, before it was complete, most likely because the provider ends a response that takes too long; none of it was used. Respond with less at once. Write a long file in parts: write_file with its first part, then add each further part with edit_file in later steps, replacing the file's last few lines (enough that they occur nowhere earlier in it) with those lines followed by the next part. End each part where every bracket it opens is closed. Keep every response short enough to finish well within ${seconds} s.]`;\n468-}\n469-\n--\n824-}) {\n825-  try {\n826:    const auditDir = path.join(os.homedir(), \".nexus\");\n827-    ensurePrivateDir(auditDir);\n828-    const auditPath = path.join(auditDir, \"audit.log\");\n--\n1702-        const text = readOnly\n1703-          ? `Workspace MCP servers and plugins are not loaded in read-only mode (${names}).`\n1704:          : `Workspace MCP servers and plugins are not loaded because this workspace is not trusted (${names}). Run \\`nexus trust\\` in it to allow them.`;\n1705-        if (this.observer?.onNotice) this.observer.onNotice(text);\n1706-        else console.warn(pc.yellow(text));\n--\n2120-    const approved = await this.ensureVerifierApproved(command, confirmHandler);\n2121-    if (!approved) return { independent: false, detail: \"verifier execution was not approved\" };\n2122:    // Nexus edited test files: run the tests as they were before the change against the changed code.\n2123-    const dir = prepareBaselineTestsCopy(this.config.workspace, this.changeBaseline!.tests!, this.changeBaseline!.verifier!);\n2124:    if (!dir) return { independent: false, detail: \"the workspace is too large to rerun the pre-change tests without Nexus's own test edits\" };\n2125-    try {\n2126-      this.activity(\"verifying\", { tool: `${command} (tests as they were before the change)` });\n--\n2128-      const run = await runTestSuiteWithExecutor(this.config.workspace, (c) => this.bridge.executeTool(\"run_command\", { command: `cd ${quoted} && ${c}`, timeout_secs: deadlineSecs }), command);\n2129-      return run.success && hasExecutedTests(run.rawOutput || \"\")\n2130:        ? { independent: true, detail: \"tests that failed before the change pass after it, with Nexus's own test edits set aside\" }\n2131:        : { independent: false, detail: \"it passes only with tests Nexus wrote or edited; the tests as they were before the change still fail\" };\n2132-    } finally {\n2133-      fs.rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n--\n2249-        tool_call_id: call.id,\n2250-        name: call.function.name,\ncli/src/agent.ts\ncli/test/agent_discovered_verifier_premutation.test.ts\ncli/test/agent_observer.test.ts\ncli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts\ncli/test/agent_terminal_controls.test.ts\ncli/test/agt111_subagent_parity.test.ts\ncli/test/provider_recovery_agent.test.ts\ncli/test/startup_trust_prompt.test.ts\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":123551660}},"started_at_ms":1793258093026,"completed_at_ms":1793258093154}}
