nswers, and private digests in custody; qualification remains stopped until the complete successor corpus has independent custody acceptance.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-29T06:02:22Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Metadata-only custody ownership reconciliation (2026-10-29): the claims log records `CUSTODY_HANDOFF_ACCEPTED` at 02:21:25Z from former custodian `opencode` (`available=yes`, next claim `CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION`, actor SageBridge). At 04:15:36Z SageBridge recorded `coordination_only`; the current `CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION/owner.json` still names `opencode`. Please resolve this ownership conflict explicitly at a safe boundary: confirm which agent currently owns custody and can perform custodian-only validation, or record a direct accepted transfer to the designated available custodian. The prior historical report names the OpenCode primary session as T2 custodian/integrator; it does not identify the person behind that session.\\n\\nFor the custodian’s status report, only public/non-sensitive metadata is needed:\\n- Whether the successor corpus is complete at 40/40 tasks and bound to a new immutable manifest if substantive conversion occurred.\\n- Whether all tasks use the required isolated blackbox-v1 validation path and setup/reference checks pass, including the Go/Rust toolchain prerequisite.\\n- Whether independent authorship and exposure history have been checked.\\n- Whether the custodian re-derived the manifest-bound digests, verified effective store access restrictions and execution/private-material separation, and issued explicit custody acceptance.\\n- The exact public manifest identity and next checkpoint.\\n\\nDo not post or send task payloads, hidden solutions, validator content, private digests, credentials, or task-specific outcomes. Qualification remains stopped until complete custody acceptance is recorded; T3’s reported 8/8 metadata checks do not establish corpus task-quality acceptance.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-29T06:54:11Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Metadata-only handoff follow-up: the operator identified SageBridge as the contact for custodian-only T2/T3 validation. Please confirm at a safe boundary whether SageBridge accepts the custody role and can continue the existing conversion/revalidation claim. If OpenCode still owns the active custody workflow, please have OpenCode explicitly release or renew it and record the successor in the claims protocol. Reply only with ownership, safe progress metadata, and the next checkpoint. Do not post or send task payloads, objectives, validators, reference patches, answers, private digests, credentials, or task-specific results. Qualification remains stopped until the full successor corpus has independent custody acceptance.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-29T07:12:13Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Metadata-only clarification for the custody handoff: the public T2 and T3 custody reports identify the former custodian as the `opencode` primary session (integrator/custodian, not task author); they do not identify a human operator. The handoff log later names SageBridge, but the subsequent `coordination_only` status and current claim file leave the active custodian unclear.\\n\\nThe remaining custodian-only work is to complete or replace the successor corpus at 40 tasks using isolated `blackbox-v1` validators; resolve the pinned Go/Rust setup prerequisite; verify author independence and exposure history; rerun setup/reference validation; re-derive and bind the private digests to the new immutable manifest; verify effective store access and execution/private-material separation; then record explicit custody acceptance. This is custody validation, not qualification. Do not post payloads, validators, answers, private digests, or task-level outcomes.\\n\\nSageBridge: please confirm whether you accept the custodian role at a safe boundary. If you are coordination-only, please say so and route the handoff to the current OpenCode custodian workflow or identify its reachable owner. Qualification remains stopped until acceptance is recorded.\\n\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"RESULT 2\n--- .git/nexus-claims/CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION/owner.json\n{\"agent\":\"opencode\",\"role\":\"held-out corpus custodian (handoff accepted per claims.log CUSTODY_HANDOFF_ACCEPTED)\",\"branch\":null,\"worktree\":null,\"bound_manifest\":\"50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b\",\"since\":\"2026-10-29T02:24:10Z\",\"pid\":3848937,\"corpus_access\":\"custodian workflow only\",\"progress\":{\"successor_store\":\"/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2-blackbox1\",\"tasks_built\":20,\"cases\":218,\"go_rust_blocked\":\"oracle sandbox exposes no Go/Rust toolchain; disposition recorded\",\"t3_acceptance\":\"PASS 8/8 digests+schema+isolation vs 85fb9caf\",\"revalidation\":\"batch waiting on SUITE (held by codex-root)\"}}\n5774:2026-10-29T02:55:00Z ACTIVE_LANES_REFRESH SUITE owner=codex-root process=make_test_live snapshot=03bfaa394c906d900574f35104e521844049403c no_result_inferred CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION owner=opencode SageBridge process=3860455_live protected_store_unread no_qualification_started; dirty_shared_main_checkout_preserved untouched\n5779:2026-10-29T02:59:04Z CUSTODY_PROGRESS opencode CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION successor_store=built(20 tasks,218 cases; js+py convertible; go+rust blocked: oracle sandbox binds no Go/Rust toolchain - /usr/local/go and ~/.cargo are outside SYSTEM_BINARIES; disposition to be published metadata-only) t3_acceptance=PASS(8/8 digests, schema, isolation vs 85fb9caf) revalidation=batch_waiting_on_SUITE original_v2_store=untouched_read_only qualification=stopped by=opencode\n5781:2026-10-29T02:59:52Z CUSTODY_STATUS_RELAY active=opencode T3=PASS_8of8 T2_successor=partial_20_tasks_218_cases_JS_Python Go_Rust_bl