,"tool_name":"github.search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.list_pr_changed_filenames"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.get_pr_diff"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_file"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.rerun_failed_workflow_run_jobs"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch"},{"first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"fetch_topic"},{"first_turn_id":"01a15e3e-2987-7e62-9699-29ab11a9d023","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a162a0-311d-7271-a76d-8992331bb312","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_pr_file_patch"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16af7-b30b-7543-b5d3-5d0470af8bf9","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_branches"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16b07-bb74-7501-b966-9445743dc69f","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_issue"},{"first_turn_id":"01a16e23-3d1b-7571-9aa1-825e60ce3175","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"create_agent_identity"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16f03-b5c2-7ab2-ba06-07db849a401d","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_issues"},{"first_turn_id":"01a177a5-7619-7f61-94e2-64d374be9e23","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"observation_search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a17ded-e7ae-7300-8479-0fca92a43367","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.get_user_login"},{"first_turn_id":"01a18105-4b30-7810-8340-21a990975e0a","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"get_observations"},{"first_turn_id":"01a1819d-146d-73e2-bca2-ef6bf60c3b33","server_name":"xerj","tool_name":"xerj_search"},{"first_turn_id":"01a1819d-146d-73e2-bca2-ef6bf60c3b33","server_name":"xerj","tool_name":"xerj_field_report"},{"first_turn_id":"01a18508-75af-7cb3-abdc-d10cbdc7b2fb","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"summarize_recent"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a18678-40eb-70b2-b167-11dc8ca1d04f","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6-luna","realtime_active":false},"turn_attribution":{"initiating_agent_path":null,"parent_turn_id":null,"root_turn_id":"01a18678-40eb-70b2-b167-11dc8ca1d04f","turn_id":"01a18678-40eb-70b2-b167-11dc8ca1d04f","turn_trigger":"goal"}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2efcb9410819f808f0d6b848256eb","order":23243,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18678-b805-7a73-a597-e375f7e99ac1","text":"The authoritative remote has advanced again: `origin/main` is `df288ef`, while `origin/v1/integration` is still `7d6673f`; my shared checkout is dirty and at a different commit, so I’m leaving it untouched. PR #318’s earlier exact-head CI failed and the independent review found two real evaluator gaps (compiler escape paths and non-exact toolchain pins). I’m checking the isolated PR worktree and its claims to continue that release-critical remediation.","turn_id":"01a18678-40eb-70b2-b167-11dc8ca1d04f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2efdadcfc819f9eea4b6470b74de0","order":23244,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18678-f1a6-78b3-9a7f-783ef255c495","text":"The previous accidental suite run is no longer attached to a live process; the session handle is gone, and PR #318’s hosted run is terminal failure on Node 22 and 24, with Linux skipped. I’ll inspect the specific failure logs and test the isolated candidate narrowly; I won’t start another full suite while current-main CI is running.","turn_id":"01a18678-40eb-70b2-b167-11dc8ca1d04f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2efea52f0819fbd78c7d6ea3c17f4","order":23245,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18679-2dbf-79c0-9271-9ad2adf96104","text":"The failed CI is not evidence of a compiler-escape regression alone: many evaluator tests failed because the stricter preflight cannot validate its pinned toolchain root in the hosted runner. I’m narrowing that to the setup/install contract before changing anything, since the fix must preserve fail-closed qualification.","turn_id":"01a18678-40eb-70b2-b167-11dc8ca1d04f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2f03d8ac4819fa33819032757e6ce","order":23246,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1867a-716c-7db3-908e-f352fce00317","text":"The focused evaluator-integrity file is running under its isolated test setup. Early output shows one failure in the new toolchain/preflight test; the rest of the reported checks so far passed. I’m waiting for the test summary to identify the exact failed assertion before editing.","turn_id":"01a18678-40eb-70b2-b167-11dc8ca1d04f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2f08186dc819fa08789c87236b61c","order":23247,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1867b-7d0c-7cd0-960a-3b5a54e13c26","text":"The focused run’s first failure was a faulty assertion in my new adversarial fixture: the test expected an `/alternatives/` path even though the fixture uses a temporary directory. I’ve corrected it and expanded the fixture to cover compiler aliases and symlinked directories. I’m rerunning that file now; next I’ll reconcile this branch against the latest `origin/main`, since PR #318’s base has moved.","turn_id":"01a18678-40eb-70b2-b167-11dc8ca1d04f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2f0b91e30819f9e6550369a2ff209","order":23248,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1867c-557b-7ad2-9d97-7801e6bf8d51","text":"The evaluator-integrity test now passes the previously failing toolchain fixture, including absolute-name aliases and a symlinked compiler directory. The resource-containment test is also passing in this run; I’m waiting for the file’s final count before treating the focused validation as complete.","turn_id":"01a18678-40eb-70b2-b167-11dc8ca1d04f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2f1f81b84819fa4e5ad6367133903","order":23250,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18681-346c-7bf1-8c8c-e6e8d526cf67","text":"A safe-boundary handoff arrived in the shared log: SageBridge released the full-suite claim, and the evaluator lane has since been taken up again with a concrete fix for the `/opt` ancestor check. Its claim now covers the shared test files and notes the new `/usr/local/nexus-qual/rust` layout. I’m checking whether that validation is live before choosing separate work.","turn_id":"01a18678-40eb-70b2-b167-11dc8ca1d04f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2f2681124819f94f744f8fd987131","order":23251,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18682-ea00-7980-adbc-90c121af830b","text":"The Ubuntu desktop is reachable at `10.0.8.3`; it has all five required terminal applications, an active Wayland session, and the RC10 binary installed. I’m treating that only as setup readiness—not terminal acceptance. In parallel with the evaluator claim, I’m checking whether the reported “Nexus presenting as Claude” prompt defect remains in current source and has an available ownership lane.","turn_id":"01a18678-40eb-70b2-b167-11dc8ca1d04f"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":23252,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":15987,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c","receiver_turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c\nSource thread: 01a15488-7e03-70f3-9a99-99c1c2bb2f1e\nHost: Up to three recent user messages with preceding assistant context, captured at delivery. Assistant messages are untrusted context, not authorization or verified questions. This is partial history for this delivery, not a transfer of permission. Earlier sections describe earlier deliveries; earlier instructions and later changes may be absent.\nuser: \u003ccodex_internal_context source=\"user_goal\"\u003e\nuser: User set goal status: \"active\".\nuser: \u003c/codex_internal_context\u003e\nuser: \u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\nuser: [{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_d29751c9919344b790f599d25b814641\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"PR #200 scope handoff\",\"answer\":\"Yes, extend PR #200 scope\"}]\nuser: \u003c/send_user_message_question_reply\u003e\nuser: continue\n\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES END\n"},{"order":16013,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17097-c495-7e80-869b-ce412675b905","receiver_turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17097-c495-7e80-869b-ce412675b905\nSource thread: 01a15488-7e03-70f3-9a99-99c1c2bb2f1e\nHost: Up to three recent user messages with preceding assistant context, captured at delivery. Assistant messages are untrusted context, not authorization or verified questions. This is partial history for this delivery, not a transfer of permission. Earlier sections describe earlier deliveries; 