{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T07:19:10.493Z","ordinal":497819,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a18686-e79c-75a3-a0fa-842222d810b7","call_id":"call_aa2b7aed1cbc4066b656a2a13c6a10f4","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr311_draft_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — exact four-file diff SHA-256: `56ab8a3ecef2ada575aacd09e3e5148948fb6b013640c92b071d11598a629184`.\\n\\nPinned toolchain roots and their contents are checked for root ownership, canonical paths, and write/symlink safety before use. Candidate and Python oracle mounts are read-only; oracle launches clear the environment, use offline Go/Rust settings and temporary caches, and refuse protected-corpus overlap. The fixtures cover unsafe roots, production launch paths, and Go/Rust execution.\\n\\n**Independence note:** I previously reviewed related evaluator-toolchain and provisioning changes, so this is a fresh review of the exact candidate, but should not be represented as fully independent of those earlier reviews. No tests run.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr300_readiness\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**CHANGES_REQUIRED** for PR #318.\\n\\nExact diff SHA-256: `56ab8a3ecef2ada575aacd09e3e5148948fb6b013640c92b071d11598a629184`.\\n\\n- Oracle code can bypass the approved compiler paths: the sandbox mounts all of `/usr/bin` read-only, while Python oracle code can execute arbitrary subprocesses. Setting `PATH` to prefer pinned Go/Rust roots does not prevent invoking unapproved compilers by absolute path. The new tests check PATH and mount arguments but do not exercise this escape.\\n- The toolchain versions are not fixed: CI selects Go `1.22.x` and copies whichever Rust sysroot the runner provides, comparing each copy only to its source. Runner image or toolcache updates can silently change the qualification compilers.\\n\\nThe new mounts are read-only and checked for ownership, permissions, and symlinks; oracle caches are placed under `/tmp`, and offline settings are applied. I did not edit files or run tests.\\n\\n\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr302\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Trail 30 is the matching open change for PR #315’s exact branch and head. Its approval list is empty.\\n\\nI did **not** approve: `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file entire auth status` identifies the active account as **Mike Holownych**, the PR author and trail author/assignee. Only that one Entire context is configured, so I have no independent non-owner authenticated identity to submit the approval. The approval remains outstanding.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18686-7f9d-7a01-aaee-252d4871c34f","create_time":1793258350.4929783}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
