ath. */\norigin/main:cli/src/client.ts:681:   * Checks made before a content-bearing request leaves: model and credential present (provider connections), and the\norigin/main:cli/src/client.ts:699:    // Spending limits cover provider connections, whose requests are recorded; the legacy endpoint path has no receipts.\norigin/main:cli/src/client.ts:718:  /** Records a receipt for an inference request (local endpoint or provider connection). */\norigin/main:cli/src/client.ts:970:    // A provider connection is pinned to its own endpoint: task content never fails over elsewhere (PRV-13).\norigin/main:cli/src/client.ts:993:    // A provider connection uses only its own key: never the appliance's stored token or any other credential.\norigin/main:cli/src/client.ts:1130:   * another provider: capability discovery is scoped to the connection in use). Not content-bearing.\norigin/main:cli/src/client.ts:1155:        // Only for a plain endpoint: cloud provider connections have no such endpoints.\norigin/main:cli/src/client.ts:1222:    if (this.conn.providerId || this.conn.protocol !== \"openai-chat\") throw new TokenCountError(\"unsupported\", \"provider connections have no request-counting endpoint\");\norigin/main:cli/src/config.ts:280:/** Base URL of a provider connection: the operator's override (flag or NEXUS_<ID>_BASE_URL), else the provider default. */\norigin/main:cli/src/config.ts:290: * The provider's own key — its variable, Nexus's credential store, or a connection registered in another client —\norigin/main:cli/src/config.ts:401:  if (provider && options.fallback) warnOnce(`--fallback is ignored for provider '${provider}': a provider connection is pinned to its own endpoint.`);\norigin/main:cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts:478:  // Same role binding as the agent: own provider, else own endpoint, else the main connection.\norigin/main:cli/src/credentials.ts:363: * The credential a provider connection uses: its environment variable, else Nexus's store, else a connection\norigin/main:cli/src/credentials.ts:366:/** The API key a provider connection uses (env, Nexus store, or another client); undefined for sign-in providers. */\norigin/main:cli/src/doctor.ts:490:    out.push(f(\"endpoint.authenticated\", \"endpoint\", \"fail\", `The endpoint rejected the credential Nexus sends (HTTP ${status}).`, [where], config.provider ? `Reconnect with \\`nexus connect ${config.provider}\\` (or ctrl+p in /model).` : \"Set LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY (or pass -k) to a credential this gateway accepts.\"));\norigin/main:cli/src/doctor.ts:926:    return f(\"credentials.store\", \"state\", \"fail\", \"Nexus's credential store is not valid JSON; stored provider connections are unavailable.\", [file], \"Move the file aside and reconnect with `nexus connect <provider>`.\");\norigin/main:cli/src/model_catalog.ts:2: * What the model picker shows: the appliance and every cloud provider, whether and how each is connected, the models\norigin/main:cli/src/model_catalog.ts:12:import { originOf, PROVIDERS, providerDefinition, type ConnectMethod } from \"./providers.js\";\norigin/main:cli/src/model_catalog.ts:146:export function connectionOf(providerId: string): { connected: boolean; source?: string; external?: boolean } {\norigin/main:cli/src/model_catalog.ts:150:    try { providerBaseUrl(\"compatible\"); } catch { return { connected: false }; }\norigin/main:cli/src/model_catalog.ts:155:  if (providerId === \"compatible\" && operatorSetting(\"NEXUS_COMPATIBLE_AUTH\") === \"none\") return { connected: true, source: \"declared key-less (NEXUS_COMPATIBLE_AUTH=none)\" };\norigin/main:cli/src/protocol.ts:153:  /** Answer to models.list: providers (with connection source, never a credential), models, current and recent. */\norigin/main:cli/src/protocol.ts:157:  /** Outcome of provider.connect / provider.disconnect. */\norigin/main:cli/src/protocol.ts:176:  | { type: \"provider.connect\"; id: string; provider: string; method: string; key?: string; endpoint?: string }\norigin