{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T07:30:58.796Z","ordinal":498352,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18691-b66b-7221-bfe3-771037193ea1","author":"/root/review_pr302","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_pr302\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — PR #318 at `f43f4e5e48947370fc03e1d0ac44a51ecd310849`, against `df288ef010a93c418e4972d3d40dc293ec9c0081`. Cumulative diff SHA-256: `008ca7e8db831b41083c4456db7afe55e043f9e8adbc0399f56cfd1fbf671cfb`. The committed tree matches the previously inspected `9ab0ab47…` snapshot.\n\n- **P1 — Unpinned compilers remain accessible to candidate code.** [eval/isolate.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:498) mounts system directories, including `/usr/bin`, into the candidate sandbox; line 502 adds pinned toolchains but does not hide other compilers. Candidate commands retain `/usr/bin:/bin` in `PATH` ([eval/run.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/run.mjs:474)). A task can therefore invoke `/usr/bin/rustc` or `/usr/bin/go` directly and bypass the pinned-toolchain PATH. The unpinned-compiler preflight is applied to oracle execution ([eval/isolate.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:532)), but not the candidate sandbox. Extend the preflight or sandbox mounts to cover candidate execution, and add an adversarial test that tries absolute compiler paths from the actual candidate process.\n\nI reviewed source and tests only; I ran no tests. The reported focused `eval_integrity` pass is owner-reported evidence, not an independent test result."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18686-7f9d-7a01-aaee-252d4871c34f","create_time":1793259058.795859,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":23281}}
