{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T11:37:50.963Z","ordinal":498845,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18773-ba73-7fe2-b0ba-43a015143a89","author":"/root/review_pr302","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_pr302\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — PR #318 head `493bffde3c961c36631d644f0e25dca834702712`, base `df288ef010a93c418e4972d3d40dc293ec9c0081`. Cumulative diff SHA-256: `5664180286129a192258ce2e18816107a6d6b6285aedda1decd1c4866bd98619`.\n\nThe P1 is resolved: [isolate.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:491) checks compiler exposure across the system directories and alternatives the candidate sandbox will mount, before it launches candidate code. The regression test attempts absolute `/usr/bin/go`, `rustc`, and `cargo` from the candidate process and requires each to be unavailable or match the pinned version ([eval_integrity.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:1376)).\n\nSkipping symlinked directory entries does not bypass the mounted-path scan: each mounted root is scanned independently, while file symlinks remain checked. Scan errors other than missing paths fail closed ([isolate.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:129)).\n\nRead-only source review; I ran no tests."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","create_time":1793273870.9635324,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":23291}}
