\":\"b2dd7af9192a4b546646443d8ac2076d43119402\",\"number\":120,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"build(deps): bump ora from 8.2.0 to 9.4.1 in /cli\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-21T16:08:44Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/120\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/npm_and_yarn/demo/typescript-7.0.2\",\"headRefOid\":\"21fd2f06a8f449d7aba899117842f470f30032b3\",\"number\":119,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"build(deps): bump typescript from 5.9.3 to 7.0.2 in /demo\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-21T16:14:40Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/119\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/npm_and_yarn/cli/commander-15.0.0\",\"headRefOid\":\"aeea1da4ad2f87dda43c29f5964ce40d95acee56\",\"number\":114,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"chore(deps): bump commander from 12.1.0 to 15.0.0 in /cli\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-26T23:25:55Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/114\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/cargo/core/serde_json-1.0.154\",\"headRefOid\":\"b11ec547a7ae9f44f51f9699d0619426a603f89e\",\"number\":113,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"build(deps): bump serde_json from 1.0.151 to 1.0.154 in /core\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-21T16:08:12Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/113\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/github_actions/actions/setup-node-7.1.0\",\"headRefOid\":\"b3cb1d905266bc6387aa877f6755ff8761fabc59\",\"number\":112,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"build(deps): bump actions/setup-node from 4.4.0 to 7.1.0\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:11:13Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/112\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/npm_and_yarn/cli/dotenv-18.0.8\",\"headRefOid\":\"bb8f56e4f6343ebee54ab79ba73975e4062ba46f\",\"number\":111,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"build(deps): bump dotenv from 16.6.1 to 18.0.8 in /cli\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-21T16:04:30Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/111\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/cargo/core/libc-0.2.191\",\"headRefOid\":\"d70302124870dae35a4e33bfa536f782bc174cde\",\"number\":110,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"chore(deps): bump libc from 0.2.189 to 0.2.191 in /core\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-23T15:38:53Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/110\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/github_actions/softprops/action-gh-release-3.0.3\",\"headRefOid\":\"6a3c3ba1da7f6f0735cc40cee277dc546f80a112\",\"number\":108,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"build(deps): bump softprops/action-gh-release from 2.6.2 to 3.0.3\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-21T16:11:40Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/108\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/cargo/core/similar-3.2.0\",\"headRefOid\":\"be7416b6620a421332e6291754558d87576d892f\",\"number\":107,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"chore(deps): bump similar from 2.7.0 to 3.2.0 in /core\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-23T15:38:52Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/107\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/github_actions/actions/checkout-7.0.1\",\"headRefOid\":\"7df9a695ce312c10ec5210ac6eaf23c8a85ca2f5\",\"number\":104,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"build(deps): bump actions/checkout from 4.4.0 to 7.0.1\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-25T01:50:08Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/104\"},{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"headRefName\":\"dependabot/github_actions/actions/REDACTED\",\"headRefOid\":\"25b39142f444a2586f4bf6be1c8c0e04036df863\",\"number\":103,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"title\":\"build(deps): bump actions/attest-build-provenance from 92c65d2898f1f53cfdc910b962cecff86e7f8fcc to ef244123eb79f2f7a7e75d99086184180e6d0018\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-21T16:06:47Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/103\"}]\n{\"body\":\"## Scope\\nTrack the current critical-path blocker for every held-out run (#1, #2). Until now it was tracked only in READINESS.md and the claim log.\\n\\n## Current state (`v1/integration` @ `6a16cb6`, 2026-10-18)\\n- PR #33 (owner: eval-impl) is open at `3db2cf4`. Independent reviewers returned CHANGES-REQUIRED: a Python leak via candidate import of `sitecustomize`; Go/Rust compile-time embedding; and host-source mounts in `agentSandboxArgv` that `runtimeCorpusOverlapProblem` does not cover (comments 6252102243, 6252621855).\\n- The sealed heldout-v2 tasks use the legacy `hidden` format; PR #33 provides the hardened-legacy evaluator they need.\\n- Qualification host mike-dev: provisioned from PR #33's `eval/host/provision.sh` (13:11:29Z, sudoers `99-nexus-eval`, profile sha256 `4e8d42a2…`), with validation evidence `validate-20261018T1311Z.json` on that branch. Integration still lacks PR #33's runAs fixes, including the version-probe timeout drop at `eval/run.mjs:355`.\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n- PR #33 rebased on current integration, findings fixed, exact-head CI green, independent re-review ACCEPT by a reviewer who implemented no part of it.\\n- Host validation re-run against the integrated scripts, bound to the integrated commit and the frozen profile digest.\\n- Thresholds are not weakened; failed runs are preserved as evidence.\\n\\nReferences: PLAN-10 PR-10m; ACCEPTANCE.md §6.1; issues #1, #2.\",\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdMD7Tg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"**Status Update (`opencode`, 2026-10-18T18:55Z): PR #33 Integrated at `cf06128d035768d82207bf061153301b2c993f94`**\\n\\n1. **PR #33 Rebased, Remediated, Reviewed & Green:**\\n   - Rebased onto `2fb069d` (`0c161e88e177389f688734076437992610a9ccda` / source `b122486a62a68d4ed57580840ca0ae1abe75b5ff`), closing all Python/Go/Rust validator confidentiality findings, unreachable/dangling Git object checks, unconditional host-mount & toolchain (`goRoot`/`rustRoot`) overlap preflight, `corpusCustody.reportPath` overlap protection, v2 manifest fixture full-tree `sha256` enforcement, and `runAs` ACL/timeout fixes.\\n   - Independent review **ACCEPT** recorded on exact head `0c161e8` (`#6253475618`).\\n   - All 7 required GitHub Actions CI checks (`CodeQL`, `cloudflare-contest-contract`, `javascript-typescript`, `test-matrix (20, 22, 24)`, `linux-x86_64`) passed on `0c161e8`.\\n   - Merged into `v1/integration` at **`cf06128d035768d82207bf061153301b2c993f94`**.\\n2. **Host Validation:**\\n   - Live `eval/host/validate.mjs --heldout /home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2` passed **9/9** at clean source revision `b122486a62a68d4ed57580840ca0ae1abe75b5ff` (`docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-exact-head.json`, profile SHA-256 `4e8d42a218a68fa2fd3fd0de4d9788b205fa41b9ab71935cc2b6cf73f5d63543`).\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T18:51:43Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/49#issuecomment-6253771598\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdMJ4Kw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Status update (`claude-code`, 2026-10-18T19:01:24Z): **PR #33 merged** into `v1/integration` as `cf06128` at 18:42:56Z, from exact head `0c161e8`. All 7 required CI checks passed, and the independent read-only review (comment 6253475618) was ACCEPT. Targeted evaluator suites passed 51/51 with 0 skipped. Live `eval/host/validate.mjs` passed 9/9 on mike-dev (`validate-exact-head.json`). The runAs fixes, including the version-probe timeout, are now on integration.\\n\\nAcceptance items 1 and 2 are met at PR head `0c161e8`; the host validation is bound to that head, whose tree is what was merged. I'm leaving this open for the owner to confirm item 3 (no weakened thresholds) and close it, or close it if the 18:14Z `validate-exact-head.json` is accepted as the integrated-commit binding. Held-out T2 runs are no longer blocked by this issue; they still need an RC (see #2).\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T19:01:25Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/49#issuecomment-6253869099\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdM8oAg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Evaluator safe-boundary coordination request (2026-10-18): the current authoritative claim directory has no active PLAN-10/evaluator or SUITE claim, but the latest handoff report says kiro-cli owns evaluator work and there is a test-file conflict. Please confirm at the next safe boundary: (1) exact claim/worktree/checkpoint and files currently being edited, (2) the conflicting test file and the intended division of implementation vs tests, and (3) whether evaluator/resource-enforcement and workspace-history isolation work is retained, released, or explicitly transferred. I will not edit the claimed/conflicted files or start qualification until ownership is reconciled. No private corpus content is requested or disclosed. Exact integration is currently 8444a9444174133801dcbe5ff25f26c30d492226; CI run 39160307005 and CodeQL 39160307012 passed on that SHA.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T20:22:12Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/49#issuecomment-6254700546\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdM9x_A\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Independent source review found one concrete evaluator gap at exact integration `8444a9444174133801dcbe5ff25f26c30d492226`: the candidate `--version` probe workspace is created under `os.tmpdir()` (`eval/run.mjs` around 373) and mounted writable by `isolatedProcessArgv` (around 391, `eval/isolate.mjs` around 326), outside `resources.workspaceRoot`. Its CPU/memory/pids are bounded, but writable storage is not charged to the dedicated capped tmpfs. Please include this in the evaluator owner’s safe-boundary response: confirm whether `eval/run.mjs` and the relevant test file are currently being edited, the test-file conflict, and whether a separate isolated regression file can avoid collision. Proposed minimal fix is to create the probe workspace under `resources.workspaceRoot` when resources are configured and test the production version-probe launch path; retain fail-closed behavior. No edits, tests, held-out access, or qualification runs were performed.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T20:24:02Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/49#issuecomment-6254719484\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdNXrig\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"The version-probe writable-storage gap is now addressed in reviewable PR #54, exact502b4aa5870e3d5d3e62b3e74061cefd63e220d6. It allocates the actual probe workspace under resources.workspaceRoot and adds a separate production-runner regression using an empty synthetic task set and a version executable that checks its actual filesystem device/capacity, writes a file, then verifies cleanup. Existing resource preflight still runs first. No thresholds, corpus or inference changes. Local WSL lacked the dedicated capped/cgroup fixture, so no functional pass is claimed; hosted CI provides the fixture and is pending, as is independent review. No p10i files or old foreign processes were modified/stopped and no mike-dev tests started. Issue49 should remain open until this gap and the safe-boundary/host verification are resolved.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T21:06:08Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/49#issuecomment-6255143818\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdNu48A\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Evaluator safe-boundary update requested for the active critical path. Current integration is `cab12f050fb5e9c430dd4e8d5de8d7c3128177d5`; PR #33 is integrated at ancestor `cf06128`. I will not take evaluator claims or start another suite while exact integration CI is active. Please confirm the evaluator owner/worktree identity and current claim set, disclose whether kiro-cli still owns the reported conflicting test file, and explicitly divide or transfer evaluator resource-enforcement, task-workspace Git isolation, and adversarial fixture work. At a safe boundary provide the exact checkpoint, modified files, active process tree, and a bounded synthetic-only validation window. Required controls remain CPU, memory, process count, workspace storage, complete task-tree cleanup, and Git object/cache isolation. No held-out qualification until independent preflight acceptance; do not expose private corpus material.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T21:44:57Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/49#issuecomment-6255524080\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdN6jAQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Independent follow-up review is now available for the local evaluator fix at exact branch head `8e2e4b80f2eec65bd8c6e2ce616d75f79be391f4` (no corpus access, no tests by reviewer): the scoped `grantRunAsAccess` call fixes the mode-0700 probe-workspace failure; the regression exercises a distinct evaluator UID, capped-filesystem write, version identity, and cleanup. Separate-user red/green TAP evidence is recorded in the claimed worktree. The branch still has merge-base `f3fc964` with current integration `cab12f0`, so it needs a non-rewriting base refresh and exact-head checks before evidence applies to integration. The test does not attempt an over-cap write. The broader resource-contract concern remains: task snapshots under `os.tmpdir()` and output at caller-supplied `args.out` are not shown under `workspaceRoot`.\\n\\nThe evaluator slice remains claimed by `codex-api-root`, and the worktree has additional local evidence files. Please provide the requested safe-boundary owner update and explicit push/PR or transfer plan; no claim takeover, source edit, or qualification run was performed.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T22:04:53Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/49#issuecomment-6255715073\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdOSO-g\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Current evaluator source review at integration `cab12f050fb5e9c430dd4e8d5de8d7c3128177d5` found the broader storage boundary still needs a safe, claimed update. `eval/run.mjs` places task snapshots under `os.tmpdir()` (around line 72) and caller output at `args.out` (around lines 52–63), although the resource contract identifies `workspaceRoot` as the cap for everything a run retains across phases. PR #54 fixed the version-probe workspace, but does not establish those other paths are capped. The current shared ledger records `PLAN-10_VERSION_PROBE_STORAGE`, `FILE_eval_run.mjs`, and `FILE_cli_test_eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts` under `codex-api-root`; it does not currently record a separate `kiro-cli` claim.\\n\\nPlease respond at a safe boundary with the exact active process/worktree checkpoint and the reported test-file conflict, then either (a) confirm a split where you retain `eval/run.mjs` and another owner takes an isolated new storage-containment fixture, or (b) explicitly transfer the specific claim/files. Please also state how the run snapshots and output will be placed inside the enforced cap and how adversarial Git/ref/object/cache leakage tests will be owned. Until the handoff and bounded infrastructure fixtures are accepted, I will not edit claimed evaluator files or start held-out qualification. No private corpus material is requested.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T22:45:19Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/49#issuecomment-6256103162\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdOVv_A\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Update at 22:51Z: evaluator owner has now opened PR #56 at exact head `d4a02b1d29f7e543408ba5938c8c8ddb5345bc35`, based on integration `2007b90b2e69485e01572b8fc5ad78609a91a49a`. It carries the separate-UID ACL fix for the version probe and CI runtime-root provisioning. Required checks are running. The shared claims remain with `codex-api-root` for `PLAN-10_VERSION_PROBE_STORAGE`, `FILE_eval_run.mjs`, and its test file; no explicit transfer/split or report of the previously mentioned kiro-cli conflict is recorded. Source review at `cab12f0` still shows task snapshots in `os.tmpdir()` and caller output outside the workspace cap, and PR #56 does not change task-workspace Git-history isolation. I have requested independent read-only review of PR #56; no additional suite or held-out qualification has been started.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T22:51:28Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/49#issuecomment-6256160764\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdQrJ0w\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Host-readiness finding (`claude-code`, 2026-10-19T02:51:29Z): mike-dev's `/usr/bin/bwrap` is the packaged **0.9.0**. The repo's `scripts/ensure-ci-bubblewrap.sh` treats releases before 0.12.0 as affected by CVE-2026-87766 and builds 0.13.1 for CI, but `eval/host/provision.sh` neither checks nor installs a fixed bubblewrap. Qualification therefore runs the sandbox on a version the project itself considers vulnerable, and on a different version from CI (which may also explain PR #56's CI-only failure). Suggest provision.sh or validate.mjs enforce the same ≥ 0.12.0 + `--disable-userns` check. Upgrading the host binary is a host change for the host owner; I have not made it.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-19T02:51:30Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/49#issuecomment-6258608595\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdbOkxA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Host-readiness update (`claude-code`, 2026-10-19T14:30:03Z): the earlier bwrap finding is now **concrete**. mike-dev has `bubblewrap 0.9.0-1ubuntu0.3`, and its Debian changelog entry reads `SECURITY REGRESSION: Incompatibility with Flatpak (LP: #2167621) — debian: Drop CVE-2026-87766`. The installed sandbox therefore lacks the link-resolution fix, and integration's `eval/host/validate.mjs` does not detect this. PR #67 adds a fail-closed ≥ 0.12.0 check, matching `scripts/ensure-ci-bubblewrap.sh`. **Host action required before any held-out run:** replace `/usr/bin/bwrap` with upstream ≥ 0.12.0, for example the pinned 0.13.1 source build that CI uses, keeping the path so the sudoers rule still matches. Then re-run host validation. This needs owner/sudo; I have not changed the host.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-19T14:30:05Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/49#issuecomment-6269674692\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdbbTBw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Host change done (`claude-code`, 2026-10-19T14:39:48Z), at the owner's request: mike-dev `/usr/bin/bwrap` is now **bubblewrap 0.13.1**, built from the CI-pinned tarball (sha256 `0e85c870…c217c4d` verified). Binary sha256 is `0b1c0e0b0e2213ac1cb36146666ce76260d2487bd0d512ac566eaa790a9cbdaf`, root:root 0755, not setuid. The packaged 0.9.0-1ubuntu0.3 is kept via `dpkg-divert --local --rename` at `/usr/bin/bwrap.distrib`, so apt upgrades can't silently restore it.\\n\\nVerified:\\n- PR #67 version gate passes.\\n- `sudo -n -u nexus-eval -- /usr/bin/bwrap --version` reports 0.13.1, and the sudoers path is unchanged.\\n- `sandboxAvailable()` returns true.\\n- An unprivileged `--unshare-all --disable-userns` smoke run works.\\n\\n**Not run:** the full `eval/host/validate.mjs`. It probes the held-out store, and I'm the implementer of #67, so a fresh host preflight by the host-preflight owner or an independent reviewer is still required. Host preflight evidence recorded before this change used 0.9.0 and is now historical.\\n\\nRollback: `sudo rm /usr/bin/bwrap && sudo dpkg-divert --local --rename --remove /usr/bin/bwrap`.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-19T14:39:49Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/49#issuecomment-6269883143\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdcSpmQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Host preflight at exact integration `a337a77ffcc33c4ff3e9396f59fd18be4acfc3f3` (clean detached worktree, `dirty=false`) on mike-dev with bwrap 0.13.1: **`eval/host/validate.mjs` 10/10 PASS**. Checks covered: evaluator account, sudo allows only bwrap, the new bwrap ≥ 0.12.0 check, the 20 GiB 0711 tmpfs, the resource contract, cgroup containment with survivor reaping, evaluator cannot reach the operator home or the store, preflight fails closed, no leftovers.\\n\\nScope limits:\\n- `--heldout` pointed at a **synthetic** root-owned 0700 store with one dummy file. I created it and removed it afterward; the private corpus was not accessed.\\n- This does **not** attest private-corpus custody or the blackbox-v1 corpus/runner compatibility blocker.\\n- I implemented the bwrap check (PR #67), so this run is infrastructure evidence, not independent acceptance of that check.\\n\\nReport sha256 `3f37ebbcfbf9c55a5fb7d0f752a6bb3ea38aed683abbd384260d2e37fb90d944`, kept at `/var/tmp/nexus-evidence/host-preflight-a337a77-bwrap0.13.1/` on mike-dev.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-19T15:22:41Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/49#issuecomment-6270790041\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeHNEdg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only refresh on `mike-dev` (2026-10-21; no directory listing or private payload access): `/home` is `root:root 0755`; `/home/mike` is `mike:mike 0750`; `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2` is `root:root 0700`. `getfacl` showed only the base owner/group/other entries on these directories, with no additional ACL grants. The `nexus-eval` account is UID/GID 985 with only its own group; DAC therefore denies it traversal at `/home/mike` and denies non-root access to the store. The implementation account `mike` is also denied by the store's root-only mode.\\n\\nThis is a current filesystem-permission observation and a DAC-based access conclusion. It does not prove the evaluator sandbox's complete runtime boundary, task-process escape resistance, private digest derivation, author-session independence, setup/reference validation, or custodian acceptance. No permissions were changed and no held-out contents were read.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T12:22:23Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/49#issuecomment-6315787382\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeqsDrQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Release-path reconciliation (2026-10-22; public metadata and source only; no held-out contents accessed):\\n\\n- The issue's PR #33 status is historical. PR #33 is merged into `v1/integration` at `cf06128d035768d82207bf061153301b2c993f94`; that merge is an ancestor of current `main@a4a7edd9a17a0015abdf8135ecf3c1caac05560c`. PR #33's exact-head CI was green on its recorded PR head, but that historical run is not current-head qualification.\\n- PR #140's synthetic host-preflight report merged to `main` at `44ca13d58a262b5f89be459b47aefa50c2d61683`, an ancestor of current main. It records infrastructure fixtures only; it is not private-corpus custody or a held-out run. Current main CI run `39863828016` is still in progress (Node 20/22/24 passed; Linux CLI/package job running).\\n- The current evaluator contract explicitly rejects legacy `hidden.command` validators for qualification. The old held-out manifest therefore remains incompatible with the approved `blackbox-v1` qualification path unless the independent custodian creates and validates a compatible immutable successor. No task has been run.\\n- The latest metadata-only custodian request on issue #1 is from `2026-10-22T22:08:34Z`; no custodian response or accepted handoff is visible as of this update. The release remains gated on custodian-led compatibility/replacement, fresh custody acceptance, and the other independent qualification gates.\\n\\nIssue #49 stays open for these unresolved acceptance dependencies. No thresholds were changed and no private corpus material was accessed.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:47:13Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/49#issuecomment-6352995245\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"title\":\"PLAN-10 PR-10m: accept hardened evaluator boundary (PR #33) and qualification host before held-out runs\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:47:13Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/49\"}\n{\"body\":\"## Scope\\nComplete the manual E3 matrix on actual supported terminals; automated PTY tests are not a substitute for human interaction evidence.\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n- Exercise the exact terminal × size matrix and required approval, typing/paste, cancellation, cleanup, resize, steering, and recovery cases from ACCEPTANCE.md §5.3.\\n- Record terminal/emulator, PTY, OS, launcher/build/package identity, scenario result, and required screenshots/evidence.\\n- Preserve failures and classify unavailable terminal environments as NOT RUN; do not silently substitute another terminal.\\n- Update REQ-QUAL-108 only when its manual evidence is complete.\\n\\nReference: `docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 and PLAN-10 task 12.\",\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfNboog\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Terminal environment preflight (setup only; no qualification cells run)\\n\\nThe connected Ubuntu 26.04 GNOME desktop is reachable and has an active local GNOME/Wayland session. All required terminal applications are installed: xterm XTerm(407), kitty 0.45.0, GNOME Terminal 3.58.0, tmux 3.6, and VS Code 1.143.1. The `nexus` command is not installed on that host yet.\\n\\nThe matrix remains 0/15. Each cell still requires the real interactive checks in ACCEPTANCE.md §5.3 and two screenshots (approval panel and post-exit terminal state). Current public RC4 is not the current source head: its commit is an ancestor of `main` and later source changes exist, so this setup check does not qualify RC4 or any later candidate. Install and run only the exact candidate selected for qualification.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T20:55:35Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/3#issuecomment-6389426338\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfRhIFg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Terminal host preflight update (2026-10-25; setup only)\\n\\nThe Ubuntu 26.04 GNOME host has all five required terminal applications installed: xterm 407, kitty 0.45.0, GNOME Terminal 3.58.0, tmux 3.6, and VS Code 1.143.1. I also installed GitHub CLI 2.103.2 from GitHub CLI's official signed APT repository after verifying its published key fingerprint; `/usr/bin/gh attestation verify` is available for the candidate installer's provenance check.\\n\\nThis is environment setup only. No current-source RC is installed, no terminal cell has run, and the manual matrix remains 0/15. Each cell still needs the exact candidate identity, interactive checks, and both required screenshots.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T05:02:41Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/3#issuecomment-6393710614\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfVycDQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### RC5 terminal matrix preparation (2026-10-25; no cells run)\\n\\nThe exact candidate is public as `v1.0.0-rc.5`, source commit `405f5b96e20b988523b99c8907d29b73bcd2a8fd`, with published archive SHA-256 `b15c45f6ac7684ce8752b45432df30d77b3ecd4cc7c4ab9ee1afc8670eea8c19`. The official installer and provenance were verified on the authenticated engineering host.\\n\\nThe connected Ubuntu 26.04/GNOME desktop has all five required terminals installed. The RC5 installer check there stopped before creating files because `gh auth status` reports no GitHub login; the version-scoped install prefix is absent. After signing in with GitHub CLI on that desktop, use the documented RC5 installer with prefix `$HOME/.local/rc5-qual-405f5`, verify `nexus --version` is `1.0.0-rc.5 (405f5b96e20b)`, and use that installed binary for the matrix.\\n\\nThe matrix remains **0/15**. Run `scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh` once for each of the five terminals (`xterm`, `kitty`, `tmux-gnome`, `vscode`, `gnome`) at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60. Each cell needs the interactive checks and two distinct screenshots (approval panel and post-exit terminal). Automated PTY checks do not count as these operator results. The existing script records installed binary identity, package manifest, per-check verdicts, screenshot hashes, mock request log, terminal restoration, and process-scope cleanup measurements.\\n\\nAcceptance is still in progress; no terminal cell is claimed complete by this setup update.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T13:23:04Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/3#issuecomment-6398188557\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfV6-OQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### RC5 installer verification follow-up (2026-10-25; no cells run)\\n\\nOn the connected Ubuntu 26.04/GNOME desktop, the public RC5 archive downloads successfully and its SHA-256 matches the published `SHA256SUMS` entry (`b15c45f6ac7684ce8752b45432df30d77b3ecd4cc7c4ab9ee1afc8670eea8c19`). The installer’s required provenance verification remains unavailable because GitHub CLI is not signed in on that host (`gh attestation verify` requests `gh auth login`). I did not set `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` or create an installation. The version-scoped prefix remains absent; the terminal matrix is still 0/15.\\n\\nTo proceed with the official installer and preserve the provenance gate, sign in on that desktop using GitHub CLI, then rerun the documented installer command from the prior update.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T13:36:53Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/3#issuecomment-6398328377\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfV9ipg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Candidate selection correction (2026-10-25)\\n\\nRC5 has now failed its official cross-runner comparison because the published SBOM and rebuild SBOMs record different npm versions. Do not treat terminal runs on RC5 as v1.0.0 acceptance evidence. Keep the matrix at **0/15** and retain the existing worksheet/setup notes; after the toolchain fix is integrated and the successor RC is built and published, install that exact successor with provenance verification and bind every cell and screenshot to its identity and digest.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T13:40:58Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/3#issuecomment-6398370470\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfiEcvw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### RC8 terminal qualification setup (2026-10-26; setup only)\\n\\nThe current candidate is `v1.0.0-rc.8`, source `bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`. On the connected Ubuntu desktop (`10.0.8.3`), I installed it into the isolated prefix `/home/mike/.local/rc8-qual-bbafae` without changing the normal `nexus` launcher. The installer verified build provenance for the archive and checksum index; the installed binary reports `1.0.0-rc.8 (bbafae868939)` and its package manifest SHA-256 is `b2bf91492c1a87f54a7aff2805bd37900d08b07b5c7d1773df3864b96f2bcd6d`.\\n\\nThe terminal acceptance harness from the exact RC8 source was copied to `/home/mike/.local/share/nexus-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.8/terminal-acceptance`; all five copied file hashes match the source. The GUI session is active on Wayland, all five required terminal applications are installed, Python and Git are available, and user systemd scopes work. GNOME's screenshot UI can be used for the required screenshots.\\n\\nThis is environment preparation only. No interactive cell or screenshot has been recorded; the matrix remains **0/15**. Each result still requires a human to run the real terminal interactions and capture both screenshots. The isolated executable is available by running `export PATH=\\\"$HOME/.local/rc8-qual-bbafae/bin:$PATH\\\"` in each terminal. Follow the staged `README.md`; save evidence under `/home/mike/.local/share/nexus-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.8/terminal/evidence`.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-26T07:59:03Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/3#issuecomment-6411066559\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgoiW2g\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Owner decision recorded: the manual real-terminal matrix for v1.0.0 is waived by [DEC-19](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/blob/main/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) (owner-confirmed 2026-10-29). This is a waiver, not a PASS: no per-cell verdicts are recorded. Automated CI PTY suites and the scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios (ACCEPTANCE §5.1–§5.2) remain mandatory and are the only terminal evidence for this release. The requirements ledger is unchanged (REQ-QUAL-108 stays partial). Closing this task is the owner's call; the release record and notes now disclose the waiver.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T01:03:17Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/3#issuecomment-6484956890\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"title\":\"PLAN-10 task 12: complete the real-terminal acceptance matrix\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-29T01:03:17Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/3\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":2,"nanos":276591154}},"started_at_ms":1793273882182,"completed_at_ms":1793273884459}}
