{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T11:38:09.650Z","ordinal":498871,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-2281ee3c-81d5-403a-8aed-547d8c25cd67","process_id":"96069","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr checks 318"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr checks 318"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"CodeQL\tpass\t2s\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/123423750800\t\ntest-matrix (22)\tpending\t0\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40866715565/job/123423206135\t\ntest-matrix (24)\tpending\t0\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40866715565/job/123423206500\t\njavascript-typescript\tpass\t1m23s\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40866715198/job/123423205191\t\nEntire Gates\tpending\t0\thttps://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/33/changes/nexus-code/33\t\nCodeRabbit\tpass\t0\t\tReview skipped\n","exit_code":8,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":873904144}},"started_at_ms":1793273888776,"completed_at_ms":1793273889650}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T11:38:09.805Z","ordinal":498872,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18774-040c-7dd0-8721-47b9ddea9a1f","call_id":"call_0e4aaf84760941a08c2cd97bf393fafc","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":0,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"85b03f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.873951893,\"exit_code\":8,\"original_token_count\":139,\"output\":\"CodeQL\\tpass\\t2s\\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/123423750800\\t\\ntest-matrix (22)\\tpending\\t0\\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40866715565/job/123423206135\\t\\ntest-matrix (24)\\tpending\\t0\\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40866715565/job/123423206500\\t\\njavascript-typescript\\tpass\\t1m23s\\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40866715198/job/123423205191\\t\\nEntire Gates\\tpending\\t0\\thttps://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/33/changes/nexus-code/33\\t\\nCodeRabbit\\tpass\\t0\\t\\tReview skipped\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":1,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"4c4fff\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.824101548,\"exit_code\":8,\"original_token_count\":139,\"output\":\"Entire Gates\\tpending\\t0\\thttps://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/38/changes/nexus-code/38\\t\\nCodeQL\\tpass\\t3s\\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/123422522863\\t\\ntest-matrix (22)\\tpending\\t0\\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40866393136/job/123422133559\\t\\njavascript-typescript\\tpass\\t1m3s\\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40866393067/job/123422133948\\t\\ntest-matrix (24)\\tpending\\t0\\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40866393136/job/123422134009\\t\\nCodeRabbit\\tpass\\t0\\t\\tReview skipped\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":2,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"31df65\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.729211169,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":842,\"output\":\"{\\\"baseRefOid\\\":\\\"df288ef010a93c418e4972d3d40dc293ec9c0081\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/38/changes/nexus-code/38\\\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\\\n\\\\n## What\\\\n\\\\nVersion-only candidate for `v1.0.0-rc.11`, cut from current `main` (post-RC10 source).\\\\n\\\\n- Root `package.json` 1.0.0-rc.10 → 1.0.0-rc.11, propagated by `scripts/sync-version.mjs` to `cli/package.json`, `cli/package-lock.json`, `core/Cargo.toml`, `core/Cargo.lock`.\\\\n- New `docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.11.md` summarising post-RC10 changes (durable operations: TDD units, operation view, git-aware isolation, context budgets/checkpoints, policy config; reliability/security fixes; refreshed release records) and stating the candidate's qualification status.\\\\n\\\\n## Why\\\\n\\\\nEvery installed-RC gate — E2/lifecycle, the required fifteen-cell manual terminal matrix, provider and held-out qualification, cross-runner reproducibility, independent acceptance — needs an artifact built from a successor tag. RC10 predates the post-RC10 fixes, so a candidate version is the prerequisite; this PR creates it and nothing more.\\\\n\\\\n**This does not tag, build, publish or qualify a release.** The tag and publication remain the owner's action. The notes explicitly leave the manual terminal matrix required (DEC-19's waiver record is withdrawn) and every installed-RC gate outstanding.\\\\n\\\\n## Verification\\\\n\\\\n- `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` → all components at 1.0.0-rc.11.\\\\n- `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` on the clean tree → source gate passes (123 rows; 12 rows deferred to exact-RC qualification).\\\\n- `git diff --check` clean; diff is five version files plus the release note.\\\\n\\\",\\\"headRefOid\\\":\\\"e13da84ff320ca85fb0efacdd6b3f5a5299287fd\\\",\\\"mergeStateStatus\\\":\\\"BLOCKED\\\",\\\"number\\\":323,\\\"reviews\\\":[],\\\"state\\\":\\\"OPEN\\\",\\\"statusCheckRollup\\\":[{\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"CheckRun\\\",\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"detailsUrl\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40866393136/job/123422133559\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"test-matrix (22)\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T11:34:15Z\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"IN_PROGRESS\\\",\\\"workflowName\\\":\\\"CI\\\"},{\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"CheckRun\\\",\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T11:35:18Z\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"SUCCESS\\\",\\\"detailsUrl\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40866393067/job/123422133948\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"javascript-typescript\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T11:34:15Z\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"COMPLETED\\\",\\\"workflowName\\\":\\\"CodeQL\\\"},{\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"CheckRun\\\",\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"detailsUrl\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40866393136/job/123422134009\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"test-matrix (24)\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T11:34:15Z\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"IN_PROGRESS\\\",\\\"workflowName\\\":\\\"CI\\\"},{\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"CheckRun\\\",\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"detailsUrl\\\":\\\"https://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/38/changes/nexus-code/38\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Entire Gates\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T11:36:38Z\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"IN_PROGRESS\\\",\\\"workflowName\\\":\\\"\\\"},{\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"CheckRun\\\",\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T11:35:10Z\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"SUCCESS\\\",\\\"detailsUrl\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/123422522863\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"CodeQL\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T11:35:07Z\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"COMPLETED\\\",\\\"workflowName\\\":\\\"\\\"},{\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"StatusContext\\\",\\\"context\\\":\\\"CodeRabbit\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T11:34:20Z\\\",\\\"state\\\":\\\"SUCCESS\\\",\\\"targetUrl\\\":\\\"\\\"}]}\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":3,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"e872b2\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000027686,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":4537,\"output\":\"# Nexus Code v1.0.0: release qualification procedure\\n\\nThis is the procedure that decides whether a release candidate (RC) may become v1.0.0. It defines:\\n\\n- the environments;\\n- the workflow matrix;\\n- the evidence each step must produce;\\n- explicit pass/fail gates.\\n\\nThree separate questions are judged and recorded separately:\\n\\n| Question | Who answers it |\\n|---|---|\\n| **Implementation self-assessment** | Did the implementer's tests pass? |\\n| **Product qualification** | Did the RC meet these gates on real workflows? |\\n| **Independent acceptance** | Did a reviewer other than the implementer agree? |\\n\\nA gate passes only on archived evidence bound to the source commit or installed RC artifact that the gate evaluates. Source-level evidence names the exact source commit; installed-RC evidence names both that commit and the installed package digest. A green test suite alone never qualifies the product.\\n\\n## 1.1 Release-candidate lifecycle and evidence identity\\n\\nThe release sequence has five distinct stages. Passing an earlier stage is a prerequisite for the next stage, not a substitute for it. Every G0–G4 acceptance ID remains mandatory; the stage determines which exact input and evidence it evaluates, not whether the check applies.\\n\\n1. **Pre-RC source gates.** Before creating an RC tag, run required source CI and every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method evaluates source, a source-built test binary, or an environment without requiring a published RC. Record the full commit ID and check results. Source checks do not establish behavior of the installed package.\\n2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\\n3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\\n4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\\n5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\\n\\nThe final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\\n\\nExact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\\n\\nThe post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\\n\\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\\n### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\\n\\n| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\\n| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\\n| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\\n| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\\n| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\\n| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\\n| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\\n| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\\n| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\\n| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\\n| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\\n| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\\n\\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\\n### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\\n\\n| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\\n|---|---|---|\\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\\n\\n## 1. Rules\\n\\n1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\\n2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\\n3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\\n4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\\n   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\\n   - raw outputs;\\n   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\\n\\n   Secrets are redacted before commit.\\n5. Any step that cannot run in the available environment is recorded as **NOT RUN** with its reason. A NOT RUN on a blocker gate fails the gate.\\n\\n## 2. Environments\\n\\n| ID | Environment | Used for |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\\n| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\\n| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\\n| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\\n| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\\n\\n## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\\n\\nEvery ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\\n\\n| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\\n| Process ownership | ACC-PROC-01 to ACC-PROC-08 (ACC-PROC-07 is the load test, run in E3) | SPEC-02 |\\n| Untrusted inputs | ACC-TRUST-01 to ACC-TRUST-09 | SPEC-03 |\\n| Continuity | ACC-CONT-01 to ACC-CONT-09 (ACC-CONT-10 is in §8) | SPEC-04 |\\n| Inference | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-09 (ACC-INF-10 is in §4) | SPEC-05 |\\n| Packaging | ACC-PKG-01 to ACC-PKG-09 | SPEC-06 |\\n| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\\n| Persistence | ACC-PER-01 to ACC-PER-07 | SPEC-08 |\\n| Governance | ACC-GOV-01 to ACC-GOV-06 | SPEC-09 |\\n| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\\n| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\\n\\n\\n### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\\n\\nThese are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\\n\\n| ID | Check | Pass condition |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\\n| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\\n| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\\n| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\\n| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\\n| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\\n| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\\n| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\\n| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\\n| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\\n| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\\n| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | All 15 cells have actual manual execution, recorded PASS/FAIL verdicts, observed outcomes, and evidence bound to the exact installed RC. Automated §5.1 and §5.2 do not substitute for these cells. Screenshot artifacts alone are waived by DEC-18. |\\n\\n## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\\n\\n### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\\n\\n1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\\n2. Install the RC with the documented command.\\n3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\\n4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\\n5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\\n\\n### 4.2 Standalone matrix\\n\\n| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\\n| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\\n| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\\n| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\\n| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\\n\\nACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\\n\\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\\n\\n| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\\n| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\\n| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\\n| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\\n\\n## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\\n\\n### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\\n\\nThese must pass:\\n\\n- `tui_approval_input_e2e`\\n- `tui_diff_e2e`\\n- `tui_maturity_e2e`\\n- `tui_model_picker_e2e`\\n- `tui_multiline_e2e`\\n- `tui_surface_e2e`\\n- new: `repl_approval_e2e`\\n- new: `process_lifecycle_e2e`\\n- new: `startup_unreachable_e2e`\\n- new: the package PTY smoke\\n\\n### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\\n\\nThese are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\\n\\n| Scenario | Pass condition |\\n247-**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12.\\n248-\\n249:## DEC-19: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\\n250-\\n251-**Status: withdrawn.** The waiver described in this decision is not in effect.\\n252-\\n253-**History.** A prior revision of this decision recorded that the release owner waived the manual matrix. That record conflicted with the explicit release requirement for five terminal environments × three sizes. The waiver is withdrawn and must not be used to disposition any v1.0.0 gate.\\n254-\\n255-**Current decision (release owner direction, 2026-10-29).** All fifteen manual E3 cells remain mandatory on the exact installed RC. Record a PASS or FAIL and observed outcomes for every required check in every cell. Automated CI or PTY runs do not substitute for operator evidence. [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) remains in force and waives screenshot artifacts only; it does not waive interaction, checks, per-cell verdicts, evidence records, or safety gates. No cell is accepted as complete without actual manual execution.\\n256-\\n257-**Disclosure.** Do not describe the manual matrix as waived. Until all fifteen cells have verified operator evidence, ACC-TUI-MANUAL remains incomplete and v1.0.0 acceptance remains blocked.\\n258-\\n259-**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS; release notes.\\n260-\\n261-## Owner and external actions required (not performed by the audit)\\n\"}}}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","create_time":1793273889.8048391}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
