{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T11:55:03.453Z","ordinal":499314,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18783-7b9d-75f2-8bed-ac513eb90697","author":"/root/review_pr300_readiness","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_pr300_readiness\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** for PR #323. Its exact head is `ea7b728c70ba05d7ff106c14c0adffd99e6012a5`; the diff SHA-256 is `535d7f5244de1708f2e90931bcf730002d341ea15fb241ae2d196805e734c872`.\n\nThe six changed files are synchronized RC11 version metadata and the new release notes. The notes accurately preserve the outstanding qualification gates and DEC-18/DEC-19 terminal requirements.\n\nThe toolchain statement in `docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.11.md:29` overstates what this candidate enforces. CI provisions toolchain directories, but the current evaluator source still dynamically selects Go and Rust toolchains; PR #318, which adds fail-closed pinned-toolchain enforcement, remains open.\n\nNode 22/24, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks pass. Linux and Entire Gates are still running. After correcting the statement, the PR may be considered for merge once all required exact-head checks and independent review pass."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","create_time":1793274903.453617,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":23324}}
