{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T11:56:46.238Z","ordinal":499380,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a13f3bc0-c14b-40e1-a38f-80a99d4796c9","process_id":"27734","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/323/comments --jq '.[-2].body'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/323/comments --jq '.[-2].body'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"**claude-code independent review — CHANGES_REQUIRED** at exact head `ea7b728c70ba05d7ff106c14c0adffd99e6012a5` (base `df288ef010a93c418e4972d3d40dc293ec9c0081`).\n\n**Owner decision, re-confirmed to me directly at 2026-10-29T11:52:20Z:** I asked the release owner directly. They named PR #316 (fc2ec326), the DEC-19 withdrawal, and the 03:55Z \"15 manual cells required\" direction cited there, and asked which decision is current. Their answer was **\"Waive matrix\"**: DEC-19 is reinstated. For v1.0.0, the manual 5×3 real-terminal matrix is **waived, not passed**. ACC-TUI-MANUAL is recorded as waived; no cell verdict is recorded or inferred. The automated CI PTY gates and the scripted installed-RC PTY gates (ACCEPTANCE §5.1–§5.2) stay mandatory. REQ-QUAL-108 stays partial. The release notes must disclose the waiver.\n\n**Blocking findings in `docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.11.md`:**\n1. The line \"The manual real-terminal matrix is **required** for v1.0.0; the earlier matrix-waiver record was withdrawn (DEC-19)\" contradicts the owner's current decision. It should say that the manual matrix is waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision (DEC-19), that terminal evidence is automated only (CI PTY plus scripted installed-RC PTY), and that DEC-18 is subsumed.\n2. The outstanding-gates paragraph lists \"the fifteen-cell manual terminal matrix\". It should list \"the automated and scripted installed-RC PTY terminal gates (§5.1–§5.2)\" instead.\n\n**Dependency:** main still carries #316's withdrawal text in DECISIONS (DEC-19), ACCEPTANCE §5.3/§10 G6, SPEC-10, PLAN-10 task 12, TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET and READINESS. Those need a reinstatement doc PR, which PR #315's head `706c3b6c` largely is: I reviewed that diff against DEC-19 and found it consistent. The notes fix should land with or after that PR. I'm not taking those files, because they're claimed or owned by the coordinator lane. Please reinstate DEC-19 or hand the files off to me.\n\n**Verified at the exact head**, in an isolated worktree with isolated HOME/XDG:\n- `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passes: 123 rows; tested 108, partial 6, implemented 2, open 7; 12 exact-RC deferrals.\n- `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports all components at 1.0.0-rc.11.\n- The version-only diff touches cli/core/root manifests and lockfiles plus the notes. Nothing else in the notes was found blocking.\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":366451987}},"started_at_ms":1793275005870,"completed_at_ms":1793275006237}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T11:56:46.357Z","ordinal":499381,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18785-0d95-74d1-b17d-813d87243423","call_id":"call_f5c0b2f4ab304de5ab0bc15e5d855026","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"**claude-code independent review — CHANGES_REQUIRED** at exact head `ea7b728c70ba05d7ff106c14c0adffd99e6012a5` (base `df288ef010a93c418e4972d3d40dc293ec9c0081`).\n\n**Owner decision, re-confirmed to me directly at 2026-10-29T11:52:20Z:** I asked the release owner directly. They named PR #316 (fc2ec326), the DEC-19 withdrawal, and the 03:55Z \"15 manual cells required\" direction cited there, and asked which decision is current. Their answer was **\"Waive matrix\"**: DEC-19 is reinstated. For v1.0.0, the manual 5×3 real-terminal matrix is **waived, not passed**. ACC-TUI-MANUAL is recorded as waived; no cell verdict is recorded or inferred. The automated CI PTY gates and the scripted installed-RC PTY gates (ACCEPTANCE §5.1–§5.2) stay mandatory. REQ-QUAL-108 stays partial. The release notes must disclose the waiver.\n\n**Blocking findings in `docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.11.md`:**\n1. The line \"The manual real-terminal matrix is **required** for v1.0.0; the earlier matrix-waiver record was withdrawn (DEC-19)\" contradicts the owner's current decision. It should say that the manual matrix is waived for v1.0.0 by owner decision (DEC-19), that terminal evidence is automated only (CI PTY plus scripted installed-RC PTY), and that DEC-18 is subsumed.\n2. The outstanding-gates paragraph lists \"the fifteen-cell manual terminal matrix\". It should list \"the automated and scripted installed-RC PTY terminal gates (§5.1–§5.2)\" instead.\n\n**Dependency:** main still carries #316's withdrawal text in DECISIONS (DEC-19), ACCEPTANCE §5.3/§10 G6, SPEC-10, PLAN-10 task 12, TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET and READINESS. Those need a reinstatement doc PR, which PR #315's head `706c3b6c` largely is: I reviewed that diff against DEC-19 and found it consistent. The notes fix should land with or after that PR. I'm not taking those files, because they're claimed or owned by the coordinator lane. Please reinstate DEC-19 or hand the files off to me.\n\n**Verified at the exact head**, in an isolated worktree with isolated HOME/XDG:\n- `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passes: 123 rows; tested 108, partial 6, implemented 2, open 7; 12 exact-RC deferrals.\n- `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports all components at 1.0.0-rc.11.\n- The version-only diff touches cli/core/root manifests and lockfiles plus the notes. Nothing else in the notes was found blocking.\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","create_time":1793275006.357609}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
