{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T12:12:00.309Z","ordinal":500165,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18792-ffb5-7b92-9873-38f9754df46f","author":"/root/review_pr302","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_pr302\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — HEAD `493bffde3c961c36631d644f0e25dca834702712`, base `df288ef010a93c418e4972d3d40dc293ec9c0081`. Current working-tree diff SHA-256: `58407d969d481625cd2b066314fd4af7fb9f0ae97b9c5fe2171e7395ed2d880e`.\n\nThe alias-path change preserves each lexical mount spelling during scanning, so shared directories mounted as `/lib` and `/usr/lib` produce separate compiler paths for masking ([isolate.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:137)). The fixture creates a directory symlink alias and asserts both spellings are detected ([eval_integrity.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:549)). Each detected path is then masked with its own `/dev/null` bind.\n\nRead-only review; no tests run."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","create_time":1793275920.309133,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":23353}}
