`task_completed`, Nexus runs `make test` / `npm test` / `cargo test` / `pytest` through `bridge.executeTool` directly. These run arbitrary repo-defined code with no approval prompt and no workspace-trust check (unlike MCP/plugins, workspace_trust.ts), and unsandboxed unless `--sandbox`. Review mode shows an approval for `edit_file` but never for the hidden repo script that follows. Builds on SEC-01; it is a separate path because it bypasses even review mode. | Cloning a hostile repo and asking for any edit runs its test script on the host without a prompt. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: gate discovered verifiers on workspace trust or a one-time approval of the exact command (shown with its script body), and run them sandboxed when one is available. Document this. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:53:| VER-02 | S2 | Every turn on local models | parser.ts:382-434 (steps 4-5); fewshots.ts:18-56 | RUNTIME (probe P1, P9). Any JSON object in the assistant's prose whose `name`/`tool`/`action` is an offered tool is executed. Examples: \"an agent would normally call {\"name\":\"run_command\",...} but I did not\" → `run_command rm -rf build` executed. A model quoting a file that contains `{\"name\":\"read_file\",\"arguments\":{\"path\":\"/etc/shadow\"}}` in a json fence → executed. The few-shot exemplars teach exactly this fenced format. The parser falls back to text even when the provider supports native tool calls. | Prompt-injection amplifier: content the model merely echoes becomes an action, unapproved by default (SEC-01). | RELEASE-REQUIRED: enable text-embedded parsing only for connections without native tool calling (capability flag). Restrict it to `<tool_call>` tags or a sole fenced block that makes up the whole reply. Never parse prose `{…}`. Add negative tests. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:134:| R-VER-1 | Repo-defined verifier commands (discovered) run only in a trusted workspace or after one approval that shows the command and script body. They run sandboxed when a sandbox is available. | safety | RELEASE-REQUIRED | An untrusted temp repo with `\"test\":\"touch /tmp/pwn\"` plus an edit request: no file created without a prompt, in both default and --approve modes. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s3_complete.py:4:s = Session(tui_argv(ws, ep, approve=True), env, 80, 24, ws, \"s3\")\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/r1d.py:4:s = Session([\"node\", INDEX, \"repl\", \"--approve\", \"-w\", ws, \"-e\", ep, \"-m\", \"m\"], env, 100, 30, ws, \"r1d\")\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:36:2. At the approval panel, type continuously across it, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/r1_repl.py:5:s = Session([\"node\", INDEX, \"repl\", \"--approve\", \"-w\", ws, \"-e\", ep, \"-m\", \"m\"], env, 100, 30, ws, \"r1a\")\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/r1_repl.py:16:s = Session([\"node\", INDEX, \"repl\", \"--approve\", \"-w\", ws, \"-e\", ep, \"-m\", \"m\"], env, 100, 30, ws, \"r1b\")\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/r1_repl.py:29:s = Session([\"node\", INDEX, \"repl\", \"--approve\", \"-w\", ws, \"-e\", ep, \"-m\", \"m\"], env, 100, 30, ws, \"r1c\")\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md:15:| C7 | Publish the video's source commits under a tag (`contest-video-2026-10`) together with the run record, or state in the docs that they are unpublished. | git tag push (owner-approved) | Medium |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:30:- Model tool call -> `agent.dispatchToolCall` (agent.ts:3880). Vault `restore()` puts real secrets back into args for non-egress tools (agent.ts:3899-3906). Flight recorder logs args. The **approval gate runs only when an `onConfirm` handler exists and the capability is `mutating`** (agent.ts:3946-3947). The handler auto-approves unless `--approve` / `/mode review` is set: repl.ts:69,281; index.ts:93,115; sidecar.ts:935.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:51:| SEC-03 | S2 | fetch_web (unapproved even in review mode) | tools.ts:52-111, 653-658 | RUNTIME (Repro R4). The SSRF guard is a hostname-string check with no DNS resolution and no redirect control (`fetch` follows redirects). `http://localtest.me:18731/` and `http://[::ffff:127.0.0.1]:18731/` both fetched a loopback-only server. Also not blocked: fd00::/8, fe80::/10, 100.64/10. The response body is read fully before truncation (tools.ts:662). | The model can reach loopback and LAN services (homelab gateway, admin UIs) and exfiltrate data in the URL query. There is no approval prompt, because fetch_web is non-mutating. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: resolve and pin the IP, check every redirect hop (`redirect: \"manual\"`), block all of v4/v6 private, ULA, link-local and mapped ranges, and cap the body size. Consider requiring approval for egress in review mode. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:53:| SEC-05 | S2 | untrusted repo opened | skills.ts:31-33; agent.ts:3301,3789 | SOURCE. Workspace skills (SKILL.md) are loaded and advertised in the system prompt with no workspace-trust check, unlike MCP and plugins (workspace_trust.ts:5-24). `activate_skill` is non-mutating, so it is never approved. | Persistent prompt injection from a cloned repo. Combined with SEC-01 this gives command execution. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: gate workspace skill directories on workspace trust, or show them as untrusted and require approval to activate. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s2_approval.py:4:s = Session(tui_argv(ws, ep, approve=True), env, 100, 30, ws, \"s2\")\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:20:**Documented commands fail.** `nexus --approve` and `nexus -r` (USER_MANUAL.md:12-26) both fail with \"unknown option\", on both launchers (REL-02, TUI-05; RUNTIME).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:66:- **Top-level `--repl`, `--live`, `-r/--resume [id]`, `--approve`.** Declared as global options that map onto the default action, so the USER_MANUAL commands work (DEC-02).\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md:17:| 3 | Create the GitHub milestone `v1.0.0` and one issue per PLAN PR slice, each linked to its ledger IDs. Because this changes GitHub state, it is an **owner-approved action** in the implementation phase. | GitHub | M0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s3.screens.txt:25: approval needed · y approve · n deny (after a pause) ──────────────────────────\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/s3.screens.txt:31:  ✓ approved Write hello.txt\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/ptylib.py:161:def tui_argv(ws, endpoint, approve=False, extra=()):\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/ptylib.py:163:    if approve:\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/ptylib.py:164:        a.append(\"--approve\")\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:21:Review mode (`--approve`) gates only capabilities with `mutating: true` (`cli/src/agent.ts:3946-3947`). The following are declared `mutating: false` (`cli/src/core/capabilities.ts`), so **review mode never asks before they run**:\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:30:- A lone Enter approves the action (TUI-02, reproduced in a PTY).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:31:- Text typed during the turn is merged into the answer, so a `y` typed early followed by Enter approves (TUI-03, reproduced).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:35:**Verifier runs bypass the gate entirely (VER-01).** Before the first edit (change baseline, `agent.ts:1602-1617`) and at every `task_completed` (`agent.ts:3432-3436`), Nexus runs the repository's own test command (`make test` / `npm test` / `cargo test` / `pytest`, chosen by `tester.ts:113-136`) through `bridge.executeTool` directly. These calls skip `dispatchToolCall`, so even review mode never asks, and no workspace-trust check applies. Opening a hostile repo and approving one `edit_file` therefore runs that repo's arbitrary test script on the host. `/test` and `nexus eval` run `execSync` on the host, bypassing the sandbox and blocking the event loop (VER-14).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:48:| TUI-02 Enter approves | RUNTIME (PTY r1a) | evidence/D_terminal.md §4 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:49:| TUI-03 typed-ahead approves | RUNTIME (PTY r1d) | D §4 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:86:- Per-command allowlists (\"always allow `npm test`\"). These are optional post-v1. The design below keeps the `a` (approve-all for session) answer.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:117:3. Change the prompt to `[y/N/d/a]`. Empty input means **No**. Only `y`/`yes` approves.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:118:4. `a` (approve all for this session) requires a confirm line: `type 'all' to confirm`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:140:- `HarnessConfig.approvalMode: \"auto\" | \"review\" | \"read-only\"`. This replaces the boolean `autoApprove` flags in the REPL and sidecar. `--mode auto` selects auto with per-origin egress approval; `--yes` and `NEXUS_APPROVAL_MODE=auto` select full access and bypass egress approval too. `--approve` selects review and `--read-only` selects read-only.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:153:- An approval handler error is DENIED with a reason. It is never treated as approved.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md:31:| 1 | Default action: on a TTY with nexus-tui resolvable, spawn `nexus-tui --live --sidecar <resolved> --node process.execPath -- …` with inherited stdio and exit with its code; otherwise use the REPL with a notice. Add global flags `--repl`, `--live`, `-r/--resume [id]`, `--approve`, `--yes`. Set `program.name(\"nexus\")`. | `index.ts:60-120,745-757` | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/running_notes.md:13:- s2 (TUI --approve, write_file): continuous typing \"yes y y please yy\\ry\\r\" at 120ms gaps across panel appearance,\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/running_notes.md:15:  -> NONE decided (file absent); panel switched to \"typing ignore