{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T12:19:40.598Z","ordinal":500553,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae339dac7d0819fbf42539da1259777","usage":{"input_tokens":171626,"cached_input_tokens":169088,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":154,"reasoning_output_tokens":40,"total_tokens":171780},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":38306314,"cached_input_tokens":37703040,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":90301,"reasoning_output_tokens":51871,"total_tokens":38396615},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9362424114,"cached_input_tokens":9262400768,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":27122607,"reasoning_output_tokens":15915084,"total_tokens":9389546721}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T12:19:41.578Z","ordinal":500554,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-b5db5b29-373d-4900-a8c4-ae46e79591c1","process_id":"44729","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,100p' docs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md; sed -n '1,130p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | rg -n -C 3 'independent|review|approval'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,100p' docs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md","name":"PROTECTIONS.md","path":"docs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,130p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","name":"ACCEPTANCE.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n -C 3 'independent|review|approval'","query":"independent|review|approval","path":null}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Repository protections for the v1 release\n\nThe branch and release-tag rulesets below were observed active through the GitHub API on 2026-10-18.\nAdministrative changes require a connection with the relevant settings permissions.\n\n## Recorded settings and observations\n\nRulesets were freshly verified on 2026-10-18. Collaborator, default-token, Actions-policy, and environment rows below are earlier recorded observations, not freshly verified by this change.\n\n| Setting | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Rulesets | Active `v1-protected-branches` (25340146) and `v1-immutable-release-tags` (25340148) |\n| Collaborators | `mikeholownych` (admin) only; every agent pushes as this account |\n| Default workflow token | `read`; workflows request extra permissions themselves (`release.yml`: `contents`, `id-token`, `attestations` write) |\n| Actions | all actions allowed; SHA pinning not required |\n| Environments | none |\n\nAll agents share one GitHub identity, so GitHub cannot separate authors from reviewers. A rule requiring an approving\nreview would deadlock every PR, because an author cannot approve their own PR. Independent review therefore stays\nwhere it is recorded today: separate reviewer agents, the claim log and the evidence directories. The rules below\nenforce what GitHub *can* check: required CI, no history rewriting, and immutable release tags.\n\n## Rules\n\n`rulesets/protected-branches.json` covers `main` and `v1/integration`:\n- no deletion and no force-push;\n- changes only through a pull request (0 required approvals, for the reason above), merged with a **merge commit\n  only** (`allowed_merge_methods: [\"merge\"]`). A squash or rebase merge would create new commits, leaving the RC tag\n  commit or the stable commit `S` off `main`;\n- required checks: `test-matrix (20)`, `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)` and `linux-x86_64`, all from\n  GitHub Actions. The retired contest-contract check is not required;\n- the strict \"branch must be up to date\" policy is **off**. See the deadlock analysis below. CONCURRENCY §5.4\n  (rebase onto the base, then rerun) remains the process rule.\n\n`rulesets/release-tags.json` covers `refs/tags/v*`:\n- tags can be created, but never moved or deleted.\n\nNo bypass actors are defined. To repair a mistaken tag, the owner disables the ruleset, records why, and enables it again.\n\n## Lifecycle check (ACCEPTANCE §1.1)\n\n1. **RC source to `main`.** PR #8 (`v1/integration` to `main`) needs the required checks. It is merged with a merge\n   commit `M`. The RC tag `v1.0.0-rc.N` goes on `M`, which is on `main`, so `release.yml`'s ancestry check passes.\n   Creating a tag is allowed.\n2. **RC rebuild.** A fix is merged through PRs, and a new tag `rc.N+1` is created. Old RC tags stay as evidence.\n3. **Stable promotion.** Commit `S` changes only the version and sits directly on the accepted RC commit `M`. A PR\n   from a branch whose head is `S` targets `main`. While `main` is still `M`, `S` is already current, and the merge\n   keeps `S` in `main`'s history. Tag `v1.0.0` goes on `S`. `release.yml` verifies it is version-only on `rc.N`.\n   - With strict \"up to date\" checks, any merge to `main` between the RC and the stable commit would force an update\n     merge into the PR branch. `S` would then no longer be directly on the RC, which is the deadlock that keeping\n     strict mode off avoids.\n   - Process rule: **nothing else merges to `main` between the accepted RC and the stable tag.**\n4. **Publication.** `release.yml` creates the stable release as a draft. `gh release edit v1.0.0 --draft=false` is not\n   affected by these rules.\n\n## Not covered by rulesets (owner settings, optional)\n\n- **Actions SHA pinning** (`sha_pinning_required`). This would break the current workflows, which pin actions by tag,\n  until every `uses:` is pinned to a full SHA. This PR pins workflow action references; verify the merged default branch before enabling the setting. It is not automatically a new v1 prerequisite.\n- **Release immutability.** This is a repository setting, not a ruleset. If enabled before publication, a published\n  release's assets cannot be replaced.\n\n## Apply, verify, roll back (owner)\n\n```sh\nR=repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code\n# first: the required contexts must equal the check names of the latest green integration run (no output = equal)\ndiff <(gh api \"$R/commits/$(git rev-parse origin/v1/integration)/check-runs\" -q '[.check_runs[].name] | sort | .[]') \\\n     <(jq -r '[.rules[] | select(.type == \"required_status_checks\") | .parameters.required_status_checks[].context] | sort | .[]' \\\n         docs/releases/rulesets/protected-branches.json)\ngh api -X POST \"$R/rulesets\" --input docs/releases/rulesets/protected-branches.json\ngh api -X POST \"$R/rulesets\" --input docs/releases/rulesets/release-tags.json\n# verify\ngh api \"$R/rules/branches/main\" -q '[.[].type]'           # deletion, non_fast_forward, pull_request, required_status_checks\ngh api \"$R/rules/branches/v1/integration\" -q '[.[].type]'\ngh api \"$R/rulesets\" -q '.[] | \"\\(.id) \\(.name) \\(.enforcement)\"'\n# roll back one ruleset\ngh api -X DELETE \"$R/rulesets/<id>\"\n```\n\nAfter applying, `git push origin <sha>:main` should be rejected, and so should moving or deleting an existing `v*`\ntag. A PR with green required checks should still merge.\n13-|---|---|\n14-| **Implementation self-assessment** | Did the implementer's tests pass? |\n15-| **Product qualification** | Did the RC meet these gates on real workflows? |\n16:| **Independent acceptance** | Did a reviewer other than the implementer agree? |\n17-\n18-A gate passes only on archived evidence bound to the source commit or installed RC artifact that the gate evaluates. Source-level evidence names the exact source commit; installed-RC evidence names both that commit and the installed package digest. A green test suite alone never qualifies the product.\n19-\n--\n24-1. **Pre-RC source gates.** Before creating an RC tag, run required source CI and every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method evaluates source, a source-built test binary, or an environment without requiring a published RC. Record the full commit ID and check results. Source checks do not establish behavior of the installed package.\n25-2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\n26-3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\n27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\n28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\n29-\n30-The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\n31-\n32:Exact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\n33-\n34-The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\n35-\n--\n40-|---|---|---|\n41-| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\n42-| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\n43:| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\n44-| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n45-| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n46:| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n47-| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n48-| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n49-| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n--\n64-1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n65-2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n66-3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n67:4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n68-   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n69-   - raw outputs;\n70-   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\n--\n110-| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n111-| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n112-| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n113:| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n114-| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n115-| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n116-| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":809867792}},"started_at_ms":1793276380767,"completed_at_ms":1793276381578}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T12:19:42.040Z","ordinal":500555,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1879a-0b58-7b03-90f8-e473959728da","call_id":"call_67372be560444ee38be5ecec2158e188","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 3531)\nTotal output lines: 129\n\n# Repository protections for the v1 release\n\nThe branch and release-tag rulesets below were observed active through the GitHub API on 2026-10-18.\nAdministrative changes require a connection with the relevant settings permissions.\n\n## Recorded settings and observations\n\nRulesets were freshly verified on 2026-10-18. Collaborator, default-token, Actions-policy, and environment rows below are earlier recorded observations, not freshly verified by this change.\n\n| Setting | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Rulesets | Active `v1-protected-branches` (25340146) and `v1-immutable-release-tags` (25340148) |\n| Collaborators | `mikeholownych` (admin) only; every agent pushes as this account |\n| Default workflow token | `read`; workflows request extra permissions themselves (`release.yml`: `contents`, `id-token`, `attestations` write) |\n| Actions | all actions allowed; SHA pinning not required |\n| Environments | none |\n\nAll agents share one GitHub identity, so GitHub cannot separate authors from reviewers. A rule requiring an approving\nreview would deadlock every PR, because an author cannot approve their own PR. Independent review therefore stays\nwhere it is recorded today: separate reviewer agents, the claim log and the evidence directories. The rules below\nenforce what GitHub *can* check: required CI, no history rewriting, and immutable release tags.\n\n## Rules\n\n`rulesets/protected-branches.json` covers `main` and `v1/integration`:\n- no deletion and no force-push;\n- changes only through a pull request (0 required approvals, for the reason above), merged with a **merge commit\n  only** (`allowed_merge_methods: [\"merge\"]`). A squash or rebase merge would create new commits, leaving the RC tag\n  commit or the stable commit `S` off `main`;\n- required checks: `test-matrix (20)`, `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)` and `linux-x86_64`, all from\n  GitHub Actions. The retired contest-contract check is not required;\n- the strict \"branch must be up to date\" policy is **off**. See the deadlock analysis below. CONCURRENCY §5.4\n  (rebase onto the base, then rerun) remains the process rule.\n\n`rulesets/release-tags.json` covers `refs/tags/v*`:\n- tags can be created, but never moved or deleted.\n\nNo bypass actors are defined. To repair a mistaken tag, the owner disables the ruleset, records why, and enables it again.\n\n## Lifecycle check (ACCEPTANCE §1.1)\n\n1. **RC source to `main`.** PR #8 (`v1/integration` to `main`) needs the required checks. It is merged with a merge\n   commit `M`. The RC tag `v1.0.0-rc.N` goes on `M`, which is on `main`, so `release.yml`'s ancestry check passes.\n   Creating a tag is allowed.\n2. **RC rebuild.** A fix is merged through PRs, and a new tag `rc.N+1` is created. Old RC tags stay as evidence.\n3. **Stable promotion.** Commit `S` changes only the version and sits directly on the accepted RC commit `M`. A PR\n   from a branch whose head is `S` targets `main`. While `main` is still `M`, `S` is already current, and the merge\n   keeps `S` in `main`'s history. Tag `v1.0.0` goes on `S`. `release.yml` verifies it is version-only on `rc.N`.\n   - With strict \"up to date\" checks, any merge to `main` between the RC and the stable commit would force an update\n     merge into the PR branch. `S` would then no longer be directly on the RC, which is the deadlock that keeping\n     strict mode off avoids.\n   - Process rule: **nothing else merges to `main` between the accepted RC and the stable tag.**\n4. **Publication.** `release.yml` creates the stable release as a draft. `gh release edit v1.0.0 --draft=false` is not\n   affected by these rules.\n\n## Not covered by rulesets (owner settings, optional)\n\n- **Actions SHA pinning** (`sha_pinning_required`). This would break the current workflows, which pin actions by tag,\n  until every `uses:` is pinned to a full SHA. This PR pins workflow action references; verify the merged default branch before enabling the setting. It is not automatically a new v1 prerequisite.\n- **Release immutability.** This is a repository…1531 tokens truncated…ted decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\n33-\n34-The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\n35-\n--\n40-|---|---|---|\n41-| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\n42-| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\n43:| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\n44-| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n45-| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n46:| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n47-| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n48-| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n49-| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n--\n64-1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n65-2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n66-3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n67:4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n68-   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n69-   - raw outputs;\n70-   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\n--\n110-| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n111-| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n112-| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n113:| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n114-| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n115-| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n116-| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","create_time":1793276382.0402026}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
