9T04:35:57Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"PR #318 remediation of independent-review P1: prevent candidate task processes from reaching unpinned Go/Rust compilers through absolute system paths; preserve existing toolchain work; synthetic fixtures only; no held-out qualification task use; no changes outside this worktree\",\n  \"validation_status\": \"Pushed head 37855d08 exact CI run 40871541877 failed Node22 and Node24 (17 failures); source failure: bwrap rejects --ro-bind /dev/null onto symlink /usr/bin/go, causing downstream evaluator/T3 sandbox failures. Focused 44/44 tests passed locally but did not model the CI symlink. Remediation in progress; independent review of prior diff remains valid only for old hash. No held-out use.\",\n  \"last_updated\": \"2026-10-29T12:34:00Z\",\n  \"head\": \"37855d08d342412b6177baa9f30dd6a31d37d10e\",\n  \"review\": \"Independent ACCEPT applies only to cumulative diff 58407d969d481625cd2b066314fd4af7fb9f0ae97b9c5fe2171e7395ed2d880e before this CI-discovered mount-target defect; new remediation requires fresh review.\",\n  \"status\": \"PR318 exact-head CI failure being corrected; do not merge. No held-out use.\"\n}\n--- /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_test_eval_integrity.test.ts/owner.json\n{\n  \"agent\": \"codex-root\",\n  \"program\": \"codex-app\",\n  \"model\": \"gpt-6.1\",\n  \"host\": \"mike-dev\",\n  \"branch\": \"v1/eval-agent-toolchain-binds\",\n  \"worktree\": \"/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds\",\n  \"base\": \"df288ef010a93c418e4972d3d40dc293ec9c0081\",\n  \"since\": \"2026-10-29T04:35:57Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"PR #318 regression coverage for pinned toolchain confinement including an adversarial absolute-path attempt through the actual candidate sandbox; synthetic fixtures only; no held-out qualification task use; no changes outside this worktree\",\n  \"head\": \"37855d08d342412b6177baa9f30dd6a31d37d10e\",\n  \"status\": \"PR318 exact-head CI failure being corrected; do not merge. No held-out use.\",\n  \"last_updated\": \"2026-10-29T12:34:00Z\",\n  \"validation_status\": \"Pushed head 37855d08 exact CI run 40871541877 failed Node22 and Node24 (17 failures); source failure: bwrap rejects --ro-bind /dev/null onto symlink /usr/bin/go, causing downstream evaluator/T3 sandbox failures. Focused 44/44 tests passed locally but did not model the CI symlink. Remediation in progress; independent review of prior diff remains valid only for old hash. No held-out use.\",\n  \"review\": \"Independent ACCEPT applies only to cumulative diff 58407d969d481625cd2b066314fd4af7fb9f0ae97b9c5fe2171e7395ed2d880e before this CI-discovered mount-target defect; new remediation requires fresh review.\"\n}\n--- /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/SUITE/owner.json\n{\"agent\":\"codex-root\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"v1/eval-agent-toolchain-binds\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds\",\"since\":\"2026-10-29T12:39:00Z\",\"scope\":\"PR318 resolved-target compiler masks and symlink regression; focused eval_integrity and eval_t3 only; no held-out tasks or payloads\"}\nAGENTS.md:13:## Entire CLI\nAGENTS.md:14:- Set `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file` in the environment before running any `entire` command (for example, `export ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file`).\n./AGENTS.md:13:## Entire CLI\n./AGENTS.md:14:- Set `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file` in the environment before running any `entire` command (for example, `export ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file`).\n./docs/WP04_CORRECTION_VERIFICATION.md:88:- **Vulnerability:** Non-Git directory walking used `dirent.isFile()`, ignoring symlinks entirely. Non-standard filesystem objects were not explicitly rejected.\n./docs/ARCHITECTURE.md:64:7. **Process group lifecycle and residual setsid escape risk.** The runner registers child process groups at spawn and terminates entire groups (`killpg`) on turn cancel, client crash, or process shutdown (REQ-AGT-109, REQ-SEC-106). Background services explicitly registered survive turn cancel but are cleaned on client exit. *Limit:* commands that explicitly invoke `setsid()` or create a new session ID escape the process group boundary unless Bubblewrap (`--sandbox`) or Docker isolation is enabled (`bwrap` uses `--die-with-parent` and PID namespaces to guarantee all descendants are swept). Documented residual risk: in unsandboxed mode, processes that detach with `setsid()` will outlive cancel sweeps.\n./docs/REPOSITORY_QUALITY.md:59:Pinned actions reduce mutable-reference risk. Build tooling downloaded by shell commands and the moving Rust stable toolchain remain separate supply-chain work; do not describe the entire build as hermetic. Cross-runner and installed-release acceptance still follow the accepted release plan.\n./docs/ISSUE12_POST_WP05_CLOSURE_ASSESSMENT.md:30:With WP-05 now fully implemented, independently falsified, and explicitly **OPERATOR ACCEPTED**, this assessment reconciles the entire original 122-requirement normative contract against the new accepted baseline.\n./docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST_CRITICAL_PATH_ASSESSMENT.md:191:6. **Thin presentation and rehearsal:** run the entire flow several times from reset fixtures, capture failure/recovery behavior, prepare a 5–10 minute script/video and reproducible instructions. The recording must show actual service and repository activity, not playback dressed as live execution.\n./docs/WP02_INDEPENDENT_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md:200:  2. Forbid subshell execution and command substitution entirely under read-only mode, or parse commands into discrete argv tokens and validate each token against an explicit immutable utility allowlist without shell execution.\n./experiments/context-validation-2026-10-04/fixtures/nexus_tools_and_system.json:1:{\"tools\":[{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"read_file\",\"description\":\"Read the contents of a file with line numbers. Use start_line and end_line for specific ranges.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Relative path to the file within the workspace.\"},\"start_line\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"1-indexed starting line number (optional).\"},\"end_line\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"1-indexed ending line number (optional).\"}},\"required\":[\"path\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"write_file\",\"description\":\"Create a new file or completely overwrite an existing file with the provided content.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Relative path to the file to create or overwrite.\"},\"content\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Complete text content of the file.\"},\"overwrite\":{\"type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"Must be true if replacing an existing file.\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"content\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"edit_file\",\"description\":\"Perform a safe search-and-replace on a file. Replaces old_content with new_content and returns the diff.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Relative path to the file to edit.\"},\"old_content\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Exact snippet of text in the file to be replaced.\"},\"new_content\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The new replacement snippet.\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"old_content\",\"new_content\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"list_dir\",\"description\":\"List files and directories in the workspace, respecting .gitignore and ignoring hidden files.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Subdirectory to list (defaults to workspace root '.').\"},\"max_depth\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Maximum directory traversal depth (default: 3).\"}}}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"search_code\",\"description\":\"High-performance code search across the workspace (ripgrep speed). Respects .gitignore.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"query\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Search string or regex pattern to search for.\"},\"is_regex\":{\"type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"Whether query is a regular expression (default: false).\"},\"max_results\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Maximum number of matching lines to return (default: 50).\"},\"file_pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Optional regex to filter filenames (e.g. '\\\\.rs$' or '\\\\.ts$').\"}},\"required\":[\"query\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"description\":\"Execute a command in a Linux shell (bash, zsh, or sh) to run builds, tests, git, package managers, etc. Standard Unix commands only (ls, cat, grep, rm, etc.).\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"command\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The bash/zsh shell command to execute.\"},\"cwd\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Optional subdirectory to run the command in.\"},\"timeout_secs\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Execution timeout in seconds (default: 60).\"},\"shell\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Linux shell to use: 'bash', 'zsh', or 'sh' (default: 'bash').\"}},\"required\":[\"command\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"find_files\",\"description\":\"Quickly locate files matching a glob or substring pattern (e.g. '*.rs', '**/*.ts', 'auth'). Respects .gitignore.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Glob or substring pattern to search for.\"},\"max_results\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Maximum results to return (default: 50).\"}},\"required\":[\"pattern\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"search_symbols\",\"description\":\"Search for function, struct, class, interface, trait, or type declarations across the codebase (AST-level symbol search).\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"query\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Optional symbol name or substring to filter declarations.\"},\"max_results\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Maximum number of symbols to return (default: 50).\"}}}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"delete_file\",\"description\":\"Delete a file or directory inside the workspace.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Relative path to file or directory to remove.\"}},\"required\":[\"path\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"fetch_web\",\"description\":\"Fetch web content, documentation, or JSON API from an HTTP/HTTPS URL. Strips HTML markup.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"url\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The complete HTTP or HTTPS URL to fetch.\"},\"max_length\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Maximum character length to return (default: 15000).\"}},\"required\":[\"url\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"task_completed\",\"description\":\"Signal that the overall task is finished and report a comprehensive final summary of changes.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"summary\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Detailed summary of all changes made and outcomes achieved.\"},\"notes\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Any instructions, follow-up recommendations, or verification steps.\"}},\"required\":[\"summary\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"spawn_subagent\",\"description\":\"Spawn an isolated subagent with its own dedicated context to investigate code, search files, or verify implementations without cluttering the main conversation history.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"prompt\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The specific objective or question for the subagent to solve.\"},\"max_steps\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Maximum steps for the subagent to take (default: 8).\"}},\"required\":[\"prompt\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"file_info\",\"description\":\"Inspect detailed metadata of a file or directory (size in bytes, permissions, line count, binary check, modified timestamp).\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Relative path to the file or directory.\"}},\"required\":[\"path\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"batch_read\",\"description\":\"Read multiple files in parallel in a single turn to eliminate multi-turn round trips.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"paths\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"List of relative paths to files to read.\"},\"max_lines_per_file\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Maximum number of lines to read per file (default: 500).\"}},\"required\":[\"paths\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"file_tree\",\"description\":\"Render a hierarchical Unicode directory tree of the workspace, respecting .gitignore and ignoring hidden files.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Subdirectory to render tree from (default: '.').\"},\"max_depth\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Maximum tree depth to traverse (default: 3).\"}}}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"patch_file\",\"description\":\"Apply a standard unified diff patch or hunk to a file.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Relative path to the file to patch.\"},\"patch\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Unified diff or hunk content (including @@ headers or -/+ lines).\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"patch\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"update_plan\",\"description\":\"Create or update the structured multi-phase execution plan for the active task. Keeps user and agent aligned on milestones.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"phases\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"name\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Name or title of this execution phase.\"},\"status\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"pending\",\"in_progress\",\"completed\"],\"description\":\"Current status of the phase.\"},\"detail\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Optional details or sub-steps for this phase.\"}},\"required\":[\"name\",\"status\"]},\"description\":\"List of plan phases in chronological order.\"}},\"required\":[\"phases\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"activate_skill\",\"description\":\"Load the complete instructions, workflow, and guidelines of a specialized agent skill into active context.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"name\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The name of the skill to activate (e.g. 'graphify').\"}},\"required\":[\"name\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"run_tests\",\"description\":\"Auto-detect and run the project test suite (cargo test, npm test, pytest, make test) with parsed failures and compiler diagnostics.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"filter\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Optional test name filter or pattern to isolate specific unit tests.\"}}}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"search_web\",\"description\":\"Search the web for programming documentation, error messages, library APIs, and technical solutions.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"query\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The technical search query (e.g. 'rust axum json extraction example').\"},\"max_results\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Maximum number of search results to return (default: 5).\"}},\"required\":[\"query\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"lsp_hover\",\"description\":\"Query Language Server Protocol (LSP) hover documentation and type signatures for a symbol at a given line and character.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The source file path to inspect.\"},\"line\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"The 1-indexed line number.\"},\"character\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"The 1-indexed character offset on the line.\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"line\",\"character\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"lsp_definition\",\"description\":\"Query Language Server Protocol (LSP) definition location for a symbol at a given line and character.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The source file path containing the symbol reference.\"},\"line\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"The 1-indexed line number.\"},\"character\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"The 1-indexed character offset on the line.\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"line\",\"character\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"lsp_diagnostics\",\"description\":\"Retrieve active Language Server Protocol (LSP) semantic compiler diagnostics for a source file.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The source file path to query diagnostics for.\"}},\"required\":[\"path\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"git_status\",\"description\":\"Inspect native repository branch and staged/modified/untracked files via Rust libgit2 engine.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{}}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"git_diff\",\"description\":\"Generate unified diff of repository changes natively via Rust libgit2 engine.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"staged\":{\"type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"If true, diff staged changes against HEAD. Otherwise diff working directory.\"},\"path_filter\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Optional file path pattern to restrict diff to.\"}}}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"git_log\",\"description\":\"Inspect recent commit history (author, hash, summary, timestamp) natively via Rust libgit2 engine.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"max_commits\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Maximum number of commits to retrieve (default: 10).\"}}}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"cst_symbols\",\"description\":\"Parse symbols, multiline signatures, doc comments, visibility, and scopes using the Rust CST parser.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"File or directory path to parse.\"},\"query\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Optional symbol name filter.\"}},\"required\":[\"path\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"outline_file\",\"description\":\"Generate a compact AST skeleton outline of a source file (functions, classes, interfaces, signatures, and line numbers) to conserve context before reading specific line ranges.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Relative path to the source file to outline.\"}},\"required\":[\"path\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"trigram_search\",\"description\":\"Ultra-fast code search accelerated by Rust inverted trigram index.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"query\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Substring or token to search for across the codebase.\"},\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Optional subdirectory to restrict search to.\"},\"max_results\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Maximum matches to return (default: 50).\"}},\"required\":[\"query\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"hybrid_search\",\"description\":\"Perform hybrid code search blending dense semantic embeddings, sparse Okapi BM25, and Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF). Ideal for discovering code by intent or meaning when exact keyword tokens are unknown.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"query\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Natural language query or code concept to search for.\"},\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Optional relative directory path to scope search.\"},\"mode\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"hybrid\",\"semantic\",\"lexical\"],\"description\":\"Search mode: 'hybrid' (blended RRF, default), 'semantic' (vector embeddings), or 'lexical' (BM25 keyword).\"},\"limit\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Maximum matches to return (default: 10).\"}},\"required\":[\"query\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"browser_navigate\",\"description\":\"Navigate the headless browser to a local development server URL (e.g. http://localhost:3000), web page, or HTML file for runtime verification.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"url\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The complete HTTP/HTTPS URL or local HTML file path to load.\"}},\"required\":[\"url\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"browser_screenshot\",\"description\":\"Capture a viewport screenshot of the active browser page to verify frontend layout or UI state.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"output_path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Optional destination file path for screenshot PNG (defaults to .nexus/screenshots/).\"}}}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"browser_click\",\"description\":\"Click an interactive DOM element on the active browser page by CSS selector or element ID.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"selector\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"CSS selector of the element to click (e.g. '#submit-btn' or 'button.login').\"}},\"required\":[\"selector\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"browser_type\",\"description\":\"Type text into an input field or textarea on the active browser page.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"selector\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"CSS selector of target input element.\"},\"text\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Text to enter into the target field.\"}},\"required\":[\"selector\",\"text\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"browser_console_logs\",\"description\":\"Inspect browser console logs, warnings, and uncaught exceptions for frontend diagnostics.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"limit\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Maximum recent log entries to return (default: 50).\"}}}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"manage_knowledge\",\"description\":\"Query or record persistent project idioms, rules, dependencies, and architectural decisions.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"action\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"get\",\"set\",\"list\",\"delete\",\"query\"],\"description\":\"The knowledge operation to execute.\"},\"key\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Knowledge entry key identifier (e.g. 'preferred-package-manager').\"},\"value\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Value or rule description to persist.\"},\"category\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"idiom\",\"architecture\",\"dependency\",\"troubleshooting\",\"rule\"],\"description\":\"Classification category for the knowledge entry.\"}},\"required\":[\"action\"]}}}],\"system\":\"You are Nexus Code, an autonomous AI software engineering agent running in a Linux shell environment.\\nYou solve coding problems, build features, fix bugs, and refactor codebases by iteratively exploring, reading, editing, and verifying files.\\n\\n### Shell Environment:\\n- Active Shell: bash (standard GNU/Linux shell environment)\\n- Workspace directory: /tmp/tools-rlsFrE\\n\\n\\n\\n### Operating Rules:\\n1. EXPLORE FIRST: Before editing files, always explore the workspace using `file_tree`, `list_dir`, `find_files`, `search_code`, or `read_file`. For large files, use `outline_file` first to inspect class/function signatures without loading the entire file into context.\\n2. HIGH-EFFICIENCY BATCHING: Prefer `batch_read` to read multiple files concurrently in a single turn, and `file_info` to inspect metadata without loading whole files.\\n3. PRECISE EDITS & PATCHES: When modifying existing files, use `edit_file` with unique snippets or `patch_file` with unified diffs.\\n4. STRUCTURED PLANNING: For multi-step tasks, use `update_plan` to establish and advance through explicit milestone phases.\\n5. VERIFICATION: After making code changes, use `run_command` with bash/zsh commands to run tests, builds, or linting (e.g. `cargo check`, `cargo test`, `npm test`, `pytest`).\\n6. SELF-CORRECTION: If a command or tool returns an error, analyze the error message, identify the root cause, and fix it.\\n7. AUTONOMOUS COMPLETION: Keep executing tools until the entire task is thoroughly resolved. When everything is verified and done, invoke `task_completed` with a detailed summary.\\n\\n### Recommended Tool Usage Exemplar:\\nExample: Modifying a specific function using edit_file\\nModel:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"tool\\\": \\\"edit_file\\\",\\n  \\\"arguments\\\": {\\n    \\\"path\\\": \\\"src/utils.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"target_content\\\": \\\"export function add(a: number, b: number): number {\\\\n  return a - b;\\\\n}\\\",\\n    \\\"replacement_content\\\": \\\"export function add(a: number, b: number): number {\\\\n  return a + b;\\\\n}\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n\\nAlways explain your reasoning before or alongside your tool calls.\"}\n./docs/USER_MANUAL.md:225:- **Process Group Termination (REQ-AGT-109, REQ-SEC-106):** Cancellation terminates the entire process group (`killpg`) of in-flight commands: `SIGTERM` is sent immediately, followed by `SIGKILL` after a 2-second grace period. The turn reaches an idle state within 5 seconds.\n./docs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md:88:  - While this prevents accidental corruption, it relies entirely on the security of the GitHub repository release asset storage. If a GitHub token or account is compromised, the attacker could replace both the tarball and `SHA256SUMS`.\n./docs/CRED003_FLIGHTRECORDER_SANITIZATION_EVIDENCE.md:27:`FlightRecorder.appendEvent()` is the single event persistence boundary. It sanitizes the entire event payload before constructing and appending the JSON line. If classification/sanitization fails, it returns a safe `recordingSkipped` event result without writing that record or propagating classifier diagnostics; authorized local execution continues. Session metadata, prompts, thoughts, tool arguments, result snippets, errors, durable state, diffs, and arbitrary nested payload fields all pass through this boundary.\n./docs/PHASE4_IMPLEMENTATION_WORK_PACKAGES.md:1193:| **WP-11** | `cargo audit`, `npm audit`, pre-commit secret scan, license auditor, SBOM generator | Entire codebase & build artifacts | 0 High/Critical CVEs, 0 unapproved licenses, 100% clean pre-commit gate |\nb9da5bb59f0d3acdb3c14bac70a60e59848d206e34ec11408883029dc836936b  -\n{\"conclusion\":\"failure\",\"headSha\":\"37855d08d342412b6177baa9f30dd6a31d37d10e\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40871541877\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":415840362}},"started_at_ms":1793277475474,"completed_at_ms":1793277476891}}
