{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T12:43:54.424Z","ordinal":501416,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a187b0-34b8-7232-949f-3985a76d06ef","author":"/root/review_pr302","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_pr302\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — At final inspection, HEAD was `42b85729d4ca4dc552f8337538ffe7f24e85d843`, base `df288ef010a93c418e4972d3d40dc293ec9c0081`, and the current working-tree diff SHA-256 was `eea960aa40403f4b5ebc3f7c228f9514d28c9842dfd4927bac0e98602d1647f5`. This differs from the supplied `8170da…` hash.\n\nThe symlink-target mapping now masks targets within scanned system roots, including alternate mounted spellings. One bypass remains:\n\n- **P2 — External symlink targets can escape masking when mounted separately.** [isolate.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:549) scans only system directories and alternatives. If `/usr/bin/go` points to `/opt/toolchains/go`, `mountedSpellingsForTarget` returns no mask because `/opt/toolchains` is outside those roots. Candidate runtime paths are mounted later ([isolate.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:583)). With `/opt/toolchains` included in `sandboxRuntimePaths`, candidate code can still execute the unpinned compiler through `/usr/bin/go`. Include additional mounted runtime paths in exposure mapping or fail closed on unmasked compiler symlinks; add a regression for this case.\n\nI ran no tests or edits."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","create_time":1793277834.424168,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":23386}}
