{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T12:52:53.580Z","ordinal":502001,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-b197665d-e103-4c17-9a90-88215f862cc9","process_id":"30336","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/V1_HELDOUT_CORPUS_CUSTODY_20261028/owner.json 2>/dev/null; cat docs/v1.0.0/README.md | head -100; sed -n '1,180p' docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.11.md; gh release list --limit 10; git tag --list 'v1.0.0*' --sort=-creatordate | head -10"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/V1_HELDOUT_CORPUS_CUSTODY_20261028/owner.json 2>/dev/null; cat docs/v1.0.0/README.md | head -100; sed -n '1,180p' docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.11.md; gh release list --limit 10; git tag --list 'v1.0.0*' --sort=-creatordate | head -10"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"agent\":\"kimi-code\",\"branch\":\"v1/qualify-all-accepted-v9\",\"since\":\"2026-10-28T23:42:27Z\",\"pid\":2827782,\"scope\":\"held-out corpus compatibility and custody handoff; no payload exposure\"}\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0: audit and planning package\n\nThis package is the evidence-based path from `v0.1.0-alpha.2` (audited at `db1ca55`, 2026-10-14) to v1.0.0.\n\n**Verdict: v1.0.0 readiness is BLOCKED.** Candidate source revision `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` passed an isolated `make build` and full `make test` run on 2026-10-16 (Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087; zero skipped). This is source-suite evidence, not RC qualification. Held-out task quality, T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider qualification, the manual terminal matrix, package/install matrix on the RC, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete. See [the current readiness reconciliation](READINESS.md) for exact open requirements and gates. The contest entry remains a separate track; judging has concluded and no contest freeze applies.\n\n## How to read it\n\n| If you want to… | Read |\n|---|---|\n| Understand what Nexus is today, what was examined, and what is wrong | [AUDIT.md](AUDIT.md) |\n| See current release readiness and remaining actions | [READINESS.md](READINESS.md) |\n| See every requirement (historical and new), its status, blocker class, and how it is accepted | [REQUIREMENTS.md](REQUIREMENTS.md) |\n| Know the order of work, the effort, and the critical path | [ROADMAP.md](ROADMAP.md) |\n| Implement a workstream | Its spec in [specs/](specs/), then its plan in [plans/](plans/) |\n| Qualify a release candidate | [ACCEPTANCE.md](ACCEPTANCE.md) |\n| Check what was actually run and what it proves | [EVIDENCE.md](EVIDENCE.md) and [evidence/](evidence/) |\n| See the decisions taken (all resolved under delegated owner authority) and the remaining owner actions | [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md) |\n| Run several agents on this plan at once without collisions | [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) (also referenced from the root `AGENTS.md`) |\n\n## Workstreams\n\n| # | Workstream | Spec | Plan | Milestone | Blockers |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 01 | Safe execution defaults and approval integrity | [SPEC-01](specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | [PLAN-01](plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | M1 | SEC-101, 102, 103, 119 |\n| 02 | Process ownership, cancellation, resource bounds | [SPEC-02](specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | [PLAN-02](plans/PLAN-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | M1 | AGT-109, SEC-106 |\n| 03 | Untrusted workspace inputs and egress boundary | [SPEC-03](specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | [PLAN-03](plans/PLAN-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | M1 | SEC-110, 111, 115, 116 |\n| 04 | Continuity, resume, durable work units | [SPEC-04](specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | [PLAN-04](plans/PLAN-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | M3 | AGT-101, 102 |\n| 05 | Standalone local inference and provider robustness | [SPEC-05](specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | [PLAN-05](plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | M3/M5 | PRV-101, 102, 106 |\n| 06 | Packaged product parity, launcher, versioning, doctor | [SPEC-06](specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | [PLAN-06](plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | M0/M2 | REL-101, 102, 103 |\n| 07 | Supply chain, compliance, release engineering | [SPEC-07](specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | [PLAN-07](plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | M2 | REL-107 |\n| 08 | Persistence hygiene | [SPEC-08](specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md) | [PLAN-08](plans/PLAN-08-persistence-hygiene.md) | M0/M4 | (prerequisite: PER-103) |\n| 09 | Requirements governance and documentation truth | [SPEC-09](specs/SPEC-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md) | [PLAN-09](plans/PLAN-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md) | M0/M6 | OPS-101, 103 |\n| 10 | v1 qualification and evaluation | [SPEC-10](specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | [PLAN-10](plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | M3/M5 | QUAL-101 to 107 |\n| 11 | Verification and tool-call integrity | [SPEC-11](specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md) | [PLAN-11](plans/PLAN-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md) | M1/M3 | AGT-112, 113, 114 |\n| 12 | In-place CLI and TUI upgrade | [SPEC-12](specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) | [PLAN-12](plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) | M2 | REL-115 |\n| C1 | Contest (separate product; post-contest maintenance; no freeze applies) | [SPEC-C1](specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md) | [PLAN-C1](plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md) | post-contest | — (not a client gate) |\n\n\n## How to execute\n\n0. If more than one agent (or person) will implement in parallel, read [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) first. It covers slice claims, worktrees, hot files, the gateway lock and merge order.\n1. **Start with M0** (ROADMAP). Merge PLAN-08 PR-8a first, so that test runs stop writing into the real `~/.nexus`. Then land PLAN-06 PR-6a (version sync) and PLAN-09 PR-9a (ledger checker, historical banners, cheap doc fixes).\n2. **M1 is the critical path.** Work through PLAN-01, PLAN-02, PLAN-03 and PLAN-11 PR-11a/b in the PR slices listed. Each plan names its safe change boundary, code locations, tests and rollback.\n3. **For every PR:**\n   - update the matching REQUIREMENTS rows (status, test reference, commit);\n   - keep `scripts/check_requirements.mjs` green;\n   - run `make test` on a snapshot copy, never while editing (tasks/lessons.md).\n4. M2 and M4 run in parallel with M1/M3. Held-out task authoring (agent-authored, as authorised) and the standalone proxy start during M1.\n5. Cut `v1.0.0-rc.1` only when G0–G4 pass. Then run ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 against the **installed** RC.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- **Requirement IDs.** `REQ-<AREA>-0xx` marks a commitment carried over from history. `REQ-<AREA>-1xx` marks a new v1 requirement.\n- **Finding IDs.** These are owned by the scoped evidence files: AGT, VER, PRV, SEC, PER, TUI, REL, DX, MNT, HIST, EVL, CON, PERF, DOC.\n- **Acceptance IDs.** `ACC-<AREA>-NN`. Each is defined in its spec, or in ACCEPTANCE §3.1.\n- **Evidence labels.** SRC, TEST, RT, MEAS, DOC, HIST, INF, UNV (REQUIREMENTS §1).\n- **Status ladder.** open → partial → implemented → tested → visually-accepted → product-qualified. Independent acceptance is recorded separately.\n\nThis package supersedes the Issue #12 matrices and the PHASE and WP documents as the source of current requirements. Those documents remain as historical record.\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.11 release candidate\n\n**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\n\n**Status:** this candidate is for exact-artifact qualification. It does not establish independent acceptance or authorize stable v1.0.0 promotion. Qualification results must identify the workflow-produced package and its digest. No successor-RC qualification has been run yet.\n\nThis release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`. It is a version-only candidate built from current `main`; it contains the post-RC10 source changes below.\n\n## Changes since RC10\n\n### Durable operations\n\n- **Test-first work units (opt-in):** `NEXUS_TDD=1` (or `AgentWorkUnitExecutor({ tdd: true })`) runs implementer units as a RED turn that must record a failing, executed verifier and a changed test, then a GREEN turn. RED evidence is a private sidecar keyed by the unit task and prompt; the verifier baseline is rebased only onto the added tests, and a RED that narrows the operator's tests or verifier is refused. See `docs/v1.0.0/TDD-WORK-UNITS.md`.\n- **Read-only operation view:** `nexus operation status --dag [--json]` and `nexus operation watch` project the unit DAG, resource eligibility, open decisions and the event tail without taking the operation lock or writing a transition. Operation text is sanitised for terminal control sequences. See `docs/v1.1.0/OPERATION_OBSERVABILITY.md`.\n- **Git-aware isolated operations (opt-in):** `spec.git = { isolate: true, baseRef? }` gives each unit its own worktree and branch, integrates completions into an operation branch with receipts, re-verifies the merged tree, and blocks with `MERGE_CONFLICT` / `INTEGRATION_FAILED` decisions. Recovery is idempotent and fails closed when integration history is missing or rewritten. See `docs/v1.1.0/GIT_AWARE_OPERATIONS.md`.\n- **Per-unit context budget and checkpoints:** `units[].contextBudget` blocks a unit before inference when the operator's cap is the binding limit and offers to lift it; `nexus operation checkpoint|checkpoints|restore` snapshots a unit's task state and conversation journals as a hash-verified bundle, with a pre-restore backup. See `docs/v1.1.0/CONTEXT_MANAGEMENT.md`.\n- **Operation policy configuration:** durable operation policy defaults can be set in the operator config; scheduler and runner internals were split (scheduler extraction, runner decomposition) with bounded diagnostics, and recovered merged operations now require verification evidence.\n\n### Reliability and security\n\n- Checkpoint restore is fail-closed on content mismatch; incomplete or duplicate checkpoint bundles are reused/cleaned correctly, and restoring a conversation removes stale journals.\n- Configured Git hooks are guarded consistently for checkpoint and retention operations, including a fail-closed race path.\n- Malformed operator configuration is reported by `nexus doctor` with recovery guidance instead of an unhandled failure.\n- Clean-checkout build identity is recorded correctly, and packaged smoke startup no longer races its log.\n- CLI terminal output sanitises control characters in corrupt-resume errors; batch read paths preserve lossy UTF-8 and propagate read errors instead of continuing.\n- Credential handling: malformed credential origins can no longer be rebound, and credential-store writes are failure-atomic under the file guard.\n- Recovery: pre-fix worktree tasks are recovered from the repository root, and upgrades recover state from the configured state directory.\n- Tooling: `update_plan` no longer mutates the workspace, and ambiguous Python verifier imports are rejected.\n- CI provisions the pinned evaluator toolchains for the qualification suites.\n\n### Release records\n\n- Readiness, terminal and qualification records were refreshed through 2026-10-29. The manual real-terminal matrix is **required** for v1.0.0; the earlier matrix-waiver record was withdrawn (DEC-19). Screenshot artifacts alone are waived (DEC-18).\n\n## Runtime requirements\n\n- Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer.\n- Node.js 22 or newer.\n- An OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint, local or explicitly selected provider.\n\nThe archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\n\n## Candidate assets\n\nThe release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.11` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\n\n## Qualification status\n\nThis is a candidate, not an accepted release. The installed-RC gates — platform and lifecycle evidence, the fifteen-cell manual terminal matrix, provider and standalone qualification, held-out task quality, cross-runner reproducibility, independent exact-RC acceptance and the requirements ledger — remain outstanding for this artifact. Passing source CI does not satisfy them.\nv1.0.0-rc.10\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.10\t2026-10-27T00:29:58Z\nv1.0.0-rc.9\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.9\t2026-10-26T17:56:16Z\nv1.0.0-rc.8\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.8\t2026-10-26T07:26:22Z\nv1.0.0-rc.7\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.7\t2026-10-26T00:07:06Z\nv1.0.0-rc.6\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.6\t2026-10-25T17:25:56Z\nv1.0.0-rc.5\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.5\t2026-10-25T12:58:55Z\nv1.0.0-rc.4\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.4\t2026-10-24T11:54:37Z\nv1.0.0-rc.3\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.3\t2026-10-23T09:06:11Z\nv1.0.0-rc.1\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.1\t2026-10-21T18:54:41Z\nv0.1.0-alpha.2\tPre-release\tv0.1.0-alpha.2\t2026-10-14T09:10:47Z\nv1.0.0-rc.10\nv1.0.0-rc.9\nv1.0.0-rc.8\nv1.0.0-rc.7\nv1.0.0-rc.6\nv1.0.0-rc.5\nv1.0.0-rc.4\nv1.0.0-rc.3\nv1.0.0-rc.2\nv1.0.0-rc.1\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":417455424}},"started_at_ms":1793278372162,"completed_at_ms":1793278373580}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T12:52:53.696Z","ordinal":502002,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a187b8-6f3f-7de2-9f64-bfc4e9b1a6c1","call_id":"call_720173dd133344a399c3e91ebc68cd72","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 3095)\nTotal output lines: 130\n\n{\"agent\":\"kimi-code\",\"branch\":\"v1/qualify-all-accepted-v9\",\"since\":\"2026-10-28T23:42:27Z\",\"pid\":2827782,\"scope\":\"held-out corpus compatibility and custody handoff; no payload exposure\"}\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0: audit and planning package\n\nThis package is the evidence-based path from `v0.1.0-alpha.2` (audited at `db1ca55`, 2026-10-14) to v1.0.0.\n\n**Verdict: v1.0.0 readiness is BLOCKED.** Candidate source revision `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` passed an isolated `make build` and full `make test` run on 2026-10-16 (Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087; zero skipped). This is source-suite evidence, not RC qualification. Held-out task quality, T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider qualification, the manual terminal matrix, package/install matrix on the RC, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete. See [the current readiness reconciliation](READINESS.md) for exact open requirements and gates. The contest entry remains a separate track; judging has concluded and no contest freeze applies.\n\n## How to read it\n\n| If you want to… | Read |\n|---|---|\n| Understand what Nexus is today, what was examined, and what is wrong | [AUDIT.md](AUDIT.md) |\n| See current release readiness and remaining actions | [READINESS.md](READINESS.md) |\n| See every requirement (historical and new), its status, blocker class, and how it is accepted | [REQUIREMENTS.md](REQUIREMENTS.md) |\n| Know the order of work, the effort, and the critical path | [ROADMAP.md](ROADMAP.md) |\n| Implement a workstream | Its spec in [specs/](specs/), then its plan in [plans/](plans/) |\n| Qualify a release candidate | [ACCEPTANCE.md](ACCEPTANCE.md) |\n| Check what was actually run and what it proves | [EVIDENCE.md](EVIDENCE.md) and [evidence/](evidence/) |\n| See the decisions taken (all resolved under delegated owner authority) and the remaining owner actions | [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md) |\n| Run several agents on this plan at once without collisions | [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) (also referenced from the root `AGENTS.md`) |\n\n## Workstreams\n\n| # | Workstream | Spec | Plan | Milestone | Blockers |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 01 | Safe execution defaults and approval integrity | [SPEC-01](specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | [PLAN-01](plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | M1 | SEC-101, 102, 103, 119 |\n| 02 | Process ownership, cancellation, resource bounds | [SPEC-02](specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | [PLAN-02](plans/PLAN-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | M1 | AGT-109, SEC-106 |\n| 03 | Untrusted workspace inputs and egress boundary | [SPEC-03](specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | [PLAN-03](plans/PLAN-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | M1 | SEC-110, 111, 115, 116 |\n| 04 | Continuity, resume, durable work units | [SPEC-04](specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | [PLAN-04](plans/PLAN-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | M3 | AGT-101, 102 |\n| 05 | Standalone local inference and provider robustness | [SPEC-05](specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | [PLAN-05](plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | M3/M5 | PRV-101, 102, 106 |\n| 06 | Packaged product parity, launcher, versioning, doctor | [SPEC-06](specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | [PLAN-06](plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | M0/M2 | REL-101, 102, 103 |\n| 07 | Supply chain, compliance, release engineering | [SPEC-07](specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | [PLAN-07](plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | M2 | REL-107 |\n| 08 | Persistence hygiene | [SPEC-08](specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md) | [PLAN-08](plans/PLAN-08-persistence-hygiene.md) | M0/M4 | (prerequisite: PER-103) |\n| 09 | Requirements governance and documentation truth | [SPEC-09](specs/SPEC-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md) | [PLAN-09](plans/PLAN-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md) | M0/M6 | OPS-101, 103 |\n| 10 | v1 qualification and evaluation | [SPEC-10](specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | [PLAN-10](plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | M3/M5 | QUAL-101 to 107 |\n| 11 | Verification and tool-call integrity | [SPEC-11](specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md) | [PLAN-11](plans/PLAN-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md) | M1/M3 | AGT-112, 113, 114 |\n| 12 | In-place CLI and TUI upgrade | [SPEC-12](specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) | [PLAN-12](plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) | M2 | REL-115 |\n| C1 | Contest (separate product; post-contest maintenance; no freeze applies) | [SPEC-C1](specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md) | [PLAN-C1](plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md) | post-contest | — (not a client gate) |\n\n\n## How to execute\n\n0. If more than one agent (or person) will implement in parallel, read [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) first. It covers slice claims, worktrees, hot files, the gateway lock and merge order.\n1. **Start with M0** (ROADMAP). Merge PLAN-08 PR-8a first, so that test runs stop writing into the real `~/.nexus`. Then land PLAN-06…595 tokens truncated…hat must record a failing, executed verifier and a changed test, then a GREEN turn. RED evidence is a private sidecar keyed by the unit task and prompt; the verifier baseline is rebased only onto the added tests, and a RED that narrows the operator's tests or verifier is refused. See `docs/v1.0.0/TDD-WORK-UNITS.md`.\n- **Read-only operation view:** `nexus operation status --dag [--json]` and `nexus operation watch` project the unit DAG, resource eligibility, open decisions and the event tail without taking the operation lock or writing a transition. Operation text is sanitised for terminal control sequences. See `docs/v1.1.0/OPERATION_OBSERVABILITY.md`.\n- **Git-aware isolated operations (opt-in):** `spec.git = { isolate: true, baseRef? }` gives each unit its own worktree and branch, integrates completions into an operation branch with receipts, re-verifies the merged tree, and blocks with `MERGE_CONFLICT` / `INTEGRATION_FAILED` decisions. Recovery is idempotent and fails closed when integration history is missing or rewritten. See `docs/v1.1.0/GIT_AWARE_OPERATIONS.md`.\n- **Per-unit context budget and checkpoints:** `units[].contextBudget` blocks a unit before inference when the operator's cap is the binding limit and offers to lift it; `nexus operation checkpoint|checkpoints|restore` snapshots a unit's task state and conversation journals as a hash-verified bundle, with a pre-restore backup. See `docs/v1.1.0/CONTEXT_MANAGEMENT.md`.\n- **Operation policy configuration:** durable operation policy defaults can be set in the operator config; scheduler and runner internals were split (scheduler extraction, runner decomposition) with bounded diagnostics, and recovered merged operations now require verification evidence.\n\n### Reliability and security\n\n- Checkpoint restore is fail-closed on content mismatch; incomplete or duplicate checkpoint bundles are reused/cleaned correctly, and restoring a conversation removes stale journals.\n- Configured Git hooks are guarded consistently for checkpoint and retention operations, including a fail-closed race path.\n- Malformed operator configuration is reported by `nexus doctor` with recovery guidance instead of an unhandled failure.\n- Clean-checkout build identity is recorded correctly, and packaged smoke startup no longer races its log.\n- CLI terminal output sanitises control characters in corrupt-resume errors; batch read paths preserve lossy UTF-8 and propagate read errors instead of continuing.\n- Credential handling: malformed credential origins can no longer be rebound, and credential-store writes are failure-atomic under the file guard.\n- Recovery: pre-fix worktree tasks are recovered from the repository root, and upgrades recover state from the configured state directory.\n- Tooling: `update_plan` no longer mutates the workspace, and ambiguous Python verifier imports are rejected.\n- CI provisions the pinned evaluator toolchains for the qualification suites.\n\n### Release records\n\n- Readiness, terminal and qualification records were refreshed through 2026-10-29. The manual real-terminal matrix is **required** for v1.0.0; the earlier matrix-waiver record was withdrawn (DEC-19). Screenshot artifacts alone are waived (DEC-18).\n\n## Runtime requirements\n\n- Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer.\n- Node.js 22 or newer.\n- An OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint, local or explicitly selected provider.\n\nThe archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\n\n## Candidate assets\n\nThe release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.11` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\n\n## Qualification status\n\nThis is a candidate, not an accepted release. The installed-RC gates — platform and lifecycle evidence, the fifteen-cell manual terminal matrix, provider and standalone qualification, held-out task quality, cross-runner reproducibility, independent exact-RC acceptance and the requirements ledger — remain outstanding for this artifact. Passing source CI does not satisfy them.\nv1.0.0-rc.10\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.10\t2026-10-27T00:29:58Z\nv1.0.0-rc.9\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.9\t2026-10-26T17:56:16Z\nv1.0.0-rc.8\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.