{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T12:53:40.262Z","ordinal":502053,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8df7d562-da04-4e44-85c1-ec6f169e2b8b","process_id":"26412","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 318 --json title,body,url"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 318 --json title,body,url"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/33/changes/nexus-code/33\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n- Bind only pinned Go and Rust toolchains into the evaluator and candidate namespace, with root ownership, symlink, resolved-path, and write-permission checks.\\n- Extend the synthetic evaluator coverage for toolchain availability and unsafe roots.\\n- Build the synthetic Rust oracle with `cargo --locked --offline`, so the read-only candidate workspace is not modified.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- Isolated CLI build passed on an immutable snapshot.\\n- `cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts`: 31 passed, 0 failed on the built snapshot.\\n- Focused toolchain regressions: 2 passed, 0 failed.\\n- `git diff --check` passed.\\n\\nNo held-out corpus tasks or payloads were used.\\n\",\"title\":\"fix(eval): bind pinned toolchains read-only\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/318\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":330484741}},"started_at_ms":1793278418931,"completed_at_ms":1793278420262}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T12:53:40.405Z","ordinal":502054,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a187b9-25b5-7840-b09d-129d3ea06fae","call_id":"call_1471aa81314b4269ae683b84e79d2e15","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"body\":\"<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/33/changes/nexus-code/33\\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n- Bind only pinned Go and Rust toolchains into the evaluator and candidate namespace, with root ownership, symlink, resolved-path, and write-permission checks.\\n- Extend the synthetic evaluator coverage for toolchain availability and unsafe roots.\\n- Build the synthetic Rust oracle with `cargo --locked --offline`, so the read-only candidate workspace is not modified.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- Isolated CLI build passed on an immutable snapshot.\\n- `cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts`: 31 passed, 0 failed on the built snapshot.\\n- Focused toolchain regressions: 2 passed, 0 failed.\\n- `git diff --check` passed.\\n\\nNo held-out corpus tasks or payloads were used.\\n\",\"title\":\"fix(eval): bind pinned toolchains read-only\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/318\"}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","create_time":1793278420.4057088}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
