{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T12:55:30.767Z","ordinal":502113,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae3423fc3dc819f8e469597b58c368b","usage":{"input_tokens":222329,"cached_input_tokens":221696,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":275,"reasoning_output_tokens":120,"total_tokens":222604},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":71969185,"cached_input_tokens":71025536,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":185369,"reasoning_output_tokens":117474,"total_tokens":72154554},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9396086985,"cached_input_tokens":9295723264,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":27217675,"reasoning_output_tokens":15980687,"total_tokens":9423304660}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T12:55:31.732Z","ordinal":502114,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f9428370-3bd2-4423-8cc6-d2a8d4df0f56","process_id":"98889","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n '^##|^###|\\bBLOCKED\\b|\\bPASS\\b|\\bOPEN\\b|RC11|held-out|custody|provider|terminal|T3|T4|cross-runner|independent|authorization' docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md docs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | head -110;"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n '^##|''^###|'\"\\\\bBLOCKED\\\\b|\\\\bPASS\\\\b|\\\\bOPEN\\\\b|RC11|held-out|custody|provider|terminal|T3|T4|cross-runner|independent|authorization\" docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md docs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","query":"^##|^###|\\bBLOCKED\\b|\\bPASS\\b|\\bOPEN\\b|RC11|held-out|custody|provider|terminal|T3|T4|cross-runner|independent|authorization","path":"READINESS.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:20:## 1.1 Release-candidate lifecycle and evidence identity\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:25:2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:32:Exact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:37:### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:42:| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:46:| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:47:| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:48:| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:49:| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:50:| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:52:| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:56:### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:62:## 1. Rules\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:75:## 2. Environments\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:81:| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:82:| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:83:| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:85:## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:104:### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:114:| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:118:| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:119:| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:120:| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | All 15 cells have actual manual execution, recorded PASS/FAIL verdicts, observed outcomes, and evidence bound to the exact installed RC. Automated §5.1 and §5.2 do not substitute for these cells. Screenshot artifacts alone are waived by DEC-18. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:123:## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:125:### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:138:### 4.2 Standalone matrix\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:142:| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:150:### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:154:| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:155:| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:156:| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:159:## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:161:### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:176:### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:190:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:192:**Required for v1.0.0.** Run every terminal × size combination below against the exact installed RC and record a verdict and observed outcomes for each cell. Automated suites in §5.1 and §5.2 remain required but do not replace operator execution. DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts only. See [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:194:Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:196:For each terminal × size, check:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:203:6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:206:Record PASS/FAIL per cell and the observed outcomes for each check, bound to the exact installed RC artifact, terminal environment, and size. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver); this does not waive any interactive check, safety gate, per-cell verdict, or evidence record.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:210:## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:214:### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:219:- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:235:### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:249:### 6.3 T3 long tasks (ACC-QUAL-T3)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:253:### 6.4 Thresholds (DEC-05; all must hold)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:257:| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:262:| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:263:| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:264:| T3 false-absence | = 0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:265:| T3 false-presence | = 0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:266:| T3 steering honoured | ≥ 95% |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:271:## 7. Install, upgrade, rollback, uninstall (ACC-PLAT; E2)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:282:| Attestation | `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` | PASS |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:288:## 8. Independent acceptance (REQ-AGT-110, ACC-CONT-10)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:302:1. An independent re-run of a sample. At minimum:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:310:   - 2 T4 classes.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:314:**Output:** `docs/reviews/<date>-v1-rc-independent-acceptance.md` with an ACCEPT, ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS, or REJECT verdict per area. \"Accept with defects\" needs an owner disposition for every defect, and for a blocker area the only acceptable disposition is a fix.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:316:## 9. Contest (separate product; not a client gate)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:329:## 10. Release decision (G6)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:335:- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:336:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI and scripted gates PASS, and all 15 manual real-terminal cells have verified operator evidence. DEC-18 waives screenshots only.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:338:- [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:339:- [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:343:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:345:- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:348:After G6, complete source checks on the exact stable-version commit before tagging, then complete the stable artifact checks in §1.1 stage 5 before publishing the draft. A failure keeps publication blocked and requires remediation plus the applicable requalification; do not mark the campaign released until published artifacts are independently verified.\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:18:## 1. Build and runtime identity\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:28:| Live cloud client | Checkout build `db1ca55` (`/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/dist`), using the operator's existing provider connections: ChatGPT via the Codex CLI sign-in; OpenRouter via the crush credential. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:30:## 2. Baseline build and test runs\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:35:| B2 | `<scratch>/clone` (git, `db1ca55`), CI order: release build before CLI tests | `npm ci`; build; `cargo test --locked`; `cargo build --locked --release --bin harness-core --bin nexus-tui`; `npm test`; `security_gates.sh`, 12:42–13:06 UTC | **Rust 266/266, CLI 905/905, security gates PASS**, working tree clean afterwards. CLI suite duration 1,169 s. | `evidence/baseline/baseline2.log` |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:42:## 3. Live runs (owner-authorized small spend, 2026-10-14, on `db1ca55`)\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:46:| L1 | `nexus providers verify --provider chatgpt -m gpt-6-luna -j` | PASS: streamed completion, tool call, tool-result round trip | `8e910140…`, `1e6c5946…`, `d8595745…` | `evidence/live/verify_chatgpt.json` |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:47:| L2 | `nexus providers verify --provider openrouter -m openrouter/free -j` | PASS. The effective model varied per request (nemotron-3-super, then laguna-xs-2.1, then laguna-s-2.1), which shows `openrouter/free` is unsuitable for matched evaluation. | `49b71fc3…`, `b05711f6…`, `2b9cc6c5…` | `evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json` |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:52:## 4. Scoped audit evidence\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:58:| `evidence/B_providers.md` | Providers and inference | `prv/{probe,tls,err}.mts` against 127.0.0.1 mocks; 125/125 targeted tests |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:60:| `evidence/D_terminal.md` + `evidence/D_pty/` | Terminal | Real-PTY scripts s1–s9 and r1a–r1d against `mockgw.py`; `pyte` screen dumps |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:68:## 5. Side effects of the audit (disclosed)\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:71:2. **Live provider receipts** were written to `<scratch>/live/.nexus/` and `<scratch>/live/ws1/.nexus/`, not to the repository.\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:85:## 6. What must be re-run after implementation\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:95:## 7. Limitations of the conclusions\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:97:- **No product qualification exists.** \"Blocked\" is established, from reproduced defects. \"Qualified\" cannot be: there is no held-out, fault-injection or standalone evidence, and the tasks used in the historical pilot were tuned.\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:104:- **Independence:** this audit is one reviewer's evidence pass, assisted by scoped sub-audits from the same reviewer. It is **not** an independent acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:106:## 8. Artifact hashes\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:3:## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 06:18 UTC)\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:9:**Open source changes:** PR [#319](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/319), head `668721d8135d3a3332bca27b820caa5a4a76c7af`, merged as `a0356c4d8f0f0b9b943d4033aff59795fcab83b4` after its independent `ACCEPT` review and required Node 22/24/Linux, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks passed. Its post-merge CI and CodeQL checks are running. PR [#318](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/318), head `2c532d701c5b84b0d3308b02897520337addc36b`, has independent `ACCEPT` source review, but both Node matrix jobs failed because `eval_hardened.test.ts` could not find `go` while testing hidden-source isolation (exit 127); Linux was skipped. This is a CI toolchain-provisioning gap, not evaluator qualification evidence. PR [#322](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/322), head `d53caea7c480c5e88dff43c6e5d4cb8a16868400`, adds CI-only pinned Go/Rust toolchain provisioning and has independent `ACCEPT` review; its Node 22/24, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks pass, with Linux still running. PR [#320](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/320), head `2124538d21b84454319c5485140b266f11510a5a`, has independent `ACCEPT` review and passing Node 22/24, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks; Linux remains in progress. PR [#321](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/321) refreshes this checkpoint and has been rebased onto the new main; the previous head's checks do not qualify the rebased candidate, which requires fresh exact-head checks and independent review. None of PRs #318, #320, #321 or #322 is merged.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:11:**Held-out custody and qualification:** The latest public metadata update on issue #1 (06:02 UTC) records unresolved custody ownership: a historical handoff log names SageBridge as an accepted successor, while the active custody record still names OpenCode. The latest posted T2 count is 20/40 tasks; no new custody acceptance or qualification result is recorded. T3's reported 8/8 covers digest/schema/isolation metadata, not task-quality qualification. The custodian identity and acknowledged transfer must be reconciled before qualification. No private payloads were accessed by implementation work. T2/T3/T4 held-out qualification, standalone/provider acceptance, long-task/fault-injection qualification, and successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility remain incomplete.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:13:**Terminal and release gates:** Acceptance §5.3 requires actual operator execution for xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. There are **0/15 accepted cells**. The operator's partial RC10 report says the client rendered at tested sizes except tmux inside GNOME Terminal, which could not be resized below 43×13; other results “seemed okay.” The report lacks test time, exact installed artifact identity, terminal versions, and per-cell check outcomes, so it does not complete any cell. Automated PTY results do not count. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` has the required terminal programs; the successor RC is not yet available for the matrix. Screenshots are waived by DEC-18 only; all interactive checks and per-cell verdicts remain mandatory under DEC-19. The latest public release is `v1.0.0-rc.10`; the selected distribution target is the GitHub installer, not npm. No stable `v1.0.0` release exists.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:15:**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Publication authorization remains granted but gated on complete mandatory acceptance. PR #319 is integrated; main post-merge CI is running. PRs #320 and #322 are in exact-head Linux validation, PR #321 is rebased with fresh checks pending, and PR #318 needs the toolchain change integrated and its exact-base qualification rerun. Exact-RC construction and qualification remain gated on pre-RC source readiness and complete independent custody acceptance; terminal operator evidence is still required before independent RC acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:17:## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 04:23 UTC; superseded)\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:23:**Candidate convergence:** PR #311 remains open at `742d00871c311d6829e8a4d0a1a3a1800701b954` on the older base `cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e`; its prior Node 22/24, Linux x86_64 and CodeQL checks passed, but they do not qualify 