{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T13:06:57.894Z","ordinal":502439,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae344f00d48819fbb744cad8aed7633","usage":{"input_tokens":70094,"cached_input_tokens":65536,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":77,"reasoning_output_tokens":60,"total_tokens":70171},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":82099896,"cached_input_tokens":81119360,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":198598,"reasoning_output_tokens":124848,"total_tokens":82298494},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9406217696,"cached_input_tokens":9305817088,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":27230904,"reasoning_output_tokens":15988061,"total_tokens":9433448600}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T13:06:57.915Z","ordinal":502440,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a187c5-50fa-7de3-a847-b21a6b5dfd73","call_id":"call_94850e07b3104e079e376c281eaed619","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr311_draft_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — exact four-file diff SHA-256: `56ab8a3ecef2ada575aacd09e3e5148948fb6b013640c92b071d11598a629184`.\\n\\nPinned toolchain roots and their contents are checked for root ownership, canonical paths, and write/symlink safety before use. Candidate and Python oracle mounts are read-only; oracle launches clear the environment, use offline Go/Rust settings and temporary caches, and refuse protected-corpus overlap. The fixtures cover unsafe roots, production launch paths, and Go/Rust execution.\\n\\n**Independence note:** I previously reviewed related evaluator-toolchain and provisioning changes, so this is a fresh review of the exact candidate, but should not be represented as fully independent of those earlier reviews. No tests run.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr300_readiness\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**CHANGES_REQUIRED** for PR #323. Its exact head is `ea7b728c70ba05d7ff106c14c0adffd99e6012a5`; the diff SHA-256 is `535d7f5244de1708f2e90931bcf730002d341ea15fb241ae2d196805e734c872`.\\n\\nThe six changed files are synchronized RC11 version metadata and the new release notes. The notes accurately preserve the outstanding qualification gates and DEC-18/DEC-19 terminal requirements.\\n\\nThe toolchain statement in `docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.11.md:29` overstates what this candidate enforces. CI provisions toolchain directories, but the current evaluator source still dynamically selects Go and Rust toolchains; PR #318, which adds fail-closed pinned-toolchain enforcement, remains open.\\n\\nNode 22/24, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks pass. Linux and Entire Gates are still running. After correcting the statement, the PR may be considered for merge once all required exact-head checks and independent review pass.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr302\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — HEAD `42b85729d4ca4dc552f8337538ffe7f24e85d843`, base `df288ef010a93c418e4972d3d40dc293ec9c0081`.\\n\\nThe incremental diff SHA-256 is `5bd02b29f99350e92f1e4c54c5358c6fb3b0b73a1d392af333eb4bcfda4f610f`; the cumulative base-to-working-tree SHA-256 is `5f00cefa97d4356ce825c5c6087126fd9c593f0776cb082bf8929266586c224d`.\\n\\nThe scanner now includes explicitly mounted runtime paths, maps compiler targets to every mounted spelling, and appends `/dev/null` masks after those runtime mounts. Scan errors fail closed. The new fixture covers an external mounted compiler target, an alternate root, and mask ordering.\\n\\nRead-only review; I ran no tests.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","create_time":1793279217.9149675}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
