":\"test-matrix (24)\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"steps\":[]}],\"status\":\"in_progress\"}\n{\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"headSha\":\"76c9bfe8e509b00e85611b684d53d135f4917366\",\"jobs\":[{\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"name\":\"javascript-typescript\",\"status\":\"completed\"}],\"status\":\"completed\"}\nCodeQL\tcompleted\tsuccess\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/123466164171\nEntire Gates\tin_progress\t\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/123465474933\ntest-matrix (24)\tin_progress\t\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40879084541/job/123465459680\ntest-matrix (22)\tin_progress\t\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40879084541/job/123465459308\njavascript-typescript\tcompleted\tsuccess\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40879084550/job/123465458542\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:450:| **CRED-003** | Credential material MUST be immune from logging, telemetry, and debugging persistence. Crash reports, flight logs, and audit trails MUST scrub all identified credential values prior to disk writes. | A crash log or stack trace MUST NOT print active bearer tokens or private keys. |\ndocs/CRED003_INDEPENDENT_QUALIFICATION.md:12:> Credential material MUST be immune from logging, telemetry, and debugging persistence. Crash reports, flight logs, and audit trails MUST scrub all identified credential values prior to disk writes.\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_ASSESSMENT.md:58:Phase 2 §17 requires credential material to be immune from logging, telemetry, and debugging persistence; it names crash reports, flight logs, and audit trails as pre-write sanitization sinks. Its acceptance criterion says a crash log or stack trace must not print active bearer tokens or private keys.\ndocs/CRED003_FLIGHTRECORDER_SANITIZATION_EVIDENCE.md:11:> Credential material MUST be immune from logging, telemetry, and debugging persistence. Crash reports, flight logs, and audit trails MUST scrub all identified credential values prior to disk writes.\ndocs/CRED003_FLIGHTRECORDER_SANITIZATION_EVIDENCE.md:29:The separate local audit append in `agent.ts` uses the shared classifier on the complete record, including workspace and tool metadata, arguments, and errors. CRED-003 explicitly names audit trails, and the previous display redactor did not cover all classifier-supported patterns. Sanitization failure is caught by the existing audit-write guard and skips the write.\ndocs/ISSUE12_POST_WP05_CLOSURE_ASSESSMENT.md:93:- **Normative Requirement:** *\"Credential material MUST be immune from logging, telemetry, and debugging persistence. Crash reports, flight logs, and audit trails MUST scrub all identified credential values prior to disk writes. A crash log or stack trace MUST NOT print active bearer tokens or private keys.\"*\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:35:**Verifier runs bypass the gate entirely (VER-01).** Before the first edit (change baseline, `agent.ts:1602-1617`) and at every `task_completed` (`agent.ts:3432-3436`), Nexus runs the repository's own test command (`make test` / `npm test` / `cargo test` / `pytest`, chosen by `tester.ts:113-136`) through `bridge.executeTool` directly. These calls skip `dispatchToolCall`, so even review mode never asks, and no workspace-trust check applies. Opening a hostile repo and approving one `edit_file` therefore runs that repo's arbitrary test script on the host. `/test` and `nexus eval` run `execSync` on the host, bypassing the sandbox and blocking the event loop (VER-14).\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md:90:| CRED-003 | 13: Credential Requirements | Credential material MUST be immune from logging, telemetry, and debugging persistence. Crash reports, flight logs, and audit trails MUST scrub all identified credential values prior to disk writes. | A crash log or stack trace MUST NOT print active bearer tokens or private keys. | Phase 2 §17 | cli/src/flight.ts, cli/src/core/egress.ts, cli/src/agent.ts; cli/test/flight_sanitization.test.ts; docs/CRED003_FLIGHTRECORDER_SANITIZATION_EVIDENCE.md; docs/CRED003_INDEPENDENT_QUALIFICATION.md; accepted implementation a285204 and qualification provenance a4f3e16 | SATISFIED_WITH_BOUNDED_OPERATING_ENVELOPE | Flight and audit durable sinks were independently verified with disk-level synthetic tests. Bounded: no separate crash-report persistence writer was found; exception-display paths were not globally qualified. See accepted CRED-003 qualification. The former CRED-003-FLIGHTLOG finding is RESOLVED. | Bounded limitation |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:23:**Candidate convergence:** PR #311 remains open at `742d00871c311d6829e8a4d0a1a3a1800701b954` on the older base `cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e`; its prior Node 22/24, Linux x86_64 and CodeQL checks passed, but they do not qualify the current base. A local candidate at `fe28ec9e686b90e69e42a7a13d55f50264b3775f` includes the reviewed source changes and readiness refresh; the completed full suite below ran on a different immutable snapshot and is not exact-candidate evidence. PR #316 carries the terminal-matrix correction at head `2e9ad10df4bab065bc9573680e3ed659709e4293` against main `b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d`; independent review accepted that exact head, CodeQL and JS/TS passed, Node 22/24 and Entire Gates remain in progress at 04:23 UTC, and GitHub reports the PR blocked. PR #315's waiver conclusion conflicts with the current release decision and must not be merged as-is.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:39:**Integrated changes and open PRs:** PR #299 merged as `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` (merge commit `145d464dd819a20bf918dfbb4f0176f2c4840a08`). PR #307 merged as `90837aa5193d7c071066d27ccefd2b2ea2db0aff`. PR #305 merged at `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`; its GitHub Entire Gates check concluded **NEUTRAL** (“No trail tracks this branch”). PR #302 was closed unmerged. PR #308 supersedes it and is open at `2c1b2dfa6b10f736367020a86228ab64a4173500` on current base `13e45a07361866d697e16b2c90e48e4fdfcd15e0`. Exact-head CI run [40757432379](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40757432379) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; Linux packaging/tests remain in progress. CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript passed. The PR head fixes the `globName` test by staging it with the literal `:(literal)` pathspec. A separate local follow-up commit `9829c61d9b2556bba25a5ec6aee8fa9f1acf9bc8` applies literal staging to the `magicName` fixture and asserts that it entered the index; this follow-up is not on the PR head. Its focused 77/77 result is owner-reported without a retained log, so that additional fixture change still needs exact-head checks before integration. PR #309 is open at `aace981bc3f46e10f1e57c5498825a76e9994ee5` on the current base. Run [40758300812](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40758300812) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript passed, and Linux packaging/tests are in progress. PR #300 is open at `f3957a67ac8f9b5ea1e60be2494b9402d943230f` on the current base. Run [40757603196](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40757603196) has Node 22 and Node 24 passing; Linux packaging/tests remain in progress. A fresh checkpoint accuracy correction was posted on PR #300 (comment [6479279112](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300#issuecomment-6479279112)); this local update addresses the stale PR heads and main-CI status identified there. Source PR checks are distinct from release qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:67:**Release PRs and exact-head checks:** PRs [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) (`004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f`), [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) (`11dc196fcdd733f8de71dfc95ff70e109d8f4492`), [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) (`3c52580ae1da6b7f1282018f4d3702dcb75f8bd7`), and [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) (`97f1c6ead710bc059126ba65b37ad1e5fde17666`) are all based on `b2ae2fe`. Exact-head Node 22/24, Linux x86_64, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks passed for these candidates. Their Entire Gates checks are failures, so none is mergeable through the required workflow. PR #302's trail reports five high-severity findings and missing reviewer approval. The independent source reviewer ACCEPTed the cumulative diff after a partial source read and did not run tests as part of that review. A separate owner-authored PR update records `tsc --noEmit` and 53/53 targeted restore tests, and advises a second review of `checkpoint.ts` because of its size. PR #299, #300, and #305 also lack successful Entire approval. No findings were bypassed and no self-approval was recorded.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:77:**Authoritative source:** `origin/main` is `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`, the PR #304 merge. Main CI [40693030763](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030763) has Node 22 and Node 24 matrix jobs passed (13:23:35 and 13:23:05 UTC); Linux x86_64 remains in progress. CodeQL [40693030710](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030710) passed at 13:07:03 UTC. On a clean detached worktree at this exact head, `HOME=/tmp/nexus-req-home XDG_CONFIG_HOME=/tmp/nexus-req-xdg node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 requirements; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to exact-RC qualification. PR #304 adds opt-in v1.1 Git-aware operations to current main; its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed and Entire Gates concluded neutral. The independent review recorded an unresolved correctness defect: an explicit restart recreates a clean worktree while resuming the old agent conversation. That behavior must be fixed and requalified before an RC built from this main can be accepted.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:79:**Source PRs:** PR [#303](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/303) is integrated at `4cac22d`; its exact-head required CI and independent review passed. PR [#304](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/304) is integrated at `b2ae2fe`; its exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, CodeQL and JS/TS checks passed and Entire Gates concluded neutral. Its independent review nevertheless found the restart/conversation defect above. PR [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) addresses that defect at `f7e573ec8de98fb3ec24a96e148a84b4ccab151f`, with independent review ACCEPT at diff SHA-256 `cf1abd6ce5e7083aebe526efaaee85380dee295fced7814a7ddedcd609a11615`. Build and focused test TypeScript check passed; the runtime test was not run locally because `SUITE` is claimed by `kimi-main`. Exact-head Node 22 and Node 24 jobs in run `40694815985` both failed with 1,882 passed, 2 failed and 2 skipped: `durable_continuity.test.ts` expected the explicit-restart recovery warning, and `tdd_work_units.test.ts` uses a fake agent without `restartConversation`. JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; Linux was skipped after the matrix failures, and Entire Gates remain pending. PR [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) is at `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` on base `b2ae2fe`; independent review ACCEPTed this exact head at diff SHA-256 `55afcdc8ed8044bb0aa0a54932c5ba6513763b564bc8fb76014b3334db33ae38`. Its Node 22/24 jobs are in progress, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, and Entire Gates are pending. Issue [#298](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/298) remains open until its fix is integrated and current-main checks pass. At the 13:34:51 UTC snapshot cutoff, before the readiness-only correction was pushed, PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) was at `e1974fd82dba1aba8e5e2e5b1bc9cf964fe6db20` on base `b2ae2fe`; Node 22/24 and Entire were in progress, while JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. The subsequent documentation-only update restarted exact-head checks; the claim record tracks its latest head and current statuses. The independent factual review found stale status/head references in the prior checkpoint; corrected evidence is pending re-review. PR [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) is at `659d6a63a8708ebe98240ec1937b0f2acdcdfac4` on base `b2ae2fe`; Node 22/24, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, while Linux x86_64 (run `40693955666`) is in progress and Entire Gates are pending. Independent read-only review ACCEPTed the final cumulative diff `1099e6ff6b68ab9907ac66c908bf45c8ab1af338d3b6a14227d45d60cf35dc29`; no tests were run as part of review. Exact-head CI is still pending.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:93:**Authoritative source and source checks:** `origin/main` is `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4`, merge commit for PR [#297](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/297). Its exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks passed; Entire Gates was neutral. Post-merge CI [40652572596](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40652572596) is running and CodeQL [40652572591](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40652572591) passed. Exact-main CI [40647479745](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40647479745) completed successfully on its parent source commit `ceaf60072b7c364edac523d2517fb12df8f5f6cd`, including Node 22/24 tests, Linux tests, packaging, reproducibility, SBOM, and installer checks. The requirements gate also passed on exact current main `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4` in an isolated worktree (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 applicable release-qualification rows remain deferred to their documented exact-RC stages). PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) is being updated to this exact main revision. Source checks do not establish installed-RC acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:109:**Integration queue:** PR #285 merged to `d3b7af3`; its exact diff hash and independent ACCEPT were preserved, and the initial state-store lock timeout did not reproduce in its full Linux retry. PR [#289](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/289) is refreshed onto `d3b7af3` at `3f66ee138b1d8aeded2902851f659873d887f307`; its seven-file patch SHA-256 remains `3e13bdaa…`. Fresh Node 22/24/JavaScript checks and Entire Gates are in progress. The first fresh reviewer response described only the docs file, but the GitHub and local diff both contain six implementation/test files plus docs; a complete read-only source review has been requested, so the rebase is not independently accepted yet. PR [#293](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/293), DecisionRejected operator documentation, is refreshed onto `d3b7af3` at `d0e1fbfb10463948b640361bb123177e9490ee1b`; its exact docs diff SHA-256 remains `83de84d7…`. Independent review ACCEPT was reconfirmed at this exact head. Fresh CI is running. Entire's refreshed trail currently reports Approvals failed (no reviewers approved), Findings passed, Up to date passed, and CI pending. The reviewer confirmed no Entire approval integration or distinct identity is available in their session, so the required trail approval remains outstanding. PR [#292](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/292) remains on base `8b24d8e1`, is reported conflicting against current main, and its Entire Gates check failed for missing reviewer approval and staleness. Its remote checks do not establish current-base readiness. No merge is inferred from stale checks.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":3,"nanos":344458926}},"started_at_ms":1793279380141,"completed_at_ms":1793279383487}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T13:09:43.865Z","ordinal":502589,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a187c7-d939-7713-a665-0c4562a75291","call_id":"call_9964eba3e09c4b41bb73165f81d2fc45","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 3938)\nTotal output lines: 22\n\n{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"headSha\":\"76c9bfe8e509b00e85611b684d53d135f4917366\",\"jobs\":[{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (22)\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"steps\":[]},{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (24)\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"steps\":[]}],\"status\":\"in_progress\"}\n{\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"headSha\":\"76c9bfe8e509b00e85611b684d53d135f4917366\",\"jobs\":[{\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"name\":\"javascript-typescript\",\"status\":\"completed\"}],\"status\":\"completed\"}\nCodeQL\tcompleted\tsuccess\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/123466164171\nEntire Gates\tin_progress\t\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/123465474933\ntest-matrix (24)\tin_progress\t\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40879084541/job/123465459680\ntest-matrix (22)\tin_progress\t\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40879084541/job/123465459308\njavascript-typescript\tcompleted\tsuccess\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40879084550/job/123465458542\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:450:| **CRED-003** | Credential material MUST be immune from logging, telemetry, and debugging persistence. Crash reports, flight logs, and audit trails MUST scrub all identified credential values prior to disk writes. | A crash log or stack trace MUST NOT print active bearer tokens or private keys. |\ndocs/CRED003_INDEPENDENT_QUALIFICATION.md:12:> Credential material MUST be immune from logging, telemetry, and debugging persistence. Crash reports, flight logs, and audit trails MUST scrub all identified credential values prior to disk writes.\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_ASSESSMENT.md:58:Phase 2 §17 requires credential material to be immune from logging, telemetry, and debugging persistence; it names crash reports, flight logs, and audit trails as pre-write sanitization sinks. Its acceptance criterion says a crash log or stack trace must not print active bearer tokens or private keys.\ndocs/CRED003_FLIGHTRECORDER_SANITIZATION_EVIDENCE.md:11:> Credential material MUST be immune from logging, telemetry, and debugging persistence. Crash reports, flight logs, and audit trails MUST scrub all identified credential values prior to disk writes.\ndocs/CRED003_FLIGHTRECORDER_SANITIZATION_EVIDENCE.md:29:The separate local audit append in `agent.ts` uses the shared classifier on the complete record, including workspace and tool metadata, arguments, and errors. CRED-003 explicitly names audit trails, and the previous display redactor did not cover all classifier-supported patterns. Sanitization failure is caught by the existing audit-write guard and skips the write.\ndocs/ISSUE12_POST_WP05_CLOSURE_ASSESSMENT.md:93:- **Normative Requirement:** *\"Credential material MUST be immune from logging, telemetry, and debugging persistence. Crash reports, flight logs, and audit trails MUST scrub all identified credential values prior to disk writes. A crash log or stack trace MUST NOT print active bearer tokens or private keys.\"*\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:35:**Verifier runs bypass the gate entirely (VER-01).** Before the first edit (change baseline, `agent.ts:1602-1617`) and at every `task_completed` (`agent.ts:3432-3436`), Nexus runs the repository's own test command (`make test` / `npm test` / `cargo test` / `pytest`, chosen by `tester.ts:113-136`) through `bridge.executeTool` directly. These calls skip `dispatchToolCall`, so even review mode never asks, and no workspace-trust check applies. Opening a hostile repo and approving one `edit_file` therefore runs that repo's arbitrary test script on the host. `/test` and `nexus eval` run `execSync` on the host, bypassing the sandbox and blocking the event loop (VER-14).\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md:90:| CRED-003 | 13: Credential Requirements | Credential material MUST be immune from logging, telemetry, and debugging persistence. Crash reports, flight logs, and audit trails MUST scrub all identified credential values prior to disk writes. | A crash log or stack trace MUST NOT print active bearer tokens or private keys. | Phase 2 §17 | cli/src/flight.ts, cli/src/core/egress.ts, cli/src/agent.ts; cli/test/flight_sanitization.test.ts; docs/CRED003_FLIGHTRECORDER_SANITIZATION_EVIDENCE.md; docs/CRED003_INDEPENDENT_QUALIFICATION.md; accepted implementation a285204 and qualification provenance a4f3e16 | SATISFIED_WITH_BOUNDED_OPERATING_ENVELOPE | Flight and audit durable…1738 tokens truncated…9) is at `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` on base `b2ae2fe`; independent review ACCEPTed this exact head at diff SHA-256 `55afcdc8ed8044bb0aa0a54932c5ba6513763b564bc8fb76014b3334db33ae38`. Its Node 22/24 jobs are in progress, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, and Entire Gates are pending. Issue [#298](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/298) remains open until its fix is integrated and current-main checks pass. At the 13:34:51 UTC snapshot cutoff, before the readiness-only correction was pushed, PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) was at `e1974fd82dba1aba8e5e2e5b1bc9cf964fe6db20` on base `b2ae2fe`; Node 22/24 and Entire were in progress, while JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. The subsequent documentation-only update restarted exact-head checks; the claim record tracks its latest head and current statuses. The independent factual review found stale status/head references in the prior checkpoint; corrected evidence is pending re-review. PR [#302](https://github.com/mikeholo