{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T13:10:35.754Z","ordinal":502651,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-1f07e114-1c2a-424c-9728-7a5be38ac610","process_id":"86773","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","export ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file; entire trail approve --help; entire auth contexts --help 2>&1 | sed -n '1,120p'; entire auth --help | sed -n '1,100p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"export ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file; entire trail approve --help; entire auth contexts --help 2>&1 | sed -n '1,120p'; entire auth --help | sed -n '1,100p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"Approve a trail.\n\n<trail> is a project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number>. Without one, follow the current branch's\nparent. --repo and --branch select a working context. Only that branch is approved,\nnot every repository on the trail. The branch work must be open.\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail approve [<trail>] [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --branch string    Select a repository branch within the trail\n  -h, --help             help for approve\n  -m, --message string   Optional approval comment\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\nList stored login contexts\n\nUsage:\n  entire auth contexts [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for contexts\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\nAuthentication subcommands. Includes login, logout, status, and login-context management (contexts, switch).\n\nUsage:\n  entire auth [flags]\n  entire auth [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  contexts    List stored login contexts\n  login       Log in to Entire\n  logout      Log out of Entire\n  status      Show authentication status\n  switch      Switch the active login context\n  token       Print an Entire bearer token — a live credential, treat as a secret\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for auth\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire auth [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":164268238}},"started_at_ms":1793279435589,"completed_at_ms":1793279435754}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T13:10:35.905Z","ordinal":502652,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a187c8-a481-76f2-b8bd-5747ef51cb89","call_id":"call_9629f0ccf2554351880536a4b6d7ed5d","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Approve a trail.\n\n<trail> is a project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number>. Without one, follow the current branch's\nparent. --repo and --branch select a working context. Only that branch is approved,\nnot every repository on the trail. The branch work must be open.\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail approve [<trail>] [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --branch string    Select a repository branch within the trail\n  -h, --help             help for approve\n  -m, --message string   Optional approval comment\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\nList stored login contexts\n\nUsage:\n  entire auth contexts [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for contexts\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\nAuthentication subcommands. Includes login, logout, status, and login-context management (contexts, switch).\n\nUsage:\n  entire auth [flags]\n  entire auth [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  contexts    List stored login contexts\n  login       Log in to Entire\n  logout      Log out of Entire\n  status      Show authentication status\n  switch      Switch the active login context\n  token       Print an Entire bearer token — a live credential, treat as a secret\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for auth\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire auth [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","create_time":1793279435.9055774}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
