{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T13:11:21.326Z","ordinal":502674,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a187c9-55ed-78b0-b3d8-2b40a1b2f802","call_id":"call_ba412d6334ab43d7823187b1881da336","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 7690)\nTotal output lines: 128\n\n**Requested codebase-review findings:** The prior checkpoint's implementation and evidence summary remains applicable; the current main includes the capability-category split, scheduler extraction, operation-runner decomposition, bounded diagnostics, `DecisionRejected` guidance, lifecycle tests, and 100 fixed-seed scheduler invariants. The operator config remains intentionally limited to `operationPolicy`; general runtime-default customization is not claimed.\n\n**Runtime identity dogfooding defect:** The user-reported RC8 behavior in which a Claude-specific skill led the model to describe Nexus as Claude Code has a source fix in merged PR [#273](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/273), integrated at `d97ccb70c87db096c75e1bd4ff58dbcdf0aa8ab1` (PR merge commit `e94208d09cb4d5023e4379187fc6c603bba960d2`). The fixed system prompt states Nexus Code is the host and is appended after workspace skills; activated skills are also prefaced with `Host application: Nexus Code`. `cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts` reproduces a Claude model plus Claude-specific skill and verifies both boundaries. That test passed 1/1 in an isolated exact-main `b293b44` snapshot; PR #273's Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks passed, and exact-main CI also passed. The public RC10 tag (`16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`) predates the PR merge, so this fix still needs verification in the successor RC.\n\n**Qualification and custody:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` is still the latest release (published 2026-10-27); the package at `b293b44` is also `1.0.0-rc.10`, so source changes require a successor RC before installed-RC qualification. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 exists. Held-out issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest public status request was posted 2026-10-28 12:42 UTC, with no custodian response as of this checkpoint. The public 40-task manifest is not custody acceptance, and no held-out qualification has started. T2/T3/T4, evaluator/custody acceptance, remaining provider and standalone gates, cross-runner reproducibility, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix remains 0/15; the Ubuntu desktop has setup evidence only, with no qualifying screenshots or cell verdicts recorded.\n\n**Disposition:** Engineering convergence remains active; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`. No RC is accepted and no stable release is published. Public RC10 remains the latest release; the repository target is the GitHub installer (npm publication is inapplicable per operator decision). Continue source remediation and exact-head review/CI, then build and qualify a successor RC only after pre-RC gates and PR #305's restart fix pass; keep all installed-RC gates bound to that exact artifact.\n\nThe 07:55 checkpoint below is retained as historical evidence; its source, CI, PR, and qualification state is superseded by this checkpoint.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 07:55 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and source checks:** `origin/main` is `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4`, merge commit for PR [#297](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/297). Its exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks passed; Entire Gates was neutral. Post-merge CI [40652572596](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40652572596) is running and CodeQL [40652572591](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40652572591) passed. Exact-main CI [40647479745](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40647479745) completed successfully on its parent source commit `ceaf60072b7c364edac523d2517fb12df8f5f6cd`, including Node 22/24 tests, Linux tests, packaging, reproducibility, SBOM, and installer checks. The requirements gate also passed on exact current main `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4` in an isolated worktree (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 applicable release-qualification rows remain deferred to their documented exact-RC stages). PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) is being updated to this exact main revision. Source checks do not establish installed-RC acceptance.\n\n**Requested codebase-review findings are part of the v1.0.0 scope:** The large capability registry is split into category modules (`cli/src/core/capabilities.ts`, 10,046 bytes, plus `capability_definitions/`); scheduler logic is in `cli/src/core/scheduler.ts` (23,696 bytes), with `operation.ts` reduced to 12,818 bytes; runner revalidation, exe…5390 tokens truncated…ave the passing exact post-merge checks listed above.\n\n**Other release-path PRs:** PR [#276](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/276) records a synthetic-only qualification-host preflight (10/10) bound to `ceabfcc`; its Node 22/24, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks pass, while Linux CI remains in progress. Its evidence does not establish custodian access, held-out qualification, or acceptance. PR [#277](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/277) addresses configured Git-hook execution during checkpoint and retention operations. Its exact diff received conflicting review dispositions: a GitHub review comment requested changes for a hook-discovery race and retention error accounting, while a separate read-only review returned ACCEPT. The findings remain unresolved pending the claimed implementation owner's response; no acceptance or merge is claimed. Node 22/24, CodeQL, and JavaScript/TypeScript checks pass; Linux CI remains in progress.\n\n**Requirements and qualification:** A clean disposable snapshot of `origin/main@ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227` passed `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 exact-RC deferrals) and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.10`. The first requirements invocation on the documentation-dirty readiness worktree was correctly refused by its clean-worktree preflight and is not treated as a gate result. The existing [RC10 OpenRouter evidence bundle](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/README.md) establishes a pinned provider verification and one passing synthetic small task; this does not establish the broader provider/standalone matrix. Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains an unaccepted prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` is listed. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open without independent custodian acceptance. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody/host acceptance, remaining provider/standalone profiles, cross-runner exact-RC reproducibility, independent exact-RC acceptance, and scripted terminal gates remain incomplete.\n\n**Human terminal acceptance:** The five-terminal by three-size matrix remains **0/15**. The operator cannot run the requested xterm 80×24 cell now; no cell result or screenshots are inferred. The prepared Ubuntu/GNOME host and worksheet remain available for a later genuine operator run. Scripted PTY evidence does not replace the human matrix. Publication remains gated on all mandatory acceptance gates.\n\nThe 15:12 and earlier checkpoints below are retained as historical evidence and superseded for current source, PR, and CI status by this checkpoint.\n\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-27 15:12 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` is `3b7af5d3cd46ab1b83e9c8df9862e09cee22b1a7`, integrating PRs [#269](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/269) and [#270](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/270) after #271 and #272. Exact-main CI [40521505143](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40521505143) and CodeQL [40521505001](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40521505001) both passed on `3b7af5d`; CI passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux tests, security gates, packaging, reproducibility, package smoke, and installer smoke. PR #269 merge-commit CI [40519862728](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40519862728) passed on `f059770`. These runs establish CI for their exact commits, not the RC10 release gates.\n\nRELEASE STATE FILES\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\n\nVERSION\n3:  \"version\": \"1.0.0-rc.11\",\nv1.0.0-rc.10\nv1.0.0-rc.9\nv1.0.0-rc.8\nv1.0.0-rc.7\nv1.0.0-rc.6\nv1.0.0-rc.5\nv1.0.0-rc.4\nv1.0.0-rc.3\n79b2f4fab6b9584c4e4e3245a5359f009889b7e2\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.4\n57b9285c6cead27b2260bf3113b3fc0b847f8169\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.4^{}\nffccefea5859db9fe5306450f891d1f137ac6c05\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.5\n405f5b96e20b988523b99c8907d29b73bcd2a8fd\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.5^{}\n28442fa4be7bfe6cbcb11718b0701360c21791d6\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.6\n6dadeaf6796375589ee4c51ee71f722e3c8adc77\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.6^{}\nd1f79e58a27c0f79f1663f662a153ae4ec5a7824\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.7\n431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.7^{}\nf847ca34e5d99508baaf5e1105b5ebd9db005026\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.8\nbbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.8^{}\nd211d1c7545d2dd629531e4f712e98a240a782c6\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.9\n4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.9^{}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","create_time":1793279481.325956}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
