{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T13:13:56.913Z","ordinal":502794,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-39fdc9ce-1796-44be-a0cd-418b72fae923","process_id":"28419","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","export ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file; entire trail finding 33 --project gh/mikeholownych --repo gh/mikeholownych/nexus-code --branch v1/eval-agent-toolchain-binds --json | jq -r '.findings[] | [.id,.severity,.status,.location.filePath,(.location.startLine|tostring),(.body|gsub(\"\\\\n\";\" \"))]|@tsv'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"export ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file; entire trail finding 33 --project gh/mikeholownych --repo gh/mikeholownych/nexus-code --branch v1/eval-agent-toolchain-binds --json | jq -r '.findings[] | [.id,.severity,.status,.location.filePath,(.location.startLine|tostring),(.body|gsub(\"\\\\n\";\" \"))]|@tsv'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"01M63SBDM79AQBEF1T0ASV0PR6\tlow\topen\teval/isolate.mjs\t120\tProduction code now goes through `scanOracleCompilerExposure` plus masks. That leaves `oracleCompilerExposureProblem` (doc: \"Reject every unpinned Go/Rust compiler…\") and `candidateCompilerExposureProblem` as test-only exports that describe a rejection the sandbox no longer performs. Tests that assert on their strings check a string formatter, not the masking boundary. Test the scan or mask output directly and drop the stale wrappers.\n01M63SBDM1C4Q2M9A0N9Z2JJ13\tlow\topen\tcli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts\t1384\t`agentSandboxArgv` now masks exposed compilers and never throws the \"candidate task has unapproved…\" message, so this try/catch and its `return` (with the comment \"An unsafe host system mount is rejected\") are leftover from the refusal design. On a scan failure the error says \"oracle compiler exposure could not be checked\", which the regex doesn't match either, so the branch can't be reached as written. Remove the wrapper and call `agentSandboxArgv` directly, as the other tests do.\n01M63Q7BV24HC89P0YEFA2ZJQW\tlow\topen\teval/isolate.mjs\t182\t`candidateCompilerExposureProblem` builds its message by regex-rewriting the oracle message. The result reads \"candidate task has unapproved Go/Rust compiler executable is exposed through oracle system mounts: …\", which is ungrammatical and still says \"oracle\". The other failure becomes \"candidate task compiler exposure could not be checked; refusing qualification\". Make the scan return the exposed paths, or take a label parameter, so each caller formats its own message.\n01M631CXMW4PJ3P5NJ950ZMVM7\tlow\topen\teval/isolate.mjs\t36\tWith the `go env GOROOT` / `rustc --print sysroot` discovery gone, `selectToolchainRoot` has no production callers. Only an old test in `eval_hardened.test.ts` still calls it, so it is iteration debris. Remove it along with that test.\n01M631CXMR8GEG8PA8TBDKTWT9\tlow\topen\teval/isolate.mjs\t490\t`addOracleMountParent` is a new parent-directory helper that scans `args` linearly. `isolatedProcessArgv` already defines `addParents` with a `madeDirs` set a few lines below. Because `/opt` and `/opt/nexus-qual` never go into `madeDirs`, the two helpers can emit duplicate `--dir` entries. Reuse the existing helper instead.\n01M631CXMGH04AAG9EEK93QQCT\tmedium\topen\teval/isolate.mjs\t66\t`resolveHostToolchains` used to skip a toolchain it couldn't use. It now throws if `/usr/local/go` or the Rust root exists but isn't fully root-owned and free of group/other write bits. It feeds `candidateSandboxHostMountSources`, `isolatedArgv` and `candidateAgentPath`, so one user-installed Go tree now aborts every candidate run, setup step and validator, including Node-only tasks. The new tests never exercise this failure.\n01M631CXMCH7YHY2B1R6NDDJ77\tmedium\topen\teval/oracle.mjs\t51\t`blackBoxOracleProblem` refuses every `runtime: \"python3\"` oracle unless both `/usr/local/go` and `/opt/nexus-qual/rust` pass the pinned-toolchain checks. The held-out t3-py-* tasks are plain Python oracles, so a host without either compiler can no longer run them. Make compiler access opt-in per check (or per task) instead of tying it to the python3 runtime.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":19546330}},"started_at_ms":1793279635893,"completed_at_ms":1793279636913}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T13:13:57.034Z","ordinal":502795,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a187cb-b62a-7eb0-a04b-fcc84afeee0b","call_id":"call_148c302564fa42deb763f0e3d238d31c","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"01M63SBDM79AQBEF1T0ASV0PR6\tlow\topen\teval/isolate.mjs\t120\tProduction code now goes through `scanOracleCompilerExposure` plus masks. That leaves `oracleCompilerExposureProblem` (doc: \"Reject every unpinned Go/Rust compiler…\") and `candidateCompilerExposureProblem` as test-only exports that describe a rejection the sandbox no longer performs. Tests that assert on their strings check a string formatter, not the masking boundary. Test the scan or mask output directly and drop the stale wrappers.\n01M63SBDM1C4Q2M9A0N9Z2JJ13\tlow\topen\tcli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts\t1384\t`agentSandboxArgv` now masks exposed compilers and never throws the \"candidate task has unapproved…\" message, so this try/catch and its `return` (with the comment \"An unsafe host system mount is rejected\") are leftover from the refusal design. On a scan failure the error says \"oracle compiler exposure could not be checked\", which the regex doesn't match either, so the branch can't be reached as written. Remove the wrapper and call `agentSandboxArgv` directly, as the other tests do.\n01M63Q7BV24HC89P0YEFA2ZJQW\tlow\topen\teval/isolate.mjs\t182\t`candidateCompilerExposureProblem` builds its message by regex-rewriting the oracle message. The result reads \"candidate task has unapproved Go/Rust compiler executable is exposed through oracle system mounts: …\", which is ungrammatical and still says \"oracle\". The other failure becomes \"candidate task compiler exposure could not be checked; refusing qualification\". Make the scan return the exposed paths, or take a label parameter, so each caller formats its own message.\n01M631CXMW4PJ3P5NJ950ZMVM7\tlow\topen\teval/isolate.mjs\t36\tWith the `go env GOROOT` / `rustc --print sysroot` discovery gone, `selectToolchainRoot` has no production callers. Only an old test in `eval_hardened.test.ts` still calls it, so it is iteration debris. Remove it along with that test.\n01M631CXMR8GEG8PA8TBDKTWT9\tlow\topen\teval/isolate.mjs\t490\t`addOracleMountParent` is a new parent-directory helper that scans `args` linearly. `isolatedProcessArgv` already defines `addParents` with a `madeDirs` set a few lines below. Because `/opt` and `/opt/nexus-qual` never go into `madeDirs`, the two helpers can emit duplicate `--dir` entries. Reuse the existing helper instead.\n01M631CXMGH04AAG9EEK93QQCT\tmedium\topen\teval/isolate.mjs\t66\t`resolveHostToolchains` used to skip a toolchain it couldn't use. It now throws if `/usr/local/go` or the Rust root exists but isn't fully root-owned and free of group/other write bits. It feeds `candidateSandboxHostMountSources`, `isolatedArgv` and `candidateAgentPath`, so one user-installed Go tree now aborts every candidate run, setup step and validator, including Node-only tasks. The new tests never exercise this failure.\n01M631CXMCH7YHY2B1R6NDDJ77\tmedium\topen\teval/oracle.mjs\t51\t`blackBoxOracleProblem` refuses every `runtime: \"python3\"` oracle unless both `/usr/local/go` and `/opt/nexus-qual/rust` pass the pinned-toolchain checks. The held-out t3-py-* tasks are plain Python oracles, so a host without either compiler can no longer run them. Make compiler access opt-in per check (or per task) instead of tying it to the python3 runtime.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","create_time":1793279637.0343792}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
