{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T13:14:37.393Z","ordinal":502817,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-389627d6-420a-42a0-b84b-a5954ca2280c","process_id":"84233","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","xerj feedback --submit --agent \"gpt-6.1\" --used-for \"check evaluation requirements before reconciling PR #318 findings\" --verdict \"Corrected command syntax and returned documentation passages, but the indexed release documents did not answer the specific evaluator toolchain questions; direct current-branch source inspection is needed\""],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"xerj feedback --submit --agent \"gpt-6.1\" --used-for \"check evaluation requirements before reconciling PR #318 findings\" --verdict \"Corrected command syntax and returned documentation passages, but the indexed release documents did not answer the specific evaluator toolchain questions; direct current-branch source inspection is needed\""}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"the `--remote` flag is unsupported when a repository argument is provided\n\nCreate a fork of a repository.\n\nWith no argument, creates a fork of the current repository. Otherwise, forks\nthe specified repository.\n\nBy default, the new fork is set to be your `origin` remote and any existing\norigin remote is renamed to `upstream`. To alter this behavior, you can set\na name for the new fork's remote with `--remote-name`.\n\nThe `upstream` remote will be set as the default remote repository.\n\nAdditional `git clone` flags can be passed after `--`.\n\n\nUSAGE\n  gh repo fork [<repository>] [-- <gitflags>...] [flags]\n\nFLAGS\n  --clone                 Clone the fork\n  --default-branch-only   Only include the default branch in the fork\n  --fork-name string      Rename the forked repository\n  --org string            Create the fork in an organization\n  --remote                Add a git remote for the fork\n  --remote-name string    Specify the name for the new remote (default \"origin\")\n\nINHERITED FLAGS\n  --help   Show help for command\n\nEXAMPLES\n  # Fork a repository\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo\n  \n  # Fork a repository and clone it locally\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo --clone\n  \n  # Fork a repository without cloning it, skip the prompt\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo --clone=false\n\nLEARN MORE\n  Use `gh <command> <subcommand> --help` for more information about a command.\n  Read the manual at https://cli.github.com/manual\n  Learn about exit codes using `gh help exit-codes`\n  Learn about accessibility experiences using `gh help accessibility`\n\nerror: this account cannot push to xerj-org/xerj, and forking failed: `gh repo fork xerj-org/xerj --remote --remote-name xerj-fork` failed\nNothing was branched.\n\n# Ready-to-run — files ONLY the field report, nothing else.\n# Run these in a clone of xerj-org/xerj, not in the project you are working in.\ngit clone https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj.git\ncd xerj\ngh repo fork xerj-org/xerj --remote --remote-name xerj-fork\nxerj feedback \\\n --agent \"gpt-6.1\" \\\n  --used-for \"check evaluation requirements before reconciling PR #318 findings\" --pointed-at \"1051 records under /home/mike/xerj-sources/nexus-code/core/src (autoindex run run-20261028T022152Z-ff10-0000)\" \\\n  --verdict \"Corrected command syntax and returned documentation passages, but the indexed release documents did not answer the specific evaluator toolchain questions; direct current-branch source inspection is needed\" --numbers \"not measured\" \\\n  -o user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-29-check-evaluation-requirements-before-reconciling.md\ngit checkout -b field-report/check-evaluation-requirements-before-reconciling\ngit add user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-29-check-evaluation-require