{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T13:20:40.025Z","ordinal":503104,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae34827115c819fa11e8d228914b8a7","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I’m addressing the concrete gate findings now: removing stale error-string wrappers and dead helper code, making the sandbox test fail on unexpected preflight errors, sharing mount-directory tracking, and allowing compiler-independent candidate tasks to proceed when an optional host compiler root is unsafe. Oracle execution still fails closed when its required pinned toolchains are unavailable. I’ve left the per-check policy question open pending your choice and the custodian’s metadata boundary."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793280039087,"completed_at_ms":1793280040025}}
