{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T13:21:29.721Z","ordinal":503144,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae34858b9a8819fa2e40f84e78cf220","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The review confirms that the shared mount-parent helper’s alleged duplicate-directory issue is a false positive; I reverted that unnecessary refactor. The test-only wrappers and dead selector are removed, the masking test now asserts scan output and actual mask arguments, and an unsafe optional host toolchain is omitted from candidate mounts instead of aborting every candidate task. Strict pinned-toolchain checks for Python oracles remain unchanged pending your policy choice."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793280088747,"completed_at_ms":1793280089720}}
