{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T13:28:03.511Z","ordinal":503369,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae349e249b0819fad1dd8f935054df9","usage":{"input_tokens":73948,"cached_input_tokens":73600,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":70,"reasoning_output_tokens":53,"total_tokens":74018},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":99204920,"cached_input_tokens":98025216,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":267552,"reasoning_output_tokens":170985,"total_tokens":99472472},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9423322720,"cached_input_tokens":9322722944,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":27299858,"reasoning_output_tokens":16034198,"total_tokens":9450622578}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T13:28:03.570Z","ordinal":503370,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a187d8-a0f2-71c1-90d3-ced0aaf416bb","call_id":"call_402c9672b1394f62940b18392d8add0b","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr311_draft_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — exact four-file diff SHA-256: `56ab8a3ecef2ada575aacd09e3e5148948fb6b013640c92b071d11598a629184`.\\n\\nPinned toolchain roots and their contents are checked for root ownership, canonical paths, and write/symlink safety before use. Candidate and Python oracle mounts are read-only; oracle launches clear the environment, use offline Go/Rust settings and temporary caches, and refuse protected-corpus overlap. The fixtures cover unsafe roots, production launch paths, and Go/Rust execution.\\n\\n**Independence note:** I previously reviewed related evaluator-toolchain and provisioning changes, so this is a fresh review of the exact candidate, but should not be represented as fully independent of those earlier reviews. No tests run.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr300_readiness\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Current `main` is `078f12b11f32ebde7a28477cddba1b68e5206ca4`. PR #323 is merged, and its exact-head checks plus post-merge CI and CodeQL passed. Main is versioned `1.0.0-rc.11`, but the public release list still ends at RC10; there is no RC11 or stable v1.0.0 release.\\n\\nRelease-critical blockers and next actions:\\n\\n- **Evaluator:** PR #318 is open at `76c9bfe8` on base `078f12b`. Node 22/24 and Entire checks are still running; JS/TS and CodeQL passed. Complete exact-head checks and independent acceptance, then integrate it.\\n- **Held-out custody:** Issue #1 remains open without custody acceptance or an acknowledged handoff. The claim metadata reports 20 tasks and revalidation waiting on SUITE. Resolve ownership safely, complete custodian-only revalidation, and record acceptance before qualification.\\n- **Exact-RC qualification:** No RC11 artifact is available. After prerequisites pass, construct it and run the required artifact, provider, standalone, held-out T2/T3/T4, cross-runner, and independent acceptance gates.\\n- **Manual terminal matrix:** The worksheet has 0/15 accepted cells. Once RC11 is installed, the operator must complete all 15 cells; DEC-18 waives screenshots only.\\n- **Readiness record:** The current `READINESS.md` checkpoint is timestamped 06:18 UTC and still reports main as `a0356c4` and RC10. Refresh it against `078f12b` before relying on it as the aggregate status.\\n\\nI made no edits, ran no suites, and accessed no held-out payloads.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr302\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Reviewed PR #318 at HEAD `76c9bfe8e509b00e85611b684d53d135f4917366`. No tests run and no held-out content accessed.\\n\\n1. **Stale test-only exposure wrappers — FALSE-POSITIVE.** The helpers at [eval/isolate.mjs:135](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:135) and [eval/isolate.mjs:227](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:227) format scan results; production sandbox builders scan and add masks directly. Tests also inspect generated mask arguments at [eval_integrity.test.ts:586](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:586). No confinement gap identified. Optional cleanup: remove or clearly label the test-facing wrappers.\\n\\n2. **Unreachable `agentSandboxArgv` catch — ACCEPT-AS-VALID.** [eval_integrity.test.ts:1435](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:1435) catches messages that the production call at [eval/isolate.mjs:551](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:551) does not emit: scan failures retain the “oracle” wording, and exposure results are masked. Remove the catch so a preflight failure fails the test instead of being hidden behind stale exception handling.\\n\\n3. **Candidate message rewrite — FALSE-POSITIVE.** The rewrite at [eval/isolate.mjs:230](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:230) produces the expected candidate wording for both scan errors and detected exposures. It is not the production enforcement path, which masks scanned paths. No security defect identified.\\n\\n4. **Unused `selectToolchainRoot` — FALSE-POSITIVE.** It has no production caller ([eval/isolate.mjs:41](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:41)); the test at [eval_hardened.test.ts:37](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/cli/test/eval_hardened.test.ts:37) tests only its precedence behavior. This is dead-code/test-maintenance scope, not a toolchain-boundary failure. Optional action: remove helper and test.\\n\\n5. **Duplicate oracle mount-parent helper — FALSE-POSITIVE.** [eval/isolate.mjs:667](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:667) checks existing `--dir` arguments before adding each parent, including parents added for the first toolchain. I found no duplicate-directory case from the described Go/Rust mounts. Optional action: simplify by sharing the existing directory set if future mount changes make the duplication risk concrete.\\n\\n6. **Unsafe toolchain root aborts all tasks — ACCEPT-AS-VALID (availability finding).** [eval/isolate.mjs:83](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:83) throws for an unsafe existing pin root, and the resolver is called by candidate mount discovery at [eval/isolate.mjs:337](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/isolate.mjs:337). Since `/usr/local/go` and `/usr/local/nexus-qual/rust` are not ordinary system mounts, an invalid root can prevent even tasks that do not use compilers from starting. Minimal safe correction: omit an unsafe root from candidate mounts and `PATH`, while retaining fail-closed checks for oracle executions that require pins and ensuring no alternate mounted path exposes that root.\\n\\n7. **Every Python oracle requires both pinned toolchains — NEEDS-SCOPE.** [oracle.mjs:51](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/oracle.mjs:51) requires both pins for all `python3` checks; execution enables the toolchain namespace at [oracle.mjs:114](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/oracle.mjs:114). This is consistent with the current cross-language oracle contract and regression fixture, which builds both Go and Rust from Python ([eval_integrity.test.ts:649](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:649)). Whether Python-only checks should avoid that dependency is a policy/scope question. If requirements are later made per-task, keep the exposure scan and masking mandatory; mount pins only for tasks that declare compiler use.\\n\\nXERJ did not return a source passage for the new helper; the required field report was submitted through its fallback endpoint.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","create_time":1793280483.5701017}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
