{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T13:43:02.336Z","ordinal":504236,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a187e6-57bf-7ca3-8b3d-4eba8eb1e2c3","author":"/root/review_pr302","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_pr302\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED.** Reviewed base `078f12b` → HEAD `1c43441e232af65c9016b4cd961d778086326e21`; cumulative diff SHA-256: `8a4c76c2a44c86232bb76e022fcff41a6304ec0785ae04482ec721d0b07caaf2`. No tests run; no held-out content accessed.\n\nThe prior inactive-root bypass is addressed: scanner exemptions now use selected roots that passed validation ([eval/isolate.mjs:135](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds-validation/eval/isolate.mjs:135), [eval/isolate.mjs:535](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds-validation/eval/isolate.mjs:535)); candidate mounts reuse those same selected sources ([eval/isolate.mjs:313](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds-validation/eval/isolate.mjs:313), [eval/isolate.mjs:558](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds-validation/eval/isolate.mjs:558)). Oracle fallback mounting also uses the selected `/opt/nexus-qual/rust` source at the canonical guest path ([eval/isolate.mjs:613](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds-validation/eval/isolate.mjs:613)).\n\nOne optional-root defect remains: if a configured source root is a **dangling symlink**, `lstatSync` succeeds, then `realpathSync` throws at [eval/isolate.mjs:83](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds-validation/eval/isolate.mjs:83)–[eval/isolate.mjs:89](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds-validation/eval/isolate.mjs:89). That aborts candidate toolchain resolution instead of omitting the unsafe source and trying Rust’s fallback. Catch expected invalid-root resolution errors and continue to the next source; retain fail-closed behavior where oracle execution requires the pins. Add a dangling-root fixture that confirms fallback selection and ordinary candidate startup remain available."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18771-cd08-7c60-9b2e-7bad123756d6","create_time":1793281382.3357637,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":23461}}
